{"qid": "9d1d299e-4b40-4f3a-8714-ea7acd1672fe", "source": "dapo", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: We say that a real number $V$ is good if there exist two closed convex subsets $X, Y$ of the unit cube in $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$, with volume $V$ each, such that for each of the three coordinate planes (that is, the planes spanned by any two of the three coordinate axes), the projections of $X$ and $Y$ onto that plane are disjoint. Find $\\sup \\{V \\mid V$ is good $\\}$. The original answer is in \\frac{m}{n} format, please give the value of m + n.\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is the final integer answer.", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: We say that a real number $V$ is good if there exist two closed convex subsets $X, Y$ of the unit cube in $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$, with volume $V$ each, such that for each of the three coordinate planes (that is, the planes spanned by any two of the three coordinate axes), the projections of $X$ and $Y$ onto that plane are disjoint. Find $\\sup \\{V \\mid V$ is good $\\}$. The original answer is in \\frac{m}{n} format, please give the value of m + n.", "true_answer": 5, "origin": "base", "source_ref": "9d1d299e-4b40-4f3a-8714-ea7acd1672fe:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 18135, 4792, 13, 1416, 679, 7670, 46822, 723, 15, 11, 16, 144683, 18, 13, 1416, 1309, 1920, 12412, 142423, 165377, 2127, 71464, 6772, 290, 46822, 11, 2454, 328, 10945, 631, 11, 2238, 484, 395, 2454, 328, 290, 3407, 30380, 41666, 350, 6077, 192392, 11, 1215, 89, 192392, 11, 186702, 192392, 936, 290, 35656, 127861, 74016, 328, 2127, 326, 865, 13291, 484, 16499, 553, 829, 69164, 11982, 350, 72, 2560, 4213, 1023, 621, 625, 64353, 741, 19792, 98608, 394, 4149, 631, 364, 2167, 1309, 10562, 10945, 2454, 665, 679, 2049, 2928, 2447, 13574, 306, 2454, 30380, 41244, 364, 88748, 25, 2214, 1920, 165