m may converge to something around maybe 1.25.\n\nLet's estimate remaining contributions beyond max 7 by approximating integral. Since tail beyond 7 may be small.\n\nWe have current sum up to m,n ≤7 about 1.135 (approx). We need contributions for larger values.\n\nLet's compute contributions for (8,8) diagonal approximate using formula: term ≈ (π)^{-1/2} k^{-2.5} with k=8 gives ≈0.564*8^{-2.5}=0.564 / (8^{2.5}) =0.564 / (8^2 * sqrt(8)) =0.564 / (64*2.828)=0.564/181.0=0.00312. Add =>1.138\n\n(9,9): 0.564/ (9^{2.5}) ; 9^{2.5}=9^2 * sqrt(9)=81*3=243; term ≈0.564/243=0.00232 total 1.140\n\n(10,10): 10^{2.5}=100*√10≈100*3.162=316.2; term≈0.564/316.2=0.00178 total 1.142\n\nSum of diagonal tail beyond 7 approximates integral of k^{-2.5} from 8 to ∞ times constant 0.564. Integral ∫_8^∞ k^{-2.5} dk = [ -2/(3) k^{-1.5} ]_8∞ = (2/3) * 8^{-1.5}= (2/3) / (8^{1.5}) = (2/3)/ (8*√8)= (2/3)/(8*2.828)= (2/3)/22.627= (2)/(67.882)=0.0295. Multiply by 0.564 gives about 0.0166. So diagonal tail adds ~0.017. So final diagonal sum maybe around 0.666+0.017=0.683.\n\nBut earlier diagonal contributed 0.666 up to 7, plus ~0.017 =0.683. Wait earlier we had 0.666 after 7, adding more up to infinity maybe 0.683. That's small.\n\nNow need off-diagonal contributions. For each difference d, sum over n of contributions. Approx for fixed d the term ~∑_{n} sqrt factor * n^{-2} * exp(??). Might behave ~ const/d? Not sure.\n\nLet's attempt to compute total sum numerically with moderate effort maybe using quick code mental? Not feasible.\n\nPerhaps the sum A equals 1. Maybe our overcount due to double counting? Wait earlier we computed (1,2)+(2,1) =0.2222 etc. Perhaps C_{m,n}=m^{n-1} n^{m-1} counts directed trees? Actually number of spanning trees in K_{m,n} is m^{n-1} n^{m-1}. That's correct.\n\nBut Zeng chooses m+n-1 rectangles; the order doesn't matter, just set. So counting subsets equals number of trees. Good.\n\nThus our sum formulation seems correct.\n\nMaybe there is known identity: Σ_{m,n≥1} m^{n