9=1 => 0 1 1 0 0 0 1 not equal.\n\ni=7 block7-13: 1 0 0 0 1 1 0 ; block14-20: 14=1,15=1,16=0,17=0,18=0,19=1,20=0 => 1 1 0 0 0 1 0 not equal.\n\ni=8 block8-14: 0 0 0 1 1 0 1 ; block15-21: 15=1,16=0,17=0,18=0,19=1,20=0,21=0 => 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 not equal.\n\ni=9 block9-15: 0 0 1 1 0 1 1 ; block16-22: 16=0,17=0,18=0,19=1,20=0,21=0,22=1 => 0 0 0 1 0 0 1 not equal.\n\ni=10 block10-16: 0 1 1 0 1 1 0 ; block17-23: 17=0,18=0,19=1,20=0,21=0,22=1,23=1 => 0 0 1 0 0 1 1 not equal.\n\ni=11 block11-17: 1 1 0 1 1 0 0 ; block18-24: 18=0,19=1,20=0,21=0,22=1,23=1,24=1 => 0 1 0 0 1 1 1 not equal.\n\ni=12 block12-18: 1 0 1 1 0 0 0 ; block19-25: 19=1,20=0,21=0,22=1,23=1,24=1,25=0 => 1 0 0 1 1 1 0 not equal.\n\ni=13 block13-19: 0 1 1 0 0 0 1 ; block20-26: 20=0,21=0,22=1,23=1,24=1,25=0,26=0 =>0 0 1 1 1 0 0 not equal.\n\ni=14 block14-20: 1 1 0 0 0 1 0 ; block21-27: 21=0,22=1,23=1,24=1,25=0,26=0,27=1 =>0 1 1 1 0 0 1 not equal.\n\ni=15 block15-21: 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 ; block22-28: 22=1,23=1,24=1,25=0,26=0,27=1,28=1 =>1 1 1 0 0 1 1 not equal.\n\ni=16 block16-22:0 0 0 1 0 0 1 ; block23-29: 23=1,24=1,25=0,26=0,27=1,28=1,29=0 =>1 1 0 0 1 1 0 not equal.\n\ni=17 block17-23:0 0 1 0 0 1 1 ; block24-30:24=1,25=0,26=0,27=1,28=1,29=0,30=1 =>1 0 0 1 1 0 1 not equal.\n\ni=18 block18-24:0 1 0 0 1 1 1 ; block25-31:25=0,26=0,27=1,28=1,29=0,30=1,31=1 =>0 0 1 1 0 1 1 not equal.\n\ni=19 block19-25:1 0 0 1 1 1 0 ; block26-32:26=0,27=1,28=1,29=0,30=1,31=1,32=0 =>0 1 1 0 1 1 0 not equal.\n\nThus no match up to i=19, seems unlikely a=7 possible.\n\nThus possible a: 1,3,5 maybe more odd like 9 fails, 11 maybe? Let's test a=11 quickly maybe using more data but could be.\n\nObservation: We found matches for a=1,3,5 where the start offset i was 0? For a=1 start i=0 works. For a=3 start i=1. For a=5 start i=4. pattern: start i = a-? Specifically i = a-2? For a=3, i=1 (a-2). For a=5, i=4 (a-1). Not clear.\n\nMaybe the condition holds for any odd a where a's binary representation is palindrome? Not.\n\nGiven limited time, probably