, 2086, 328, 8522, 108073, 5251, 63009, 25, 353, 314, 21494, 22305, 33, 18085, 230, 34, 92, 284, 3201, 314, 21494, 3201, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 11876, 17, 364, 10620, 1217, 23864, 353, 4493, 63009, 13, 2214, 2454, 13501, 336, 11, 35968, 480, 8844, 27661, 483, 16174, 265, 10853, 350, 18303, 741, 623, 2086, 328, 27661, 306, 336, 382, 2086, 328, 7881, 306, 31512, 11, 175342, 260, 1875, 13, 12265, 290, 31512, 17804, 722, 323, 4501, 11, 581, 679, 21494, 22305, 72, 28, 16, 107298, 83, 1875, 92, 265, 10853, 314, 323, 13, 8820, 2454, 265, 10853, 14210, 364, 84787, 11, 4215, 1072, 63009, 328, 260, 1875, 314, 3609, 2086, 328, 27661, 2061, 5251, 63009, 314, 353, 364, 7943, 260, 1875, 382, 1217, 3543, 581, 2023, 23864, 2360, 2454, 119115, 8522, 20190, 30, 11555, 6760, 33063, 316, 9707, 1001, 8522, 777, 13501, 13, 2632, 777, 13501, 11, 1354, 553, 323, 4501, 2454, 12989, 1511, 27661, 11, 20547, 306, 3609, 2086, 328, 6760, 29640, 431, 61948, 3851, 5251, 63009, 12629, 323, 81061, 350, 21309, 6760, 395, 2454, 13501, 741, 20064, 2006, 25, 2454, 55807, 328, 261, 8522, 418, 306, 261, 13501, 14066, 395, 722, 1617, 1022, 33, 91, 4501, 13, 2632, 4215, 1072, 63009, 328, 4215, 1072, 27661, 306, 484, 13501, 328, 1022, 33, 91, 314, 323, 81061, 364, 7943, 1217, 29702, 4215, 1072, 27661, 328, 350, 91, 33, 91, 425, 284, 3201, 8, 2236, 2454, 8522, 14518, 306, 284, 3201, 63009, 13, 2632, 1402, 10720, 3201, 1022, 33, 91, 425, 284, 3201, 314, 323, 81061, 13, 350, 129214, 220, 18, 1029, 170167, 284, 3201, 314, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 11876, 17, 13, 2632, 3561, 4307, 314, 21494, 3201, 1022, 33, 91, 425, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 11876, 17, 314, 220, 16, 14, 17, 21494, 3201, 350, 91, 33, 91, 61, 17, 533, 1022, 33, 91, 8, 314, 220, 16, 14, 17, 350, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 61, 17, 533, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 99940, 10620, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 314, 3609, 61948, 3851, 328, 6760, 29640, 431, 350, 21309, 10610, 328, 6760, 326, 8522, 741, 9024, 175342, 2454, 6760, 14518, 306, 428, 7054, 27661, 13, 34138, 1072, 1215, 428, 7054, 314, 21494, 3201, 1022, 33, 91, 13, 8820, 591, 42006, 350, 16, 3127, 395, 2454, 1215, 11, 21494, 22305, 33, 18085, 233, 87, 92, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 8, 314, 323, 12, 16, 13, 31663, 289, 1072, 1215, 8967, 21494, 22305, 87, 92, 21494, 22305, 33, 18085, 233, 87, 92, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 8, 314, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 741, 26982, 4307, 314, 21494, 3201, 21494, 22305, 87, 18085, 230, 33, 92, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 8, 314, 21494, 3201, 1022, 33, 91, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 741, 13602, 395, 2454, 4355, 418, 11, 480, 62274, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 8, 395, 2454, 328, 1617, 1022, 33, 91, 5571, 13, 2632, 581, 679, 1402, 10720, 3201, 1022, 33, 91, 350, 91, 33, 123685, 16, 8, 314, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 741, 350, 129214, 220, 19, 1029, 7943, 7477, 3561, 4307, 314, 21494, 3201, 350, 91, 33, 91, 61, 17, 533, 1022, 33, 91, 8, 314, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 61, 17, 533, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 364, 84787, 180687, 220, 19, 8967, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 61, 17, 533, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 314, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 741, 2632, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 61, 17, 314, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 8, 659, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 13, 9700, 364, 10620, 180687, 220, 18, 3561, 4307, 314, 220, 16, 14, 17, 350, 10720, 1022, 33, 91, 61, 17, 533, 21494, 1022, 33, 91, 8, 314, 220, 16, 14, 17, 425, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 8, 591, 71593, 19, 13, 2632, 3561, 4307, 314, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 11876, 17, 364, 84787, 323, 81061, 314, 323, 6932, 12, 16, 11876, 17, 871, 372, 314, 350, 85, 12, 16, 11876, 17, 314, 350, 1353, 2290, 533, 220, 16, 11876, 17, 314, 220, 1353, 504, 14, 17, 314, 220, 3234, 15, 364, 84787, 372, 2804, 413, 9707, 220, 3234, 15, 13, 2632, 290, 1606, 4149, 1432, 382, 220, 3234, 15, 364, 7943, 1309, 316, 14866, 24140, 25, 17484, 1354, 4310, 261, 2364, 52718, 31060, 483, 323, 28, 1353, 2290, 11, 372, 28, 3234, 15, 30, 1416, 24923, 372, 8155, 26, 1309, 316, 6757, 4149, 364, 2167, 1309, 316, 1646, 261, 920, 328, 27661, 326, 63009, 484, 35441, 6409, 13, 1328, 29212, 10860, 75745, 261, 73104, 2993, 585, 16499, 328, 2569, 2335, 30, 41021, 1746, 364, 39520, 2454, 10610, 328, 5571, 14518, 306, 9707, 1001, 4355, 11, 326, 2454, 4355, 2349, 14210, 11, 326, 2454, 4355, 328, 2349, 220, 17, 76, 10, 16, 21241, 306, 284, 63009, 11, 1217, 2454, 13501, 382, 261, 31512, 328, 631, 1511, 18125, 328, 14210, 16174, 364, 976, 24923, 61524, 19387, 372, 314, 350, 85, 12, 16, 11876, 17, 23994, 328, 4878, 11, 49328, 61524, 5060, 350, 13980, 25222, 402, 7060, 220, 17, 741, 2632, 1062, 8866, 484, 126205, 6409, 738, 679, 484, 372, 13, 2632, 6052, 382, 220, 3234, 15, 350, 22365, 741, 19792, 316, 6757, 16336, 24525, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 220, 3234, 15, 364, 2167, 2804, 4733, 392, 160761, 25, 220, 3234, 15, 4050], "n_tokens": 1644, "words": 995, "band_lo": 698.75, "band_hi": 2795.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to interpret the combinatorial structure.\n\nWe have 10001 students. They form clubs (sets of students). Condition 1: each unordered pair of students belongs to exactly one club. So clubs form a pairwise covering design: a pairwise block design where every pair of points appears in exactly one block. That's a Steiner system S(2, ?, v). Here block sizes can vary (odd sizes) but each pair exactly once.\n\nCondition 2: For each student and each society, the student is in exactly one club of the society. Means societies are collections of clubs? \"For each student and each society, the student is in exactly one club of the society.\" So a society consists of some clubs (maybe overlapping). For a given society S, and a given student x, there is exactly one club within S that contains x. So within a society, clubs partition the set of students (each student appears in exactly one club of that society). So each society is a partition of the students into clubs. Since clubs can belong to multiple societies.\n\nCondition 3: Each club has an odd number of students. A club with size 2m+1 is in exactly m societies.\n\nGoal: total number of societies k possible values.\n\nWe need to find possible designs satisfying these constraints for v=10001 (odd). Let's denote clubs as blocks. Each block B has size b=2m+1 (odd). In each block, it belongs to exactly m societies. So each block has multiplicity (number of societies containing it) = (b-1)/2.\n\nLet’s denote sets: Let V = set of students, |V|=n = 10001.\n\nLet’s have collection of clubs C. For each club B ∈ C, |B| odd. The pair condition: for each unordered pair {x,y} ⊂ V, there is exactly one B containing both. That's exactly a Steiner 2-design with variable block sizes, but still each pair uniquely contained.\n\nLet’s denote λ=1.\n\nStandard parameters for a 2-(v, k_i, 1) design with varying block sizes: number of blocks containing a given point x: r_x = number of clubs containing x. Because each other point y must be paired with x in exactly one club, each club containing x contributes (|B|-1) distinct y's. So sum_{B ∋ x} (|B|-1) = v-1 = 10000. (Equation 1)\n\nSimilarly, total number of unordered pairs is v(v-1)/2 = 10001*10000/2 = 10001*5000 = 50,005,000. Each club B contributes choose(|B|,2) pairs. So sum_{B∈C} C(|B|,2) = 50,005,000. (Equation 2)\n\nNow societies: each society partitions V into clubs. For a given society S, the clubs in S form a partition of V: they are pairwise disjoint and union all V. Since each student is in exactly one club of the society. Since clubs can belong to multiple societies, partitions can be different.\n\nLet’s denote for each club B, it belongs to m_B = (|B|-1)/2 societies.\n\nLet’s count incidences of (society, club): total number of pairs (S,B) with B ∈ S equals sum over clubs of m_B. Also can compute via societies: each society partitions V into clubs, of varying odd sizes, covering all V. So for a given society S, the number of clubs in S equals something; sum over societies of number of clubs is also sum m_B.\n\nConsider total number of club occurrences across societies: T = Σ_{B∈C} m_B = Σ_B (|B|-1)/2.\n\nNow also compute T via societies. For each society S, suppose it uses clubs with sizes s_i (odd). The number of clubs in S is number of parts in partition, denote t_S. Since the partition covers all v students, we have Σ_{i=1}^{t_S} s_i = v. Also each s_i odd.\n\nThus, sum over societies of t_S = total number of clubs used across societies = T.\n\nBut t_S is also something we could compute using each student's club membership? Each student belongs to exactly one club per society. So per society, there are v students each placed into clubs, resulting in total number of student-club incidences across societies equal v*k (each student for each society). Another way: each occurrence of a club B in a society accounts for all its |B| students. So sum over societies of sum over clubs in that society of |B| = v*k.\n\nBut also equals sum over clubs of (|B| * m_B) because each club appears in m_B societies. So:\n\nΣ_B |B| * m_B = v*k. (Equation 3)\n\nRecall m_B = (|B|-1)/2. So left side = Σ_B |B| * (|B|-1)/2 = 1/2 Σ_B (|B|^2 - |B|) = 1/2 ( Σ |B|^2 - Σ |B| ).\n\nNow Σ |B| = total incidences of student-club (each pair of student and club). Let denote each student appears in r_x clubs. Sum over x r_x = Σ_B |B|. Also from equation (1): for each x, Σ_{B∋x} (|B|-1) = v-1. Summing over x gives Σ_{x} Σ_{B∋x} (|B|-1) = v(v-1). Left side = Σ_B Σ_{x∈B} (|B|-1) = Σ_B |B| (|B|-1). Because for each block B, it contributes (|B|-1) for each of its |B| points. So we have:\n\nΣ_B |B| (|B|-1) = v(v-1). (Equation 4)\n\nBut note left side = Σ_B (|B|^2 - |B|) = Σ |B|^2 - Σ |B|.\n\nThus Equation 4 gives Σ |B|^2 - Σ |B| = v(v-1). So Σ |B|^2 = v(v-1) + Σ |B|. Good.\n\nNow Equation 3 left side = 1/2 (Σ |B|^2 - Σ |B|) = 1/2 * v(v-1) from Eq4. So left side = v(v-1)/2.\n\nThus v*k = v(v-1)/2 => k = (v-1)/2 = (10001 - 1)/2 = 10000/2 = 5000.\n\nThus k must be exactly 5000. So the only possible value is 5000.\n\nBut need to verify existence: Does there exist a design satisfying constraints with v=10001, k=5000? We derived k necessary; need to ensure possible.\n\nWe need to find a set of clubs and societies that satisfy conditions. This essentially requires constructing a finite projective plane of order q? Let's test.\n\nGiven each pair of points appears in exactly one block, and each block size odd, and each block of size 2m+1 occurs in m societies, also each society is a partition of V into blocks of odd sizes.\n\nThe derived equations forced k = (v-1)/2 regardless of details, assuming equations hold (which rely on condition 2). So any structure that satisfies conditions will have that k. So answer is 5000 (unique). Need to ensure integer obviously.\n\nThus answer: 5000.\n\nWe must output \"ANSWER: 5000\".", "response": "ANSWER: 5000", "answer": 5000, "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -0.00010025003564351209, "p_correct": 0.9998997549892233, "logp_correct": -0.00010025003564351209, "cot_lp_mean": -0.5063931835584357, "cot_lp_min64": -1.1932951229373963, "frac_below_-5": 0.00798035604665439, "digit_lp_min": -0.7243548631668091, "answer_first_mention_lp": -3.576278118089249e-07, "n_cot_tokens": 1629, "lp_end": -1.3470558769768104e-05, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -3.933898824470816e-06, "logp_nocot": -3.2995995581150055, "p_nocot": 0.03689793992388973, "uplift": 3.299499308079362}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "e98866f7-0de1-49c9-ada3-3765ee8b4757", "source": "dapo", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Kelvin and $15$ other frogs are in a meeting, for a total of $16$ frogs. During the meeting, each pair of distinct frogs becomes friends with probability $\\frac{1}{2}$. Kelvin thinks the situation after the meeting is [I]cool[/I] if for each of the $16$ frogs, the number of friends they made during the meeting is a multiple of $4$. Say that the probability of the situation being cool can be expressed in the form $\\frac{a}{b}$, where $a$ and $b$ are relatively prime. Find $a$.\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is the final integer answer.", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Kelvin and $15$ other frogs are in a meeting, for a total of $16$ frogs. During the meeting, each pair of distinct frogs becomes friends with probability $\\frac{1}{2}$. Kelvin thinks the situation after the meeting is [I]cool[/I] if for each of the $16$ frogs, the number of friends they made during the meeting is a multiple of $4$. Say that the probability of the situation being cool can be expressed in the form $\\frac{a}{b}$, where $a$ and $b$ are relatively prime. Find $a$.", "true_answer": 1167, "origin": "base", "source_ref": "e98866f7-0de1-49c9-ada3-3765ee8b4757:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 679, 220, 1125, 175684, 350, 26167, 181775, 741, 19171, 844, 149617, 7465, 402, 220, 1125, 38360, 1919, 2454, 11165, 14518, 38341, 483, 4921, 220, 16, 14, 17, 13, 2214, 2454, 25363, 11, 1617, 9882, 2804, 413, 167813, 656, 220, 19, 13, 1416, 1309, 34933, 484, 722, 25363, 18210, 553, 70720, 328, 220, 19, 13, 45438, 3605, 328, 73392, 1919, 2454, 25363, 9882, 42308, 94, 15, 1812, 19, 11, 38484, 656, 3609, 73392, 220, 17, 42923, 34, 7, 1125, 11, 17, 15468, 364, 2167, 1309, 2086, 328, 177015, 75935, 123676, 483, 12421, 71638, 1919, 2