{"qid": "1179a239-6d9e-4a7c-b1c3-7e6f2ceca25c", "source": "dapo", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: In a rectangular $57 \\times 57$ grid of cells, $k$ of the cells are colored black. What is the smallest positive integer $k$ such that there must exist a rectangle, with sides parallel to the edges of the grid, that has its four vertices at the center of distinct black cells?\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is the final integer answer.", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: In a rectangular $57 \\times 57$ grid of cells, $k$ of the cells are colored black. What is the smallest positive integer $k$ such that there must exist a rectangle, with sides parallel to the edges of the grid, that has its four vertices at the center of distinct black cells?", "true_answer": 457, "origin": "base", "source_ref": "1179a239-6d9e-4a7c-b1c3-7e6f2ceca25c:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 679, 220, 5085, 87, 5085, 10586, 871, 5571, 540, 26037, 328, 11242, 13, 25151, 372, 5960, 11242, 13, 27042, 16218, 484, 1354, 13031, 448, 16300, 13254, 3626, 45808, 12119, 4242, 39479, 553, 5960, 4206, 26037, 11, 722, 16913, 13, 1328, 382, 1299, 12129, 261, 141795, 190565, 25307, 68745, 45808, 306, 261, 10586, 13, 197203, 316, 25, 581, 679, 261, 220, 5085, 87, 5085, 15600, 12248, 11, 483, 372, 8104, 13, 9764, 19957, 372, 2238, 484, 1062, 29002, 328, 372, 8104, 16691, 261, 392, 639, 11893, 68745, 45808, 1, 575, 2560, 4213, 1920, 13585, 326, 1920, 15697, 1919, 722, 4242, 143513, 553, 5960, 13, 1328, 382, 290, 392, 65, 488, 497, 651, 137209, 1, 4792, 25, 290, 65043, 1104, 662, 42125, 4792, 25, 10562, 2086, 328, 22569, 306, 54467, 497, 651, 7465, 2935, 261, 658, 22305, 17, 11, 17, 92, 350, 72, 2560, 4213, 363, 19, 741, 7306, 13585, 326, 15697, 553, 38360, 26, 5960, 11242, 553, 22569, 13, 27042, 19957, 372, 2238, 484, 1062, 54467, 497,