{"qid": "43242339-0c8e-4e4e-8ddb-f74e3a73f91a", "source": "dapo", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Somewhere in the universe, $n$ students are taking a $10$-question math competition.  Their collective performance is called [i]laughable[/i] if, for some pair of questions, there exist $57$ students such that either all of them answered both questions correctly or none of them answered both questions correctly.  Compute the smallest $n$ such that the performance is necessarily laughable.\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is the final integer answer.", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Somewhere in the universe, $n$ students are taking a $10$-question math competition.  Their collective performance is called [i]laughable[/i] if, for some pair of questions, there exist $57$ students such that either all of them answered both questions correctly or none of them answered both questions correctly.  Compute the smallest $n$ such that the performance is necessarily laughable.", "true_answer": 253, "origin": "base", "source_ref": "43242339-0c8e-4e4e-8ddb-f74e3a73f91a:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 42173, 297, 2238, 484, 1062, 920, 328, 297, 15600, 52254, 328, 5517, 220, 702, 350, 52315, 6145, 14, 131685, 8, 2804, 10232, 261, 10610, 328, 27933, 350, 36007, 8, 2238, 484, 1354, 13031, 261, 58845, 328, 220, 5085, 4501, 1919, 4784, 722, 679, 2684, 18189, 402, 2617, 1920, 27933, 350, 47163, 220, 16, 8, 503, 2973, 220, 15, 30, 24305, 392, 105049, 722, 328, 1373, 28446, 2973, 5359, 20323, 503, 12698, 328, 1373, 28446, 2973, 5359, 20323, 3692, 125152, 3518, 2617, 220, 5085, 4501, 11, 395, 484, 10610, 328, 5359, 11, 4784, 1753, 6760, 3508, 2973, 1849, 350, 72, 2560, 4213, 8302, 350, 16, 11, 16, 915, 503, 1753, 6760, 3508, 2973, 8201, 350, 15, 11, 15, 741, 1225, 2226, 625, 1841, 6137, 1078, 16435, 18587, 