505, 1819, 290, 73005, 9874, 28026, 13, 21926, 1299, 392, 371, 343, 32246, 128540, 81, 2367, 69029, 50557, 363, 18, 71, 382, 625, 5355, 364, 7943, 4335, 290, 3880, 11, 12951, 290, 1001, 484, 382, 175798, 483, 363, 18, 16300, 326, 25511, 16499, 889, 860, 17679, 41666, 503, 363, 17, 51760, 382, 10112, 290, 2974, 4151, 58, 1008, 6045, 371, 366, 13186, 501, 16074, 690, 30, 30456, 413, 415, 18, 71, 30, 4037, 3239, 364, 58369, 28035, 2454, 945, 364, 32707, 276, 467, 2283, 3643, 16641, 379, 25, 623, 418, 382, 540, 6170, 11, 3407, 532, 63489, 6771, 11, 2454, 532, 18618, 316, 382, 467, 2283, 3643, 3566, 350, 3583, 140797, 18, 8, 17, 741, 1843, 2454, 382, 467, 2283, 3643, 93819, 2238, 484, 1043, 1920, 101385, 8896, 553, 123676, 5151, 326, 4895, 290, 16499, 30, 623, 382, 467, 2283, 3643, 3566, 382, 625, 123676, 26, 4275, 74343, 3706, 25, 10049, 140797, 18, 8, 17, 13, 623, 15883, 18618, 316, 532, 382, 549, 46047, 30, 50557, 625, 549, 46047, 11, 889, 290, 92838, 15286, 316, 11728, 328, 25511, 28026, 364, 84787, 625, 363, 18, 71, 364, 2231, 9712, 565, 110815, 25, 723, 34, 22, 39, 1311, 45, 60, 8866, 382, 1299, 261, 23273, 3636, 68141, 483, 3407, 16111, 75438, 64592, 44860, 261, 89643, 76776, 61908, 13, 623, 90882, 382, 415, 18, 67, 30, 24305, 474, 9712, 565, 110815, 382, 290, 87455, 152173, 328, 64374, 1233, 130036, 30, 13974, 8866, 382, 197465, 25, 1225, 382, 290, 220, 16, 12, 1071, 378, 3869, 565, 78, 58, 17, 13, 17, 13, 17, 60, 82236, 1986, 30, 21926, 474, 9712, 565, 110815, 13, 220, 16, 12, 1071, 378, 3869, 565, 78, 58, 17, 13, 17, 13, 17, 60, 82236, 1986, 853, 415, 18, 67, 90882, 350, 9995, 27789, 78, 22803, 1986, 306, 16540, 1625, 741, 50557, 220, 16, 12, 1071, 378, 3869, 565, 78, 58, 17, 13, 17, 13, 17, 60, 82236, 1986, 853, 448, 70924, 6170, 11, 3407, 363, 17, 51760, 30, 7744, 6771, 316, 11777, 26918, 1986, 30, 41021, 2411, 25, 418, 3869, 565, 78, 58, 17, 13, 17, 13, 17, 60, 82236, 1986, 350, 34, 23, 39, 899, 8, 853, 415, 18, 67, 90882, 350, 9995, 261, 85242, 32246, 172396, 741, 1843, 481, 13284, 261, 15883, 483, 68141, 11, 2928, 415, 18, 67, 13, 415, 18, 67, 6664, 363, 18, 16300, 11, 363, 17, 137754, 11, 25511, 28026, 16499, 30, 415, 18, 67, 853, 336, 21, 11, 5178, 13, 1225, 6664, 363, 18, 16300, 11, 3407, 363, 17, 51760, 137754, 11, 70924, 6170, 11, 326, 3669, 67, 350, 4091, 47970, 741, 4037, 363, 18, 71, 364, 84787, 474, 9712, 565, 110815, 382, 415, 18, 67, 11, 625, 363, 18, 71, 364, 19884, 4151, 58, 1008, 6045, 371, 366, 13186, 501, 16074, 690, 25, 138743, 415, 18, 71, 1423, 54458, 413, 1299, 261, 11082, 76732, 1900, 12796, 138672, 316, 3407, 285, 13186, 12, 16, 11, 18, 2469, 4655, 13306, 13, 4569, 2023, 3644, 415, 18, 71, 483, 363, 18, 16300, 11, 3407, 363, 17, 51760, 11, 3669, 71, 16499, 11, 326, 17679, 3669, 85, 885, 30, 4037, 3239, 364, 33418, 5447, 88, 3303, 78, 58, 1008, 6045, 371, 366, 13186, 501, 16074, 690, 25, 54458, 413, 415, 18, 71, 472, 1775, 364, 2167, 1309, 1118, 853, 363, 18, 71, 16515, 13, 32417, 19271, 53785, 11, 363, 18, 71, 382, 395, 319, 1940, 4213, 79397, 295, 21868, 328, 3407, 32820, 22148, 84, 1094, 402, 261, 85242, 32246, 150868, 28699, 73005, 483, 70924, 30, 50557, 10112, 392, 15630, 4806, 1, 9591, 1299, 722, 1900, 30, 3004, 364, 58369, 8065, 3684, 8197, 25, 363, 18, 71, 2438, 3566, 15652, 25, 392, 197115, 7, 106804, 8, 44624, 1900, 69029, 4037, 364, 39520, 5846, 2713, 11, 1023, 1340, 2665, 6760, 316, 7477, 484, 1606, 363, 18, 71, 382, 23121, 656, 261, 73005, 484, 853, 261, 363, 18, 16300, 326, 261, 25511, 28026, 16499, 889, 860, 17679, 41666, 13, 623, 1606, 1001, 6960, 316, 679, 484, 382, 290, 2974, 4151, 58, 16, 11, 17, 3452, 25, 18, 11, 19, 3452, 2337, 20, 11, 21, 3452, 6, 1089, 371, 366, 13186, 12, 16, 11, 18, 11, 19, 11, 21, 11, 22, 11, 24, 60074, 16074, 690, 1118, 382, 175798, 326, 853, 1606, 363, 18, 326, 3669, 71, 11, 889, 5192, 316, 3407, 15883, 3643, 8896, 36276, 5357, 194494, 2905, 10112, 1217, 853, 220, 18, 363, 17, 30, 1843, 138672, 12796, 5357, 194494, 2905, 11, 10112, 415, 18, 71, 364, 7943, 12951, 484, 73005, 382, 175798, 483, 415, 18, 71, 11, 625, 363, 18, 71, 13, 623, 12384, 1001, 350, 51122, 5447, 88, 3303, 78, 29081, 1340, 413, 2893, 10838, 277, 889, 853, 363, 18, 326, 3669, 71, 1606, 871, 363, 18, 71, 13, 41021, 2411, 25, 19291, 5447, 88, 3303, 78, 154071, 371, 366, 13186, 1008, 7890, 316, 413, 261, 12384, 14600, 4523, 76776, 2420, 1919, 290, 11082, 10089, 382, 1299, 261, 5892, 4806, 484, 382, 625, 175798, 26, 2023, 679, 261, 25511, 28026, 16499, 1819, 290, 11082, 12796, 889, 17679, 11728, 328, 90882, 364, 84787, 6052, 10112, 363, 350, 51122, 5447, 88, 3303, 78, 153558, 41021, 5655, 363, 364], "n_tokens": 1745, "words": 1043, "band_lo": 521.5, "band_hi": 2086.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to determine which molecule among the options has C3h symmetry. C3h point group: has a C3 principal axis and a horizontal mirror plane (σh) perpendicular to that axis. It also includes a S3 improper rotation? Actually C3h includes C3 and σh, leading to S3 (C3 * σh). The group has elements: E, C3, C3^2, σh, S3, S3^5 (or S3^5?), but basically need molecule with C3 axis and horizontal mirror plane but no C2 axes. So which of the given molecules has such symmetry.\n\nLet's think about structures.\n\n(1) Triisopropyl borate: structure B(OiPr)3. Boron with three isopropoxy groups attached. Typically trigonal planar around B? Actually boron is sp2, borate anion maybe tetrahedral? Triisopropyl borate (B(OCH(CH3)2)3). The B atom attached to three O atoms each attached to isopropyl groups. The overall molecule is similar to B(OR)3, where R groups are identical. If the three isopropyl groups are arranged symmetrically around B, the point group would be C3v if the substituents are identical and arrangement is trigonal planar. However presence of horizontal mirror plane? Triisopropyl borate is not planar; the B is trigonal planar but the O-alkyl groups have some conformations. If each isopropyl is not symmetric, likely reduces symmetry. C3h would require mirror plane perpendicular to C3 axis (i.e., plane through the B and O atoms? Actually horizontal plane through B? Wait C3 axis vertical, σh horizontal. For B(OR)3 planar, you'd have a C3 axis through B perpendicular to the plane, and the plane itself is σh (the molecular plane). That would be C3h? Actually planar trigonal with identical substituents: point group D3h if there are also three C2 axes perpendicular to the principal axis. B(OR)3 planar would have D3h: C3 axis, three C2 axes in plane, σh (the molecular plane) and three σv vertical. However due to substituents being not planar (they protrude out of plane), the C2 axes are lost, leaving C3v maybe. C3v includes C3 axis and 3 vertical sigma planes. There's no horizontal sigma. C3h is rarer. It could be like staggered ethane? Actually staggered ethane belongs to D3d.\n\nThus triisopropyl borate likely not C3h.\n\n(2) Quinuclidine: bicyclic amine (C7H13N), structure is like a bridged piperidine; symmetry? Quinuclidine is a bicyclic cage with C2v? Actually quinuclidine has a C2 axis through nitrogen and opposite carbon? Might be D3? No. Likely C2v or C3? Not.\n\n(3) Benzo[1,2-c:3,4-c':5,6-c'']trifuran-1,3,4,6,7,9-hexaone. That's likely a fused aromatic system? Need to visualize: a benzo fused to three furan-1,3-diones? Complex. Might have C3h symmetry? The name suggests threefold symmetry around a central benzene ring fused to three furan-1,3-diones. Could be like a trio of carbonyl groups arranged cyclically with a horizontal mirror plane. Possibly.\n\n(4) Triphenyleno[1,2-c:5,6-c':9,10-c'']trifuran-1,3,6,8,11,13-hexaone. That's like larger fused system maybe with D3h.\n\nWe need C3h specifically.\n\nC3h point group arises in molecules like staggered propeller shapes with a horizontal mirror plane, like certain trisubstituted pyramidal compounds where substituents are arranged in a propeller with equal twist such that there is a plane perpendicular to the C3 axis that cuts through the molecule giving mirror. That's like \"trigonal antiprism\"? Actually C3h is not common.\n\nBut given the options, perhaps the one that is planar with C3 axis and horizontal plane but no vertical planes or C2 axes is maybe the benzo[... ]trifuran hexaone? Could be D3h? Not sure.\n\nLet's examine each more.\n\nTriisopropyl borate: The B is at center, three O atoms similar, each O attached to isopropyl group (CH(CH3)2). If each isopropyl rotated such that their two methyl groups are symmetric above and below the plane? The isopropyl group is not symmetric; it's branched: CH(CH3)2. The carbon attached to O is chiral? Actually not chiral, but the substitution leads to lack of horizontal mirror.\n\nThus not C3h.\n\nQuinuclidine: [C7H13N] structure is like a bridgehead nitrogen with three ethylene bridges forming a bicyclic cage. The symmetry is D3d? Wait quinuclidine is the saturated analogue of quinoxaline? Its structure is symmetrical: It is the 1-azabicyclo[2.2.2]octane? That's quinuclidine. 1-azabicyclo[2.2.2]octane has D3d symmetry (like cyclohexane in chair form). Actually 1-azabicyclo[2.2.2]octane has an inversion center, three C2 axes? It's similar to norbornane? Let's think: Bicyclo[2.2.2]octane (C8H12) has D3d symmetry (like a trigonal prism). If you replace a carbon with nitrogen, still D3d. D3d includes C3 axis, C2 perpendicular, horizontal mirror plane? D3d has S6, etc. It includes C3 axis, three C2 axes perpendicular, inversion center, and σd (dihedral). Not C3h.\n\nThus quinuclidine is D3d, not C3h.\n\nBenzo[... ]trifuran hexaone: Possibly D3h ? Might be like a central benzene ring fused to three furan-1,3-dione units. That could give D3h with C3 axis, three C2 axes, σh plane, and vertical σv's? Not sure.\n\nTriphenyleno[... ]trifuran hexaone: Might be D3h as well.\n\nWe need which has C3h specifically. Among typical molecules, C3h is for e.g., staggered arrangement of three identical substituents on a trigonal pyramidal molecule with inversion? Actually maybe \"propeller\" shape like allene? No.\n\nLet's quickly search memory: C3h point group examples: \"tris(ethylene)benzene\"? Not.\n\nGiven exam style, they may expect student to note that only C3h is satisfied by a molecule that has a C3 axis and a horizontal mirror plane but no vertical planes. The only one likely to have that is the benzo[1,2-c:3,4-c':5,6-c'']trifuran-1,3,4,6,7,9-hexaone which is planar and has only C3 and σh, but due to three carbonyl groups arranged symmetrically maybe also has 3 C2? If fused ring symmetrically, maybe D3h.\n\nBut perhaps that molecule is planar with D3h, not C3h. The larger one (triphenyleno...) may be nonplanar but has C3 and σh only => C3h. Let's think: Triphenyleno[...]trifuran... seems to be a larger polycyclic system where the central core is like a propeller that is not planar; could have a horizontal mirror plane through the central ring but vertical lack of symmetry.\n\nThus answer maybe C (triphenyleno...). Let's choose C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.1920922133867862e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999941, "logp_correct": -5.9244706618424585e-15, "letter_mass": 1.000000000000006, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.7162580856752291, "cot_lp_min64": -1.4017790406557715, "frac_below_-5": 0.01674364896073903, "digit_lp_min": -2.0277016162872314, "answer_first_mention_lp": null, "n_cot_tokens": 1732, "lp_end": -0.43117430806159973, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -3.576278118089249e-07, "logp_nocot": -5.663984490892498, "p_nocot": 0.0034686684491789777, "uplift": 5.663984490892492, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.114866, "B": 0.848755, "C": 0.003469, "D": 0.03291}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "rec2mwDP38Ocj5kO9", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Why does the hydroboration reaction between a conjugated diene and Ipc2BH form a single product, even at different temperatures?\n\nA) The given reaction is stereospecific, and hence only one stereoisomer is formed.\nB) It is a concerted reaction, and no rearrangements are possible.\nC) The formation of the product is independent of the temperature at which the reaction takes place.\nD) The reaction is syn-addition, which means both groups are added to the same face, leading to a single product.\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Why does the hydroboration reaction between a conjugated diene and Ipc2BH form a single product, even at different temperatures?\n\nA) The given reaction is stereospecific, and hence only one stereoisomer is formed.\nB) It is a concerted reaction, and no rearrangements are possible.\nC) The formation of the product is independent of the temperature at which the reaction takes place.\nD) The reaction is syn-addition, which means both groups are added to the same face, leading to a single product.\n", "true_answer": "B", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "rec2mwDP38Ocj5kO9:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 30532, 290, 4928, 13, 71722, 6270, 387, 328, 261, 89227, 780, 272, 6628, 483, 357, 6344, 17, 118015, 350, 4091, 276, 467, 2283, 3643, 6270, 1986, 8, 44860, 261, 4590, 1888, 11, 115053, 328, 12088, 13, 22483, 1402, 32, 8, 129157, 382, 51516, 365, 16416, 11, 1606, 1001, 51516, 20671, 22516, 20680, 558, 33, 8, 62838, 295, 21416, 11, 860, 98785, 147657, 4149, 558, 34, 8, 7451, 18704, 13313, 328, 12088, 558, 35, 8, 129157, 382, 9041, 40367, 868, 11, 2973, 8896, 5768, 316, 2684, 4950, 11, 8117, 316, 261, 4590, 1888, 364, 34405, 