, 15, 13, 47419, 8076, 364, 21106, 314, 646, 710, 365, 8087, 15, 13, 47419, 8076, 8, 314, 220, 10676, 13, 19, 6793, 364, 84787, 3411, 6574, 16620, 148177, 7396, 6574, 10676, 172051, 17796, 355, 25, 220, 15363, 148177, 10676, 6793, 15248, 364, 84787, 6052, 7158, 355, 13], "n_tokens": 807, "words": 204, "band_lo": 131.25, "band_hi": 525.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to find apparent contact angle on rough surface using Cassie-Baxter equation:\n\ncos θ* = f_s * cos θ + f_v * cos 180° (air). Where f_s = area fraction of solid (coating) in contact with liquid, f_v = 1 - f_s = area fraction of air. cos 180° = -1. So:\n\ncos θ* = f_s * cos θ - (1 - f_s).\n\nGiven f_s = 0.47, f_v = 0.53.\n\nGiven intrinsic (smooth) contact angles: θ_w = 127°, θ_o = 96°.\n\nCompute cos for each:\n\ncos 127°: Need value. Cos 127°=cos(180-53)= -cos53°. cos53°≈0.6018. So cos127° = -0.6018.\n\ncos 96°: cos 96° = cos(90+6) = -sin6° ≈ -0.104528. Let's compute: sin6°≈0.1045. So cos96° ≈ -0.1045.\n\nNow compute apparent:\n\ncos θ*_w = 0.47 * (-0.6018) - (1-0.47) = (0.47 * -0.6018) - 0.53.\n\n0.47 * -0.6018 = -0.282846. Subtract 0.53 => -0.282846 - 0.53 = -0.812846.\n\nThus cos θ*_w ≈ -0.812846.\n\nNow get θ*_w = arccos(-0.812846). arccos negative >90°. Compute angle: cos 144° = cos(180-36)= -cos36°. cos36°≈0.8090. So cos144°≈ -0.8090. That's close. Cos 145° = -cos35°= -0.8192. Our value -0.8128 corresponds to angle approx 144.5°. So about 144-145°. Options: A water 144°, B 148°, C 151°, D 140°. Closest is A (144°). Good.\n\nNow oil: cos θ*_o = 0.47 * (-0.1045) - 0.53 = -0.049115 - 0.53 = -0.579115.\n\nθ*_o = arccos(-0.5791). cos 125° = -cos55° = -0.5736. cos126° = -cos54° = -0.5878. So angle ~125.5°. Options: A oil125°, B 131°, C 136°, D 118°. Closest is A (125°). So answer A.\n\nThus answer choice A.\n\nCheck rounding? Might there be slight difference using more precise numbers.\n\nLet's compute more precisely:\n\ncos127° = cos(127*π/180) =? Use calculator mental: cos127° = -0.601815. Good.\n\ncos96° = -0.104528.\n\nNow compute:\n\ncos* water = 0.47*(-0.601815) - 0.53 = -0.282852 +? Actually -0.282852 - 0.53 = -0.812852.\n\nAngle = arccos(-0.812852) = 144.7°.\n\nOil: cos* = 0.47*(-0.104528) -0.53 = -0.049128 -0.53 = -0.579128.\n\nAngle = arccos(-0.579128) = 125.4°.\n\nThus water ~145°, oil ~125°. Option A: 144°,125° matches.\n\nThus answer choice A.", "response": "ANSWER: A", "answer": "A", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -5.8412379075889476e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999605, "logp_correct": -3.949864443086087e-14, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000395, "p_letters": {"A": 1.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.29981198220364047, "cot_lp_min64": -0.7625679702305086, "frac_below_-5": 0.008816120906801008, "digit_lp_min": -4.161748886108398, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.031737811863422394, "n_cot_tokens": 794, "lp_end": -5.8412379075889476e-06, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -2.3841855067985307e-07, "logp_nocot": -6.065675649570596, "p_nocot": 0.0023211891741276997, "uplift": 6.065675649570557, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.002321, "B": 0.729296, "C": 0.268293, "D": 9e-05}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "rec4SDXAy1UuwcoHP", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: The integrated spectrum of a galaxy with z= 0.0018 shows that the Hydrogen molecule line ratios are 1–0S(2) / 1–0S(0) = 1.62 and 1–0S(1) / 2–1S(1) = 7.3, while for the ionized lines in the spectra, the derredened fluxes referenced to Hb are:\n\nHa = 3.07\n[OIII] λ5007 = 10.6\n[FeII] λ16435 = 0.8\n[N II] λ6583 = 1.91\n\nWhich of the following emitting phenomena better describes the observed fluxes? Star formation, an accreting supermassive black hole, an evolved stellar population, or a low metallicity and low ionization interstellar medium.\n\nA) Star formation\nB) An accreting supermassive black hole\nC) An evolved stellar population\nD) A low metallicity and low ionization interstellar medium\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: The integrated spectrum of a galaxy with z= 0.0018 shows that the Hydrogen molecule line ratios are 1–0S(2) / 1–0S(0) = 1.62 and 1–0S(1) / 2–1S(1) = 7.3, while for the ionized lines in the spectra, the derredened fluxes referenced to Hb are:\n\nHa = 3.07\n[OIII] λ5007 = 10.6\n[FeII] λ16435 = 0.8\n[N II] λ6583 = 1.91\n\nWhich of the following emitting phenomena better describes the observed fluxes? Star formation, an accreting supermassive black hole, an evolved stellar population, or a low metallicity and low ionization interstellar medium.\n\nA) Star formation\nB) An accreting supermassive black hole\nC) An evolved stellar population\nD) A low metallicity and low ionization interstellar medium\n", "true_answer": "B", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "rec4SDXAy1UuwcoHP:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 18135, 4335, 55890, 2543, 69972, 25, 487, 17, 36628, 8698, 25, 220, 16, 12, 15, 336, 7, 17, 11876, 16, 12, 15, 336, 7, 15, 25987, 16, 13, 8947, 326, 220, 16, 12, 15, 336, 7, 16, 11876, 17, 12, 16, 336, 7, 16, 25987, 22, 13, 18, 13, 8820, 26485, 2110, 8698, 15001, 316, 487, 6331, 25, 487, 727, 37632, 6331, 28, 18, 13, 3173, 11, 723, 46, 23565, 60, 3234, 22, 37632, 6331, 28, 702, 13, 21, 11, 723, 5563, 6013, 60, 220, 16, 13, 44545, 81193, 76, 37632, 6331, 28, 15, 13, 23, 11, 723, 45, 6013, 60, 46004, 18, 37632, 6331, 28, 16, 13, 8956, 364, 2167, 1309, 316, 13001, 1118, 46487, 15248, 25, 8253, 18704, 350, 39, 6013, 21043, 936, 19215, 45, 350, 359, 894, 1744, 115235, 39, 936, 48656, 71974, 11540, 350, 68, 1940, 4213, 1926, 12, 2971, 33, 30, 114646, 866, 95807, 503, 4465, 142865, 122465, 11, 4465, 97321, 2860, 5436, 44, 364, 58369, 30890, 19271, 2543, 69972, 1402, 12, 487, 727, 37632, 6331, 89075, 19119, 180524, 6574, 17, 13, 7189, 395, 1890, 418, 540, 220, 702, 61, 19, 658, 13, 54666, 295, 220, 18, 13, 3173, 24832, 45226, 43921, 7299, 11, 25435, 364, 12, 723, 46, 23565, 18500, 39, 6331, 314, 220, 702, 13, 21, 382, 1932, 26, 19271, 487, 6013, 21043, 679, 723, 46, 23565, 18500, 39, 6331, 464, 93, 18, 10112, 869, 316, 220, 20, 395, 1932, 15801, 153981, 13, 220, 702, 13, 21, 23379, 19215, 45, 350, 50, 806, 71014, 8, 503, 4465, 60970, 536, 350, 21910, 532, 37632, 4465, 11, 12088, 1932, 8967, 5532, 723, 46, 23565, 21953, 3072, 478, 6013, 37632, 727, 18051, 30, 478, 6013, 37632, 727, 314, 350, 45, 6013, 37632, 6331, 60504, 39, 727, 37632, 6331, 8, 314, 220, 16, 13, 8956, 14, 18, 13, 3173, 314, 220, 15, 13, 39589, 13, 21926, 36748, 26, 19271, 8253, 44860, 129137, 679, 478, 6013, 37632, 727, 464, 15, 13, 20, 26, 19215, 45, 679, 1424, 15, 13, 21, 13, 2632, 220, 15, 13, 21, 185028, 364, 12, 723, 5563, 6013, 60, 220, 16, 13, 44545, 81193, 76, 820, 487, 6331, 314, 220, 15, 13, 23, 13, 41631, 723, 5563, 6013, 60, 4783, 8668, 483, 117317, 11, 2539, 86923, 152286, 11, 19215, 45, 24125, 2543, 7967, 11, 1217, 483, 48656, 8253, 11540, 30, 4037, 19271, 395, 14147, 487, 6013, 364, 39, 17, 2543, 69972, 25, 623, 18051, 220, 16, 12, 15, 336, 7, 16, 11876, 17, 12, 16, 336, 7, 16, 8, 314, 220, 22, 13, 18, 13, 103594, 163125, 59684, 1932, 18051, 65176, 702, 12, 1055, 741, 29490, 134145, 59684, 6931, 65176, 17, 741, 2632, 18051, 220, 22, 13, 18, 24832, 35031, 350, 198935, 503, 2127, 37601, 8, 2932, 1236, 29490, 10112, 13, 220, 16, 12, 15, 336, 7, 17, 11876, 16, 12, 15, 336, 7, 15, 25987, 16, 13, 8947, 11, 35031, 115092, 6574, 16, 13, 20, 350, 140634, 12088, 741, 2632, 20434, 483, 35031, 364, 84787, 487, 17, 55890, 382, 17576, 2146, 15209, 11, 6960, 5192, 316, 117317, 11, 19215, 45, 2127, 37601, 25419, 11, 5178, 364, 39520, 5532, 723, 46, 23565, 18500, 39, 6331, 326, 36748, 723, 45, 6013, 18500, 39, 727, 11, 2932, 35031, 487, 17, 11, 23379, 19215, 45, 350, 359, 894, 1744, 115235, 39, 8, 503, 117317, 591, 2539, 86923, 68, 306, 8253, 87709, 30, 730, 8253, 44860, 7967, 11, 723, 46, 23565, 60, 625, 484, 1932, 11, 326, 487, 17, 18051, 1481, 413, 6931, 350, 32844, 3599, 1939, 741, 8820, 723, 5563, 6013, 60, 36748, 364, 25613, 60970, 536, 11, 4465, 26485, 2860, 5436, 44, 25, 4465, 60970, 536, 15286, 316, 1932, 723, 46, 23565, 18500, 39, 6331, 889, 4465, 478, 6013, 37632, 727, 350, 21910, 478, 4465, 741, 7306, 478, 6013, 37632, 727, 6574, 15, 13, 21, 625, 4465, 13, 2632, 4465, 60970, 536, 625, 364, 36, 94254, 71974, 11540, 350, 3786, 12, 2971, 33, 8, 665, 10635, 114646, 866, 22085, 4465, 26485, 2860, 8698, 11, 13586, 723, 46, 23565, 18500, 39, 6331, 11, 625, 1932, 364, 84787, 1636, 382, 19215, 45, 350, 359, 894, 1744, 115235, 39, 741, 2632, 6052, 418, 13], "n_tokens": 701, "words": 305, "band_lo": 141.0, "band_hi": 564.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to interpret given emission line ratios: H2 molecular lines: 1-0 S(2)/1-0 S(0)=1.62 and 1-0 S(1)/2-1 S(1)=7.3. Also ionized lines relative to Hβ: Hα/Hβ=3.07, [OIII]5007/Hβ=10.6, [FeII] 1.644 µm/Hβ=0.8, [NII]6583/Hβ=1.91.\n\nWe need to decide which phenomenon matches: star formation (HII regions), AGN (accreting SMBH), evolved stellar population (e.g., post-AGB? LINER?), or low-metallicity, low-ionization ISM.\n\nLet's recall typical line ratios:\n\n- Hα/Hβ intrinsic recombination ~2.86 for case B at 10^4 K. Observed 3.07 indicates modest reddening, okay.\n\n- [OIII]/Hβ = 10.6 is high; typical HII regions have [OIII]/Hβ <~3 maybe up to 5 for high-excitation. 10.6 suggests AGN (Seyfert) or low metallicity (since O/H low, temperature high gives strong [OIII]). But NII/Hα ratio? NII/Hα = (NII/Hβ)/(Hα/Hβ) = 1.91/3.07 = 0.622. That's moderate; typical star forming galaxies have NII/Hα <0.5; AGN have >0.6. So 0.6 borderline.\n\n- [FeII] 1.644 µm / Hβ = 0.8. Strong [FeII] often associated with shocks, supernova remnants, AGN narrow line region, also with evolved star population? Not typical for pure HII.\n\nH2 line ratios: The ratio 1-0 S(1)/2-1 S(1) = 7.3. Thermal excitation yields high ratio (~10-15). UV fluorescence yields lower (~2). So ratio 7.3 indicates thermal (shock or X-ray) plus some UV maybe. 1-0 S(2)/1-0 S(0)=1.62, thermal predicts ~1.5 (depends temperature). So consistent with thermal.\n\nThus H2 emission is thermally excited, likely due to shocks, AGN X-ray heating, etc.\n\nGiven strong [OIII]/Hβ and moderate [NII]/Hα, plus thermal H2, suggests AGN (accreting SMBH) or shocks from supernovae in starburst? In star forming region, [OIII] not that high, and H2 ratio would be lower (fluorescent). Also [FeII] moderate.\n\nLow metallicity, low ionization ISM: low metallicity leads to high [OIII]/Hβ but low NII/Hα (since N low). Here NII/Hα ~0.6 not low. So low metallicity not.\n\nEvolved stellar population (post-AGB) can produce LINER-like low ionization lines, weak [OIII]/Hβ, not high.\n\nThus best is AGN (accreting SMBH). So answer B.", "response": "ANSWER: B", "answer": "B", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -8.702239938429557e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999246, "logp_correct": -7.54031460991856e-14, "letter_mass": 1.00000000