75, 382, 2684, 49895, 364, 84787, 581, 17722, 25, 44237, 2407, 61, 17, 659, 284, 109888, 61, 17, 8, 659, 275, 314, 391, 122020, 350, 54065, 2896, 53, 4308, 61, 17, 483, 274, 28, 16, 741, 9024, 284, 314, 11442, 13, 22, 11, 391, 28, 16840, 13, 21, 13, 116151, 395, 275, 364, 12845, 457, 109888, 314, 44237, 2407, 61, 17, 659, 284, 61, 17, 741, 7801, 3609, 314, 457, 109888, 659, 275, 314, 391, 13, 69048, 81, 25, 44237, 2407, 61, 17, 659, 284, 61, 17, 8, 314, 391, 533, 275, 13, 22980, 2973, 18089, 25, 275, 61, 17, 659, 284, 61, 17, 314, 391, 61, 17, 533, 17, 391, 275, 659, 275, 61, 17, 871, 13491, 275, 61, 17, 871, 284, 61, 17, 314, 391, 61, 17, 533, 17, 391, 275, 871, 17722, 275, 314, 350, 44, 61, 17, 533, 284, 61, 17, 60504, 17, 391, 3991, 13022, 10954, 5542, 20690, 395, 1920, 19146, 57549, 540, 2867, 483, 4842, 2695, 3099, 1888, 13, 45438, 25, 391, 61, 17, 314, 220, 16840, 13, 21, 61, 17, 314, 35717, 23864, 25, 220, 16840, 13, 21, 61, 17, 314, 350, 10165, 12, 15, 13, 19, 73602, 17, 314, 220, 6514, 504, 533, 220, 17, 9, 10165, 9, 15, 13, 19, 659, 15, 13, 1125, 314, 6514, 504, 533, 12307, 659, 15, 13, 1125, 28, 8034, 2843, 13, 1125, 13, 284, 61, 17, 314, 220, 11442, 13, 22, 61, 17, 314, 350, 13365, 533, 15, 13, 18, 73602, 17, 314, 12307, 2636, 533, 17, 9, 13365, 9, 15, 13, 18, 659, 15, 13, 3114, 314, 12307, 2636, 533, 8876, 13, 21, 659, 15, 13, 3114, 314, 8780, 8540, 13, 3796, 13, 85220, 25, 220, 8034, 2843, 13, 1125, 533, 8780, 8540, 13, 3796, 314, 220, 48267, 20, 13, 5462, 13, 6549, 38484, 656, 350, 17, 44, 8, 314, 220, 17, 9, 16840, 13, 21, 314, 31468, 13, 17, 13, 275, 314, 220, 48267, 20, 13, 5462, 820, 31468, 13, 17, 314, 1078, 220, 2270, 13, 23, 2896, 53, 350, 21910, 13306, 2896, 53, 4308, 741, 45438, 25, 220, 31468, 13, 17, 9, 1130, 314, 50016, 21, 11, 16132, 1932, 11, 813, 220, 48267, 20, 13, 22, 14, 31468, 13, 17, 28, 2270, 13, 23, 33956, 364, 5808, 129539, 2081, 121749, 5954, 314, 1617, 3609, 5954, 314, 18736, 314, 220, 2270, 13, 23, 2896, 53, 350, 21910, 4842, 2695, 741, 19308, 263, 3609, 5954, 314, 391, 533, 275, 314, 220, 16840, 13, 21, 533, 2270, 13, 23, 314, 13923, 13, 23, 2896, 53, 13, 13974, 2867, 4842, 382, 220, 11442, 13, 22, 11, 813, 1617, 121749, 5954, 314, 220, 13923, 13, 23, 533, 11442, 13, 22, 314, 19, 13, 16, 2896, 53, 364, 84787, 20666, 25, 2637, 263, 6574, 19, 13, 16, 2896, 53, 11, 129539, 2081, 6574, 2270, 13, 23, 2896, 53, 364, 12211, 540, 3880, 25, 415, 8, 220, 19, 13, 899, 2896, 53, 11, 220, 2270, 13, 23, 2896, 53, 15248, 13, 2632, 6052, 415, 364, 84787, 6011, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 415], "n_tokens": 707, "words": 244, "band_lo": 137.0, "band_hi": 548.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to interpret question: Pi(+) decays at rest into mu(+) + neutrino (presumably muon neutrino). Find kinetic energies of product particles: muon and neutrino? Probably find KE of mu+ and neutrino (which is massless). Given rest masses: pi+ 139.6 MeV, mu+ 105.7 MeV. So decay at rest: initial total energy = m_pi c^2 = 139.6 MeV. Total momentum zero. After decay: muon mass 105.7 MeV plus neutrino mass ~0 (ignore). Let muon energy = E_mu = sqrt(p^2 c^2 + m_mu^2 c^4). Neutrino energy = pc (since massless). Conservation of energy: E_mu + pc = 139.6. Conservation of momentum: muon momentum p_mu = p (opposite sign). So p is same magnitude.\n\nThus we solve: sqrt(p^2 + m_mu^2) + p = M_pi (units MeV/c^2 with c=1). Let m =105.7, M=139.6. Solve for p.\n\nLet E_mu = sqrt(p^2 + m^2). Then total = E_mu + p = M. Rearr: sqrt(p^2 + m^2) = M - p. Square both sides: p^2 + m^2 = M^2 -2 M p + p^2 => cancel p^2 => m^2 = M^2 -2 M p => solve p = (M^2 - m^2)/(2 M).\n\nYes that's known formula for two-body decay at rest with massless second product. Compute: M^2 = 139.6^2 = let's compute: 139.6^2 = (140-0.4)^2 = 19600 - 2*140*0.4 +0.16 =19600 -112 +0.16=19488.16. m^2 = 105.7^2 = (106 -0.3)^2 =11236 -2*106*0.3 +0.09 =11236 -63.6 +0.09 =11172.49. Difference: 19488.16 -11172.49 = 8315.67. Now divide by (2M) = 2*139.6 =279.2. p = 8315.67 /279.2 = about 29.8 MeV (since units MeV/c). Compute: 279.2*30 =8376, slightly high, so 8315.7/279.2=29.8 approx.\n\nSo neutrino kinetic energy = its total energy = pc = 29.8 MeV (since massless). Muon total energy = M - p = 139.6 -29.8 =109.8 MeV. Its rest mass is 105.7, so its kinetic energy = 109.8 -105.7 =4.1 MeV.\n\nThus KE: muon ~4.1 MeV, neutrino ~29.8 MeV.\n\nLook at options: D) 4.12 MeV, 29.8 MeV matches. So answer D.\n\nThus format: ANSWER: D", "response": "ANSWER: D", "answer": "D", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.31130149583214e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999926, "logp_correct": -7.414768541263711e-15, "letter_mass": 0.9999998807907321, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 1.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.30682108087976606, "cot_lp_min64": -0.6047373177871157, "frac_below_-5": 0.005763688760806916, "digit_lp_min": -5.62861967086792, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.005692461505532265, "n_cot_tokens": 694, "lp_end": -0.011463724076747894, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -2.3841855067985307e-07, "logp_nocot": -1.5544633376130772, "p_nocot": 0.2113027504565524, "uplift": 1.5544633376130699, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.57438, "B": 0.211303, "C": 0.003014, "D": 0.211303}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "rec4YVw9r9DC0DK6U", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Measuring stellar inclinations is fundamental in both stellar and exoplanetary research. However, it presents a significant challenge. Assuming that stellar inclinations follow an isotropic distribution, what would be the ratio of the number of stars with inclination angles in the range of 45 to 90 degrees to those with inclinations in the range of 0 to 45 degrees?\n\nA) ~ 1.4\nB) ~ 1.0\nC) ~ 2.4\nD) ~ 0.4\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Measuring stellar inclinations is fundamental in both stellar and exoplanetary research. However, it presents a significant challenge. Assuming that stellar inclinations follow an isotropic distribution, what would be the ratio of the number of stars with inclination angles in the range of 45 to 90 degrees to those with inclinations in the range of 0 to 45 degrees?\n\nA) ~ 1.4\nB) ~ 1.0\nC) ~ 2.4\nD) ~ 0.4\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "rec4YVw9r9DC0DK6U:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 18051, 328, 8663, 328, 13701, 483, 135766, 43448, 350, 72, 8, 306, 33269, 220, 2548, 316, 220, 2744, 18210, 326, 220, 15, 316, 220, 2548, 18210, 11, 49328, 103932, 71571, 12545, 13, 2214, 103932, 71571, 7526, 29546, 11, 12545, 328, 135766, 575, 350, 7140, 2870, 2543, 328, 21832, 326, 23769, 16300, 8, 853, 34933, 27591, 99864, 316, 2187, 575, 11, 395, 575, 2870, 220, 15, 326, 220, 2744, 6793, 350, 141027, 1606, 575, 869, 316, 220, 2744, 5192, 316, 90882, 741, 50557, 3149, 51811, 25, 34933, 777, 8785, 16538, 272, 45879, 314, 2187, 575, 1320, 272, 4106, 11, 21219, 1072, 51811, 26, 4335, 7526, 29546, 11, 34933, 27591, 328, 575, 382, 275, 3649, 8, 314, 2187, 575, 820, 350, 69966, 280, 62, 15, 42923, 1345, 14, 17, 92, 2187, 575, 1320, 8, 314, 2187, 575, 820, 220, 16, 314, 2187, 575, 11, 2236, 30089, 591, 220, 15, 316, 3478, 14, 17, 2187, 575, 1320, 314, 220, 16, 13, 2632, 34933, 484, 135766, 24384, 2870, 261, 326, 287, 382, 35353, 104, 62, 64, 61, 65, 2187, 575, 1320, 314, 533, 10732, 575, 176721, 64, 61, 65, 314, 8974, 261, 533, 8974, 287, 13, 2214, 3352, 220, 15, 316, 220, 2548, 148177, 34933, 314, 8974, 220, 15, 533, 8974, 2548, 314, 220, 16, 533, 143029, 17, 14, 17, 42308, 230, 220, 16, 533, 220, 15, 13, 36298, 16, 314, 220, 15, 13, 30907, 24, 13, 26714, 220, 2548, 316, 220, 2744, 148177, 34933, 314, 8974, 2548, 533, 8974, 2744, 314, 143029, 17, 14, 17, 533, 220, 15, 314, 220, 15, 13, 36298, 16, 13, 84705, 314, 220, 15, 13, 36298, 16, 820, 220, 15, 13, 30907, 24, 314, 220, 17, 13, 32006, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 19, 13, 2632, 6052, 363, 364, 84787, 4733, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 363], "n_tokens": 313, "words": 140, "band_lo": 59.0, "band_hi": 236.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need ratio of numbers of stars with inclination angles (i) in ranges 45 to 90 degrees and 0 to 45 degrees, assuming isotropic distribution. For isotropic random orientation, distribution of inclination i (angle between line of sight and rotation axis) has probability density proportional to sin i, for i between 0 and 90° (assuming only i up to 90 due to symmetry). Actually full sphere: probability per solid angle dΩ = sin i di dφ, uniform over sphere; given random orientation, probability density of i is p(i) = sin i / (integral_0^{π/2} sin i di) = sin i / 1 = sin i, because integral from 0 to π/2 sin i di = 1. So probability that inclination lies between a and b is ∫_a^b sin i di = -cos i |_a^b = cos a - cos b. For range 0 to 45°, probability = cos 0 - cos45 = 1 - √2/2 ≈ 1 - 0.7071 = 0.2929. Range 45 to 90°, probability = cos45 - cos90 = √2/2 - 0 = 0.7071. Ratio = 0.7071 / 0.2929 = 2.414 ≈ 2.4. So answer C.\n\nThus output: ANSWER: C", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -5.960450948805374e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999304, "logp_correct": -6.964683007832512e-14, "letter_mass": 0.9999948740269444, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.3864954623422086, "cot_lp_min64": -0.7417128364909749, "frac_below_-5": 0.006666666666666667, "digit_lp_min": -1.5020277500152588, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.02375033311545849, "n_cot_tokens": 300, "lp_end": -0.07984883338212967, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -1.1920928244535389e-07, "logp_nocot": -5.255250955340007, "p_nocot": 0.005220036131647427, "uplift": 5.255250955339938, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.994763, "B": 1.7e-05, "C": 0.00522, "D": 0.0}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
