20, 16, 14, 9534, 15, 42308, 230, 220, 16, 13, 36950, 5085, 68, 12, 19, 11, 220, 16, 14, 6718, 15, 314, 220, 16, 13, 19837, 5462, 68, 12, 19, 13, 85220, 25, 220, 16, 14, 9534, 15, 533, 220, 16, 14, 6718, 15, 314, 533, 15, 13, 1302, 34162, 40606, 20, 30, 24305, 23864, 220, 16, 14, 9534, 15, 533, 220, 16, 14, 6718, 15, 314, 350, 6718, 15, 533, 220, 9534, 15, 60504, 4689, 11, 1302, 11, 1302, 8, 314, 533, 1353, 15, 14, 4689, 11, 1302, 11, 1302, 314, 533, 17, 13, 35527, 68, 12, 20, 314, 533, 17, 13, 35527, 68, 12, 20, 13, 2632, 12626, 13, 7801, 533, 1353, 504, 425, 350, 46069, 8, 314, 659, 1353, 504, 425, 220, 17, 13, 35527, 68, 12, 20, 314, 220, 15, 13, 25706, 16, 13, 2632, 12332, 314, 2794, 7, 15, 13, 25706, 16, 8, 314, 220, 16, 13, 30713, 364, 84787, 18051, 21073, 656, 12332, 6574, 16, 13, 2092, 364, 51113, 5317, 363, 6574, 16, 13, 2092, 364, 84787, 6052, 363, 364, 4383, 13319, 538, 12088, 39943, 316, 220, 3234, 15, 658, 25, 1815, 12332, 314, 2794, 8087, 1353, 504, 14793, 16, 14, 3234, 15, 533, 220, 16, 14, 6718, 15, 915, 314, 2794, 8087, 1353, 504, 14793, 15, 13, 1302, 17, 533, 15, 13, 1302, 19341, 22, 25987, 533, 1353, 504, 9, 18, 13, 2546, 68, 12, 20, 314, 533, 15, 13, 15517, 871, 2794, 8087, 15, 13, 15517, 25987, 15, 13, 46860, 350, 613, 27550, 741, 4037, 20238, 3880, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 363, 364], "n_tokens": 1025, "words": 335, "band_lo": 170.25, "band_hi": 681.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to compute ratio of populations of neutral silicon atoms in two energy levels, ratio N2/N1 maybe? The ratio changes due to effective temperature change. Under LTE, Boltzmann distribution: n_i/n_j = (g_i/g_j) exp[-(E_i - E_j)/kT]. So ratio change due to T change. The transition corresponds to wavelength 14404 Å ~ 1.4404 microns = 1.4404e-6 m. Energy difference ΔE = hc/λ. Compute. h=6.626e-34 J s, c=3e8 m/s, λ=1.4404e-6 m => ΔE = (6.626e-34*3e8)/(1.4404e-6) = (1.9878e-25)/(1.4404e-6)?? Wait compute: 6.626e-34 * 3e8 = 1.9878e-25 J·m. Divide by 1.4404e-6 m = 1.9878e-25 /1.4404e-6 = 1.380e-19 J. Let's compute more precisely: 1.9878e-25 /1.4404e-6 = 1.3804e-19 J. Convert to eV: 1 eV = 1.602e-19 J, so ΔE ≈ 0.8615 eV.\n\nNow the ratio of populations of level 2 to level 1: N2/N1 = (g2/g1) exp(-ΔE/kT). Assuming g2/g1 maybe same? Not given. They ask factor change, maybe independent of g ratio because same for both T, so factor is exp(-ΔE/kT_plage)/exp(-ΔE/kT_no). So factor = exp[-ΔE/k (1/T_plage - 1/T_no)].\n\nWe need T_no = 6000 K? Actually effective temperature without plages is 6000K. With 30% plage, overall photospheric effective temperature changes by 1000 K. So new Teff = 6000 ± 1000? Which direction? Plages are hotter regions. The overall photospheric effective temperature likely increases? If 30% surface hotter, overall effective temperature may increase; but statement: overall photospheric effective temperature changes by 1000 K. Could be increase by 1000 K (i.e., to 7000 K). Let's assume increase.\n\nThus T1 = 6000 K, T2 = 7000 K.\n\nNow compute factor = exp(-ΔE/k (1/7000 - 1/6000)). Evaluate.\n\nk = 1.381e-23 J/K. ΔE = 1.3804e-19 J.\n\nCompute ΔE/k = 1.3804e-19 / 1.381e-23 = 10000? Let's compute: 1.3804e-19 /1.381e-23 = 1.3804/1.381 *10^( -19+23 ) = 0.9996 *10^4 = 9996 ≈ 1.0e4 K. Indeed ΔE/k ≈ 10000 K (makes sense because 0.86 eV corresponds to ~ 10000 K).\n\nSo factor = exp( - (ΔE/k)*(1/T2 - 1/T1) ) = exp( -10000*(1/7000 - 1/6000) ).\n\nCompute 1/7000 ≈ 1.42857e-4, 1/6000 = 1.66667e-4. Difference: 1/7000 - 1/6000 = -0.0000238095? Wait compute 1/7000 - 1/6000 = (6000 - 7000)/(42,000,000) = -1000/42,000,000 = -2.381e-5 = -2.381e-5. So negative. Then -10000 * (negative) = +10000 * 2.381e-5 = 0.2381. So factor = exp(0.2381) = 1.269.\n\nThus ratio increases by factor ~1.27.\n\nMatches option C ~1.27.\n\nThus answer C.\n\nCheck alternative if temperature decreased to 5000 K: then factor = exp(-10000*(1/5000 - 1/6000)) = exp(-10000*(0.0002 -0.0001667)= -10000*3.33e-5 = -0.333 => exp(-0.333)=0.717 (decrease). Not matching options.\n\nThus answer: C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -2.8967437174287625e-05, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999916, "logp_correct": -8.397046837474204e-15, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000084, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.31024053369756205, "cot_lp_min64": -0.7894054110787603, "frac_below_-5": 0.004940711462450593, "digit_lp_min": -6.626928329467773, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 1012, "lp_end": -0.1470276564359665, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -1.1920928244535389e-07, "logp_nocot": -6.257019697989601, "p_nocot": 0.0019169503827950736, "uplift": 6.257019697989593, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.773353, "B": 0.221569, "C": 0.001917, "D": 0.003161}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "rec9W28HgpEUeUN8k", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Calculate the amount of non-Gaussianity(nG) in the Schrödinger cat state using relative entropy measure. The state is defined as,\n|psi> =( cos(phi)|alpha> + sin(phi)|-alpha> )/ N;\nHere, alpha is the amplitude, phi is the phase and N is the normalisation constant.\nN = sqrt(1+ sin(2*phi)*exp(-2*alpha^2)).\nThe relative entropy measure is given as,\ndel_b = [trace(rho* ln(rho))-trace(tau* ln(tau))]\nwhere tau is the density matrix of a reference Gaussian state and rho is the density matrix of the above non-Gaussian state.\nCalculate the nG for phi =-pi /4 and alpha= 0.5.\n\nA) 0.25\nB) 2.48\nC) 1.38\nD) 0\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Calculate the amount of non-Gaussianity(nG) in the Schrödinger cat state using relative entropy measure. The state is defined as,\n|psi> =( cos(phi)|alpha> + sin(phi)|-alpha> )/ N;\nHere, alpha is the amplitude, phi is the phase and N is the normalisation constant.\nN = sqrt(1+ sin(2*phi)*exp(-2*alpha^2)).\nThe relative entropy measure is given as,\ndel_b = [trace(rho* ln(rho))-trace(tau* ln(tau))]\nwhere tau is the density matrix of a reference Gaussian state and rho is the density matrix of the above non-Gaussian state.\nCalculate the nG for phi =-pi /4 and alpha= 0.5.\n\nA) 0.25\nB) 2.48\nC) 1.38\nD) 0\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "rec9W28HgpEUeUN8k:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 23864, 2893, 13112, 64, 28810, 536, 4493, 15001, 104037, 25, 336, 4729, 1555, 12439, 84841, 25987, 1410, 4729, 1555, 68859, 54241, 14080, 1410, 4729, 1555, 68859, 15586, 741, 50557, 4335, 18800, 1535, 314, 1514, 4729, 1555, 68859, 54241, 14080, 1410, 2025, 753, 68859, 15586, 741, 24305, 1023, 11955, 15586, 3