17, 32803, 26, 6821, 1934, 1577, 163125, 581, 679, 1001, 306, 297, 28, 18, 26, 2023, 3006, 3099, 1354, 741, 41021, 29671, 364, 7650, 31061, 395, 220, 19, 30285, 483, 2999, 220, 17, 777, 3211, 364, 42087, 25, 3609, 5954, 1424, 1055, 36, 19957, 364, 2167, 679, 4149, 98537, 350, 77, 8374, 869, 316, 10112, 220, 19, 741, 41021, 119647, 1562, 150243, 364, 2167, 1309, 220, 19, 30285, 26, 2454, 3211, 575, 665, 679, 220, 15, 11, 16, 11, 17, 95974, 13, 34138, 95974, 314, 19, 13, 45438, 3609, 5954, 4215, 297, 10853, 61, 17, 425, 457, 425, 95974, 10853, 364, 2167, 4279, 679, 7740, 25, 350, 17, 11, 17, 8, 10915, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 17, 871, 220, 702, 36, 364, 7127, 15209, 25, 350, 17, 11, 16, 11, 16, 8, 95974, 25, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 16, 871, 220, 1055, 36, 364, 10620, 3099, 15209, 6960, 350, 17, 11, 15, 11, 17, 8, 10112, 30, 21926, 95974, 25, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 15, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 17, 871, 5954, 314, 220, 17, 9, 16, 36, 659, 220, 17, 9, 24, 36, 314, 220, 17, 36, 10, 1157, 36, 314, 455, 36, 13, 3072, 1354, 1340, 413, 6931, 364, 49377, 350, 16, 11, 17, 11, 16, 3127, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 16, 871, 5954, 314, 16, 9, 16, 36, 10, 17, 9, 19, 36, 10, 16, 9, 24, 36, 314, 16, 10, 23, 10, 24, 28, 1157, 36, 364, 49377, 350, 16, 11, 16, 11, 17, 3127, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 17, 871, 5954, 314, 16, 10, 19, 10, 1157, 28, 1860, 36, 364, 49377, 350, 17, 11, 15, 11, 16, 11, 16, 3127, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 19, 4138, 16, 871, 5954, 314, 17, 9, 16, 10, 24, 10, 1125, 28, 17, 10, 1161, 28, 2092, 36, 364, 49377, 350, 17, 11, 16, 11, 15, 11, 16, 3127, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 19, 4138, 16, 871, 220, 17, 10, 19, 10, 1125, 28, 1709, 36, 364, 49377, 350, 15, 11, 17, 11, 17, 3127, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 17, 871, 220, 17, 9, 19, 10, 17, 9, 24, 28, 23, 10, 1157, 28, 2109, 36, 364, 49377, 350, 17, 11, 15, 11, 15, 11, 17, 3127, 297, 28, 16, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 19, 4138, 17, 871, 220, 17, 10, 1398, 28, 3020, 36, 364, 7943, 581, 1309, 42173, 1424, 1055, 36, 13, 32417, 46716, 25, 220, 1157, 36, 591, 350, 16, 11, 17, 11, 16, 8, 382, 17098, 13, 8820, 220, 455, 36, 591, 350, 17, 11, 15, 11, 17, 741, 220, 1157, 36, 382, 6931, 1572, 220, 455, 36, 13, 2763, 1354, 1062, 12282, 483, 3609, 5954, 220, 1125, 36, 30, 41021, 2075, 350, 17, 11, 17, 11, 15, 20707, 21926, 7740, 13, 350, 17, 11, 16, 11, 15, 11, 16, 8, 10175, 220, 1709, 36, 364, 4827, 1078, 350, 16, 11, 18, 11, 15, 20707, 4037, 9279, 2236, 2999, 220, 17, 777, 3211, 364, 26070, 581, 679, 350, 15, 11, 17, 11, 16, 11, 16, 3127, 297, 28, 17, 4138, 17, 11, 297, 28, 18, 4138, 16, 11, 297, 28, 19, 4138, 16, 871, 220, 23, 10, 24, 10, 1125, 28, 2546, 36, 364, 84787, 3099, 15209, 7890, 220, 1157, 36, 364, 84787, 70824, 25, 7740, 220, 702, 36, 11, 1577, 15209, 220, 1055, 36, 11, 3099, 15209, 220, 1157, 36, 364, 8093, 355, 25, 220, 702, 36, 11, 220, 1055, 36, 11, 220, 1157, 36, 15248, 364, 84787, 6052, 355, 364, 4383, 3880, 25, 355, 8, 220, 702, 36, 11, 220, 1055, 36, 11, 220, 1157, 36, 13, 11377, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 355, 13], "n_tokens": 1244, "words": 539, "band_lo": 272.25, "band_hi": 1089.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to determine energies of many-fermion system (identical spin-1/2 particles) in infinite well. Since spin-1/2 fermions, each spatial level can hold up to 2 particles (due to spin degeneracy). Total 4 identical fermions. Need ground state configuration: Fill lowest single-particle levels following Pauli principle.\n\nSingle-particle energies: E_n = n^2 * E (where E = π^2 ħ^2 /2mL^2). So n=1: 1E, n=2:4E, n=3:9E, n=4:16E,...\n\nEach level can hold 2 fermions (spin up & down). With 4 particles, ground state: fill n=1 with 2 particles (energy 1E each), n=2 with 2 particles (energy 4E each). Total energy = 2*1E + 2*4E = 2E + 8E = 10E.\n\nThat's ground state total energy: 10E. Good.\n\nNow first excited state: We need to consider the lowest possible total energy higher than ground where one particle is promoted to next available level? Usually excitations correspond to many-body states with one particle moved to next higher single-particle level. For fermions with spin degeneracy.\n\nWe have ground config: (n=1,2 each with spin up/down) occupancy: (1,1,2,2) maybe.\n\nFirst excited many-body state: promote one particle from highest occupied level (n=2) to next unoccupied level (n=3). So we will have: n=1 holds 2 particles; n=2 holds 1 particle; n=3 holds 1 particle. Energy: 2*1E + 1*4E + 1*9E = 2E + 4E + 9E = 15E.\n\nCheck if there is any other configuration with lower energy? Could promote one from n=1 to n=3, leaving n=2 with 2? That gives energies: n=1 one particle (1E), n=2 two particles (8E), n=3 one particle (9E) total = 1+8+9=18E >15E. So first excited is 15E.\n\nSecond excited: Next many-body level above: we can promote another particle to higher level, need configuration giving next higher total energy after 15E.\n\nPossibilities: Starting from ground, we could promote two particles: maybe both from n=2 to n=3 (but only one can go because n=3 can hold 2 spins; currently after first excitation we have one in n=3; could put second there). Let's enumerate.\n\nConfiguration possibilities for 4 particles with max 2 per level.\n\nGoal: total energy >15E minimal.\n\nWe have possible occupations (n levels up to maybe 4). Let's systematically list combos.\n\nWe need 4 particles; each level i can have 0,1,2 occupancy. Sum occupancy =4. Compute total energy sum n_i^2 * E * occupancy_i.\n\nWe already have ground: (2,2) meaning n=1 occ2, n=2 occ2 => 10E.\n\nFirst excited: (2,1,1) occupancy: n=1 occ2, n=2 occ1, n=3 occ1 => 15E.\n\nNow second excited likely (2,0,2) maybe? That's occupancy: n=1 occ2, n=2 occ0, n=3 occ2 => energy = 2*1E + 2*9E = 2E+18E =20E. But there may be lower.\n\nConsider (1,2,1): n=1 occ1, n=2 occ2, n=3 occ1 => energy =1*1E+2*4E+1*9E =1+8+9=18E.\n\nConsider (1,1,2): n=1 occ1, n=2 occ1, n=3 occ2 => energy =1+4+18=23E.\n\nConsider (2,0,1,1): n=1 occ2, n=3 occ1, n=4 occ1 => energy =2*1+9+16=2+25=27E.\n\nConsider (2,1,0,1): n=1 occ2, n=2 occ1, n=4 occ1 => 2+4+16=22E.\n\nConsider (0,2,2): n=2 occ2, n=3 occ2 => 2*4+2*9=8+18=26E.\n\nConsider (2,0,0,2): n=1 occ2, n=4 occ2 => 2+32=34E.\n\nBut we need smallest >15E. Among computed: 18E from (1,2,1) is candidate. Also 20E from (2,0,2). 18E is lower than 20E. Is there any configuration with total energy 16E? Let's try (2,2,0)? That's ground. (2,1,0,1) gave 22E.\n\nWhat about (1,3,0)? Not allowed because max 2 per level.\n\nCould we have (0,2,1,1): n=2 occ2, n=3 occ1, n=4 occ1 => 8+9+16=33E.\n\nThus second excited seems 18E.\n\nThus energies: ground 10E, first excited 15E, second excited 18E.\n\nOption A: 10E, 15E, 18E matches.\n\nThus answer A.\n\nCheck options: A) 10E, 15E, 18E. Yes.\n\nThus answer: A.", "response": "ANSWER: A", "answer": "A", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.3351351299206726e-05, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999257, "logp_correct": -7.423843481960198e-14, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000744, "p_letters": {"A": 1.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.4019751946200242, "cot_lp_min64": -1.0667896948874542, "frac_below_-5": 0.007311129163281885, "digit_lp_min": -3.2525038719177246, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.03523493558168411, "n_cot_tokens": 1231, "lp_end": -8.821448318485636e-06, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -5.504602767283206, "p_nocot": 0.004068004204331501, "uplift": 5.5046027672831315, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.004068, "B": 0.000295, "C": 0.00023, "D": 0.995408}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
