069, 1161, 9, 15, 13, 27369, 19, 314, 350, 858, 13, 1161, 68, 12, 18, 44406, 1055, 13, 19, 68, 12, 18, 8, 314, 350, 858, 13, 1161, 9, 1055, 13, 19, 111066, 12, 21, 314, 220, 31788, 13, 2467, 319, 12, 21, 314, 220, 17, 13, 49816, 20, 68, 12, 19, 13, 2632, 149054, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 6768, 68, 12, 19, 425, 220, 16, 68, 3020, 30, 24305, 581, 2928, 679, 12332, 220, 16, 68, 3020, 30, 50557, 581, 1458, 220, 20, 68, 3020, 11, 57388, 656, 220, 15, 13, 11822, 8017, 314, 220, 15, 13, 32069, 1161, 68, 3020, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36831, 68, 2546, 30, 41021, 23864, 5983, 7480, 1402, 45, 15, 28, 20, 68, 3020, 364, 113552, 656, 17667, 16, 727, 350, 15, 13, 11822, 8017, 3127, 220, 20, 68, 3020, 425, 220, 15, 13, 11822, 8017, 314, 220, 20, 425, 15, 13, 11822, 8017, 319, 3020, 314, 220, 15, 13, 32069, 1161, 319, 3020, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36831, 68, 1398, 30, 24305, 220, 15, 13, 32069, 1161, 33839, 702, 61, 3020, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36831, 12378, 702, 61, 1398, 350, 21910, 12847, 1920, 12528, 741, 41351, 220, 15, 13, 32069, 1161, 425, 702, 61, 3020, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36831, 12378, 702, 61, 1398, 13, 9700, 364, 10620, 57388, 656, 319, 183239, 1727, 17, 260, 102838, 15, 13, 27369, 19, 871, 220, 16, 13, 36831, 68, 1398, 425, 220, 15, 13, 27369, 19, 314, 350, 16, 13, 36831, 9, 15, 13, 27369, 19, 8, 319, 1398, 314, 220, 15, 13, 42363, 43787, 319, 1398, 314, 220, 17, 13, 50710, 20, 68, 1130, 364, 84787, 149054, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 6768, 68, 1130, 364, 10620, 38484, 656, 101279, 220, 15, 13, 6106, 3152, 871, 478, 22477, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 6768, 68, 1130, 820, 220, 15, 13, 6106, 3152, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 19354, 68, 2911, 30, 41021, 23864, 25, 220, 17, 13, 6768, 820, 15, 13, 6106, 3152, 42308, 230, 220, 1494, 13, 3152, 13, 2632, 220, 17, 13, 6768, 68, 1130, 820, 15, 13, 6106, 3152, 314, 220, 1494, 13, 3152, 68, 1130, 314, 220, 17, 13, 36075, 68, 2911, 364, 84787, 478, 22477, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 20, 12378, 702, 61, 2911, 364, 4861, 328, 49895, 220, 702, 61, 2911, 871, 7158, 415, 364, 4383, 538, 173776, 25, 17667, 16, 727, 382, 1606, 997, 26, 581, 4279, 83982, 364, 84787, 6052, 415, 364, 4383, 538, 1062, 1273, 29298, 591, 865, 484, 1504, 12790, 11965, 326, 1885, 19630, 30, 5339, 20690, 9474, 484, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 415, 364], "n_tokens": 1911, "words": 653, "band_lo": 218.75, "band_hi": 875.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to compute number of Y nuclei after 1 hour given decay chain with branching from X to Y via alpha decay, and X also decays by beta to something else (not Y). Also Y decays further by alpha to P. So we have a system:\n\nLet N_X(t), N_Y(t), N_P(t). Initial: N_X0 = 5e34, N_Y0 = 0.\n\nDecays:\nX -> Y with rate λ1α = 0.00385 s^-1.\nX -> other (β) with rate λ1β = 0.11786 s^-1. This removes X but not produce Y.\n\nThus total decay constant for X: λ_X = λ1α + λ1β = 0.00385 + 0.11786 = 0.12171 s^-1.\n\nY decays to P with λ2 = 0.00116 s^-1. No other losses.\n\nGoal: N_Y after t = 1 hour = 3600 s.\n\nWe have differential equations:\n\ndN_X/dt = - λ_X N_X\n\n=> N_X(t) = N_X0 exp(-λ_X t).\n\ndN_Y/dt = λ1α N_X - λ2 N_Y\n\n=> This is a classic production-decay equation. Solution: N_Y(t) = ∫_0^t λ1α N_X(s) e^{-λ2 (t-s)} ds.\n\nPlug N_X(s) = N_X0 e^{-λ_X s}.\n\n=> N_Y(t) = λ1α N_X0 ∫_0^t e^{-λ_X s} e^{-λ2 (t-s)} ds = λ1α N_X0 e^{-λ2 t} ∫_0^t e^{-(λ_X - λ2) s} ds.\n\nCompute integral: ∫_0^t e^{-(λ_X - λ2)s} ds = [1 - e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t}] / (λ_X - λ2), provided λ_X ≠ λ2.\n\nThus N_Y(t) = λ1α N_X0 e^{-λ2 t} * (1 - e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t}) / (λ_X - λ2).\n\nAlternatively can also write as: N_Y = (λ1α N_X0 / (λ_X - λ2)) (e^{-λ2 t} - e^{-λ_X t}).\n\nCheck: Actually typical solution for parent-daughter where parent decays with λ_p, daughter decays with λ_d, and production fraction f of parent leads to daughter: N_d = (f λ_p N0)/(λ_d - λ_p) (e^{-λ_p t} - e^{-λ_d t}). Wait sign reversed. Let's re-derive: dN_d/dt = f λ_p N_p - λ_d N_d. With N_p = N0 e^{-λ_p t}. Solve with integrating factor e^{λ_d t}: d(N_d e^{λ_d t})/dt = f λ_p N0 e^{-(λ_p - λ_d) t}. Integrate: N_d e^{λ_d t} = f λ_p N0 ∫_0^t e^{-(λ_p - λ_d) s} ds = f λ_p N0 (1 - e^{-(λ_p - λ_d) t})/(λ_p - λ_d). So N_d = f λ_p N0 e^{-λ_d t} (1 - e^{-(λ_p - λ_d) t})/(λ_p - λ_d). That's same as earlier.\n\nAlternatively N_d = (f λ_p N0)/(λ_d - λ_p) (e^{-λ_p t} - e^{-λ_d t}) (since sign change). Indeed multiply numerator and denominator: (f λ_p N0)/(λ_d - λ_p) (e^{-λ_p t} - e^{-λ_d t}) . Let's verify: Start with earlier expression: λ1α N0 e^{-λ2 t} (1 - e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t})/(λ_X - λ2). Multiply numerator and denominator by -1 -> λ1α N0 e^{-λ2 t}(e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t} -1)/(λ2 - λ_X). But e^{-λ2 t} e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t}= e^{-λ_X t}. So it becomes λ1α N0 (e^{-λ_X t} - e^{-λ2 t})/(λ2 - λ_X). That's same.\n\nThus compute N_Y after 3600 s.\n\nFirst compute λ_X = 0.12171 s^-1. λ2 = 0.00116 s^-1. The difference λ_X - λ2 = 0.12055 s^-1 approx.\n\nCompute exponentials:\n\ne^{-λ_X t} = e^{-0.12171 * 3600}.\n\n0.12171 * 3600 = 438.156. e^{-438} is effectively zero (~10^{-190}). So N_X after 1 hour basically 0.\n\ne^{-λ2 t} = e^{-0.00116 * 3600} = e^{-4.176} ≈ 0.0154 (since e^{-4}=0.0183; e^{-0.176}=0.839; product ≈0.0154). So decayed significantly but not completely.\n\nTherefore N_Y(t) ≈ (λ1α N0)/(λ_X - λ2) (e^{-λ_X t} - e^{-λ2 t})/(?) Wait using formula N_Y = (λ1α N0)/(λ_X - λ2) (e^{-λ2 t} - e^{-λ_X t}) ?\n\nLet's use N_Y = λ1α N0 e^{-λ2 t} (1 - e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t})/(λ_X - λ2).\n\nSince e^{-(λ_X - λ2) t} = e^{-0.12055*3600} = e^{-433.98} ≈ 0. So 1 - ~0 = 1.\n\nThus N_Y ≈ λ1α N0 e^{-λ2 t} / (λ_X - λ2).\n\nPlug numbers: λ1α = 0.00385 s^-1. N0 = 5e34. e^{-λ2 t}=0.0154. denominator = 0.12055 s^-1.\n\nCompute numerator: λ1α * N0 * e^{-λ2 t} = 0.00385 * 5e34 * 0.0154.\n\nFirst 0.00385 * 5 = 0.01925. Times 0.0154 = 0.01925*0.0154 ≈ 0.000296 (since 0.02*0.015=0.0003). Let's compute accurately: 0.01925*0.0154 = (19.25e-3)*(15.4e-3) = (19.25*15.4)e-6 = 296.35 e-6 = 2.9635e-4. So numerator ≈ 2.96e-4 * 1e34? Wait we still have factor 1e34? Actually we had 5e34, multiply by 0.00385 = 0.01925e34 = 1.925e33? Let's compute stepwise:\n\nN0=5e34.\n\nMultiply by λ1α (0.00385): 5e34 * 0.00385 = 5 *0.00385 e34 = 0.01925 e34 = 1.925e32? Wait 0.01925 ×10^34 = 1.925×10^32 (since shift two orders). Indeed 0.01925 *10^34 = 1.925×10^32. Good.\n\nNow multiply by e^{-λ2 t}=0.0154 => 1.925e32 * 0.0154 = (1.925*0.0154) e32 = 0.029645 e32 = 2.9645e30.\n\nThus numerator ≈ 2.96e30.\n\nNow divide by denominator 0.12055 => N_Y ≈ 2.96e30 / 0.12055 ≈ 2.456e31? Let's compute: 2.96 /0.12055 ≈ 24.55. So 2.96e30 /0.12055 = 24.55e30 = 2.455e31.\n\nThus N_Y ≈ 2.5×10^31.\n\nOrder of magnitude 10^31 => choice D.\n\nCheck if branching: λ1α is only part; we already accounted.\n\nThus answer D.\n\nCheck if any other contributions from Y that were produced earlier and decayed? Our formula considered that.\n\nThus answer: D.", "response": "ANSWER: D", "answer": "D", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -9.775115351828845e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999949, "logp_correct": -5.1437826433240244e-15, "letter_mass": 0.9999998807907298, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 1.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.24844167869584574, "cot_lp_min64": -0.9430462808798108, "frac_below_-5": 0.005795574288724974, "digit_lp_min": -2.578890800476074, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 1898, "lp_end": -0.0455952063202858, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -3.576278118089249e-07, "logp_nocot": -4.051619944742248, "p_nocot": 0.01739417420304019, "uplift": 4.051619944742242, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.739619, "B": 0.077955, "C": 0.165031, "D": 0.017394}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recKm6LNWykGapmCr", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: If a charge q is placed d distance away from the center of a grounded conducting sphere of radius R. Calculate the net potential energy of this system.\n\nA) U=- (1/2) *kq^2 R/(d^2 -R^2)\nB) U=- kq^2 d/(d^2 -R^2)\nC) U=-(1/2) kq^2 R^2/(d^2 -R^2)\nD) U=- (1/2) kq^2 d/(d^2 +R^2)\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: If a charge q is placed d distance away from the center of a grounded conducting sphere of radius R. Calculate the net potential energy of this system.\n\nA) U=- (1/2) *kq^2 R/(d^2 -R^2)\nB) U=- kq^2 d/(d^2 -R^2)\nC) U=-(1/2) kq^2 R^2/(d^2 -R^2)\nD) U=- (1/2) kq^2 d/(d^2 +R^2)\n", "true_answer": "A", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recKm6LNWykGapmCr:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 2776, 6451, 5954, 328, 8363, 5862, 77618, 47204, 51811, 2360, 2595, 328, 7493, 13, 2214, 77618, 51811, 21090, 460, 11, 2438, 8363, 2335, 540, 9324, 272, 591, 6170, 350, 141623, 51811, 11, 272, 29, 49, 741, 7979, 8363, 2335, 6, 314, 533, 350, 49, 6662, 8, 2335, 12989, 540, 9324, 460, 61, 17, 6662, 591, 6170, 4251, 2543, 350, 79475, 51811, 741, 74397, 5954, 328, 2420, 314, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 2335, 425, 631, 197294, 5089, 10607, 540, 5100, 328, 1374, 8363, 30, 50557, 5954, 328, 12282, 314, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 2335, 631, 20261, 41892, 30, 2214, 2438, 8363, 326, 57797, 14843, 11, 5954, 382, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 2335, 631, 8254, 19384, 5192, 316, 57797, 14843, 350, 3365, 741, 4569, 29702, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 372, 2335, 2335, 6, 820, 350, 40614, 2870, 2335, 326, 2335, 3426, 53583, 2870, 1374, 2335, 350, 266, 9324, 272, 8, 326, 3621, 540, 428, 6, 314, 460, 61, 17, 6662, 591, 6170, 11, 402, 2684, 2543, 11, 813, 39612, 314, 272, 533, 460, 61, 17, 6662, 314, 350, 67, 61, 17, 533, 460, 61, 17, 11876, 67, 364, 84787, 601, 314, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 372, 2335, 2335, 6, 820, 350, 67, 533, 460, 61, 17, 6662, 8, 314, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 372, 2335, 21382, 350, 49, 6662, 8, 2335, 8, 820, 3536, 67, 61, 17, 533, 460, 61, 17, 11876, 67, 8, 314, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 372, 21382, 460, 2335, 61, 17, 820, 272, 8, 425, 350, 67, 820, 350, 67, 61, 17, 533, 460, 61, 17, 915, 314, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 372, 21382, 460, 2335, 61, 17, 8, 820, 350, 67, 61, 17, 533, 460, 61, 17, 741, 2632, 601, 314, 533, 350, 16, 14, 17, 8, 372, 2335, 61, 17, 460, 820, 350, 67, 61, 17, 533, 460, 61, 17, 741, 21926, 5317, 355, 364, 84787, 6052, 355, 13], "n_tokens": 336, "words": 165, "band_lo": 107.5, "band_hi": 430.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need net potential energy of charge near grounded conducting sphere using method of images. For grounded sphere radius R, point charge q at distance d from center (outside sphere, d>R). Image charge q' = - (R/d) q placed at distance R^2/d from center along line (inside sphere). Potential energy of system = (1/2) q * V_due_to_image at location of real charge? Actually energy of configuration = (1/2) q V_induced? For point charge and induced charges, energy is (1/2) q V_at_q due to induced charges (image). That equals (1/2) k q q' / (distance between q and q'). Distance between real q (at distance d) and image at r' = R^2/d from center, on same line, so separation = d - R^2/d = (d^2 - R^2)/d.\n\nThus U = (1/2) k q q' / (d - R^2/d) = (1/2) k q (- (R/d) q) / ((d^2 - R^2)/d) = (1/2) k (- R q^2 / d) * (d / (d^2 - R^2)) = (1/2) k (- R q^2) / (d^2 - R^2). So U = - (1/2) k q^2 R / (d^2 - R^2). That's option A.\n\nThus answer A.", "response": "ANSWER: A", "answer": "A", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -7.390948667307384e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999992688, "logp_correct": -7.311628501258768e-13, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000007312, "p_letters": {"A": 1.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.