, 265, 314, 350, 76, 2170, 659, 284, 62, 1345, 73602, 17, 13, 116151, 395, 457, 1359, 4335, 4278, 13, 3072, 1023, 3810, 135911, 24313, 483, 4335, 120589, 29274, 100122, 3492, 6207, 11, 889, 581, 665, 57364, 17722, 395, 4278, 4335, 457, 1359, 30, 3072, 581, 4128, 679, 457, 1359, 364, 58369, 23864, 24313, 120589, 5954, 395, 19271, 135911, 5954, 328, 2569, 372, 51, 30, 7649, 135911, 5954, 4278, 314, 372, 51, 13, 14166, 353, 28, 16, 658, 11, 813, 4278, 42308, 230, 372, 3201, 353, 314, 220, 23, 13, 40657, 68, 12, 20, 319, 53, 13, 7801, 17722, 395, 457, 1359, 2360, 42006, 25, 350, 76, 2170, 659, 284, 62, 1345, 73602, 17, 314, 284, 1359, 61, 17, 659, 220, 19, 457, 1359, 4278, 13, 457, 1359, 314, 43900, 76, 2170, 659, 284, 62, 1345, 73602, 17, 533, 284, 1359, 61, 17, 60, 820, 350, 19, 4278, 741, 45438, 57556, 306, 319, 53, 25, 284, 1359, 314, 220, 47050, 13, 18, 2896, 53, 314, 220, 24, 13, 35067, 68, 23, 319, 53, 13, 284, 2170, 314, 220, 49943, 13, 21, 2896, 53, 314, 220, 24, 13, 38517, 68, 23, 319, 53, 13, 284, 62, 1345, 314, 220, 16840, 13, 21, 2896, 53, 314, 220, 16, 13, 38517, 68, 23, 319, 53, 364, 17434, 25, 284, 2170, 659, 284, 62, 1345, 314, 220, 24, 13, 38517, 68, 23, 659, 220, 16, 13, 38517, 68, 23, 314, 220, 16, 13, 49420, 17, 68, 24, 319, 53, 13, 22980, 25, 350, 16, 13, 49420, 17, 68, 24, 73602, 17, 42308, 230, 220, 16, 13, 18395, 22, 68, 1157, 319, 53, 61, 17, 350, 21910, 350, 16, 13, 3062, 68, 24, 73602, 17, 314, 220, 16, 13, 19341, 19, 68, 1157, 741, 284, 1359, 61, 17, 314, 350, 24, 13, 35067, 68, 23, 73602, 17, 42308, 230, 220, 23, 13, 42181, 68, 1422, 319, 53, 61, 17, 350, 21910, 220, 24, 13, 3150, 68, 23, 61, 17, 314, 220, 23, 13, 2241, 68, 1422, 741, 85220, 26143, 314, 220, 16, 13, 18395, 22, 68, 1157, 533, 220, 23, 13, 42181, 68, 1422, 314, 220, 17, 13, 48517, 68, 1422, 319, 53, 61, 17, 364, 10620, 38484, 656, 350, 19, 4278, 8, 1919, 4278, 28, 23, 13, 40657, 68, 12, 20, 319, 53, 13, 220, 19, 891, 314, 220, 18, 13, 39596, 68, 12, 19, 319, 53, 13, 2632, 457, 1359, 314, 220, 17, 13, 48517, 68, 1422, 820, 220, 18, 13, 39596, 68, 12, 19, 314, 220, 23, 13, 1494, 68, 455, 319, 53, 350, 76945, 741, 41021, 23864, 25, 220, 17, 13, 48517, 68, 1422, 820, 220, 18, 13, 39596, 68, 12, 19, 314, 220, 17, 13, 48517, 68, 1422, 820, 220, 18, 13, 39596, 68, 12, 19, 314, 220, 17, 13, 48517, 68, 1422, 425, 350, 16, 820, 220, 18, 13, 39596, 68, 12, 19, 8, 314, 220, 17, 13, 48517, 68, 1422, 425, 350, 17, 13, 9752, 68, 18, 8, 33956, 314, 220, 23, 13, 26975, 68, 455, 319, 53, 13, 11377, 15248, 5317, 418, 220, 23, 13, 1494, 33839, 220, 702, 61, 455, 319, 53, 364, 84787, 6052, 382, 418, 13, 2632, 1023, 22476, 7201, 290, 120589, 5954, 24313, 11, 889, 4335, 1023, 3810, 135911, 24313, 10112, 38441, 26, 889, 6052, 15248, 418, 364, 84787, 4733, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 418], "n_tokens": 1184, "words": 588, "band_lo": 364.5, "band_hi": 1458.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to find threshold photon energy required for reaction p + γ → n + π^+. Proton ultra-relativistic; photon from CMB at 1 K (but we need photon energy threshold). Actually problem asks: \"Find the energy threshold of the photon in ev which is needed for the production of neutron and pion, when the temperature of the background radiation drops to 1 Kelvin.\" So we need photon energy threshold given CMB temperature 1 K? Wait CMB temperature is 2.7 K normally; but they ask when T=1 K perhaps later. Photon energy distribution: typical photon energy ~ kT. But threshold means the minimum photon energy in lab frame required to produce the reaction with a proton of high energy? Usually we fix proton energy (ultra-high) and find threshold photon energy. However they say \"ultra high energy proton coming from deep space\". Not given its energy. But they give hint that proton is ultra relativistic, momentum equals energy (c=1). At threshold final particles are at rest in center-of-mass? Actually in lab (proton moving, photon head-on). At threshold, the final particles are produced with minimal kinetic energy in CM frame; in lab they move together? The condition: In CM frame, final particles at rest (i.e., total momentum zero). In lab, proton has high energy Ep, photon has energy ε. Need to find ε threshold given Ep unknown? Usually you solve for minimal proton energy for given photon energy, like Greisen-Zatsepin-Kuzmin (GZK) cutoff: p + γ_CMB → Δ+ → n + π+. We compute proton threshold energy given average photon energy (kT). But here they ask photon threshold energy given proton ultra-relativistic. However photon energy is ~kT = ~ 8.617e-5 eV/K * 1 K = 8.617e-5 eV. That's tiny, far less than thresholds which are ~10^20 eV for proton. So perhaps they ask what proton energy required for a 1K photon to cause reaction. But options are 10^20 eV scales, which correspond to proton energy threshold. Indeed GZK predicts proton threshold ~5×10^19 eV for CMB photons (~6×10^-4 eV). So options around 10^20 eV. So likely they ask proton energy threshold, not photon. However wording says \"energy threshold of the photon in ev\". Maybe mis-stated, they want energy (or momentum) of proton? Let's compute.\n\nStandard calculation: In lab frame where photon of energy ε collides head-on with proton of energy E_p (ultra-relativistic), the invariant s = m_p^2 + 2 E_p ε (1 - cosθ). For head-on, θ = π → (1 - cosθ) = 2. Actually 1 - cosπ = 2. So s = m_p^2 + 4 E_p ε. At threshold, s = (m_n + m_π)^2. Solve for E_p given ε. But they ask photon threshold with given proton ultra-relativistic, but we can invert solve for ε given E_p? But we don't have E_p.\n\nLet's compute threshold proton energy for typical photon energy of order kT? Use photon energy ε = kT. Take T=1 K, so ε ≈ k_B T = 8.617e-5 eV. Then solve for E_p using equation: (m_n + m_π)^2 = m_p^2 + 4 E_p ε. E_p = [(m_n + m_π)^2 - m_p^2] / (4 ε). Compute masses in eV: m_p = 938.3 MeV = 9.383e8 eV. m_n = 939.6 MeV = 9.396e8 eV. m_π = 139.6 MeV = 1.396e8 eV.\n\nSum: m_n + m_π = 9.396e8 + 1.396e8 = 1.0792e9 eV. Square: (1.0792e9)^2 ≈ 1.1647e18 eV^2 (since (1.08e9)^2 = 1.1664e18). m_p^2 = (9.383e8)^2 ≈ 8.806e17 eV^2 (since 9.38e8^2 = 8.80e17). Difference Δ = 1.1647e18 - 8.806e17 = 2.841e17 eV^2.\n\nNow divide by (4 ε) where ε=8.617e-5 eV. 4ε = 3.447e-4 eV. So E_p = 2.841e17 / 3.447e-4 = 8.24e20 eV (approx). Let's compute: 2.841e17 / 3.447e-4 = 2.841e17 / 3.447e-4 = 2.841e17 * (1 / 3.447e-4) = 2.841e17 * (2.900e3) approx = 8.239e20 eV. Yes matches option B 8.24 × 10^20 eV.\n\nThus answer is B. So they indeed wanted the proton energy threshold, but given they ask photon threshold maybe confusion; but answer matches B.\n\nThus output: ANSWER: B", "response": "ANSWER: B", "answer": "B", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -7.152555951961403e-07, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999802, "logp_correct": -1.9705645958983638e-14, "letter_mass": 0.9999997615814974, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.5156650401119699, "cot_lp_min64": -1.2813815729007842, "frac_below_-5": 0.013663535439795047, "digit_lp_min": -2.1863839626312256, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 1171, "lp_end": -0.01467200182378292, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -3.576278118089249e-07, "logp_nocot": -2.8125979807102044, "p_nocot": 0.060048783984556056, "uplift": 2.812597980710185, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.939321, "B": 0.060049, "C": 0.000315, "D": 0.000315}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recLslg5RfvRfUHAx", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Consider a linear harmonic oscillator and let, Ψ0 and Ψ 1 be its real, normalized ground and first excited state energy eigenfunctions respectively.\nLet Ψ = AΨ0 + BΨ1 with A and B real numbers be the wave function of the oscillator at some instant of time. What values of A and B maximize expectation value of position ?\n\nA) A = sqrt(1/2), B = -sqrt(1/2)\nB) A = sqrt(1/3), B = -sqrt(2/3)\nC) A=1/sqrt(2), B=1/sqrt(2)\nD) A = sqrt(1/3), B = sqrt(2/3)\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Consider a linear harmonic oscillator and let, Ψ0 and Ψ 1 be its real, normalized ground and first excited state energy eigenfunctions respectively.\nLet Ψ = AΨ0 + BΨ1 with A and B real numbers be the wave function of the oscillator at some instant of time. What values of A and B maximize expectation value of position ?\n\nA) A = sqrt(1/2), B = -sqrt(1/2)\nB) A = sqrt(1/3), B = -sqrt(2/3)\nC) A=1/sqrt(2), B=1/sqrt(2)\nD) A = sqrt(1/3), B = sqrt(2/3)\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recLslg5RfvRfUHAx:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 44207, 55387, 1432, 328, 4010, 464, 87, 29, 395, 2539, 4504, 80339, 314, 355, 80339, 15, 659, 418, 80339, 16, 350, 13187, 76338, 741, 80339, 15, 326, 80339, 16, 553, 1374, 59625, 10561, 44580, 328, 142698, 170747, 13, 2214, 261, 123676, 142698, 170747, 11, 80339, 15, 382, 1952, 11, 80339, 16, 382, 14210, 13, 49814, 387, 1432, 328, 4010, 306, 261, 14147, 10561, 5294, 25, 464, 87, 29, 314, 220, 15, 395, 2973, 2236, 20485, 44580, 553, 4784, 1952, 503, 14210, 350, 18303, 8967, 12421, 472, 6287, 427, 382, 14210, 4238, 14210, 30, 24305, 1215, 9, 37764, 16, 61, 17, 25, 60982, 16, 382, 14210, 11, 60982, 16, 61, 17, 1952, 11, 1215, 14210, 871, 30089, 12421, 741, 2632, 1606, 8088, 2914, 62274, 25, 464, 87, 29, 314, 220, 17, 355, 418, 35353, 104, 80339, 15, 4061, 8, 1215, 80339, 16, 4061, 8, 29472, 350, 21910, 2973, 1374, 741, 2632, 44207, 49895, 483, 5618, 316, 115461, 44762, 355, 61, 17, 659, 418, 61, 17, 314, 220, 16, 350, 21910, 80339, 59625, 741, 12265, 55387, 382, 23876, 306, 1888, 16520, 350, 46914, 503, 12626, 741, 121125, 30089, 25, 357, 314, 35353, 104, 80339, 15, 1215, 80339, 16, 29472, 13, 2214, 142698, 170747, 11, 581, 1761, 63451, 11019, 18075, 25, 1215, 314, 44237, 7, 5762, 27334, 17, 284, 112349, 915, 350, 64, 659, 261, 78115, 741, 23226, 3577, 464, 15, 91, 1215, 1022, 16, 29, 314, 44237, 7, 5762, 27334, 17, 284, 112349, 915, 464, 15, 91, 261, 659, 261, 78115, 1022, 16, 29, 314, 44237, 7, 5762, 27334, 17, 284, 112349, 915, 350, 464, 15, 91, 261, 1022, 16, 29, 659, 464, 15, 91, 261, 78115, 1022, 16, 29, 14868, 261, 131679, 11, 813, 464, 15, 91, 261, 1022, 16, 29, 314, 44237, 7, 16, 8, 464, 15, 91, 15, 29, 314, 220, 16, 13, 261, 78115, 51090, 25, 464, 15, 91, 261, 78115, 1022, 16, 29, 314, 220, 15, 2236, 484, 8967, 464, 15, 91, 17, 34397, 2632, 12248, 3577, 314, 44237, 7, 5762, 27334, 17, 284, 112349, 8784, 2632, 357, 314, 44237, 7, 5762, 27334, 17, 284, 112349, 8784, 69952, 364, 84787, 464, 87, 29, 314, 220, 17, 355, 418, 357, 13, 2632, 44207, 8841, 464, 87, 29, 481, 1682, 44207, 1888, 355, 418, 5401, 316, 355, 61, 17, 659, 418, 61, 17, 314, 220, 16, 13, 12265, 2973, 1374, 11, 1888, 16520, 2999, 1261, 355, 314, 418, 314, 220, 16, 14, 103946, 17, 350, 46914, 741, 4569, 8967, 16520, 314, 220, 16, 14, 17, 13, 3072, 7477, 2232, 25, 1843, 418, 12626, 11, 1888, 12626, 11, 9874, 1349, 13, 2632, 44207, 464, 87, 29, 8841, 2747, 355, 326, 418, 2973, 8841, 12629, 15410, 25642, 13, 17796, 363, 25, 355, 314, 220, 16, 14, 103946, 17, 11, 418, 314, 220, 16, 14, 103946, 17, 13, 21926, 6052, 364, 84787, 6052, 382, 363, 364, 4383, 3880, 25, 363, 15248, 13, 2632, 9570, 364], "n_tokens": 498, "words": 227, "band_lo": 126.25, "band_hi": 505.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need maximize expectation value of position <x> for superposition ψ = A ψ0 + B ψ1 (real coefficients). ψ0 and ψ1 are real normalized eigenfunctions of harmonic oscillator. For a symmetric harmonic oscillator, ψ0 is even, ψ1 is odd. Expectation value of position in a pure eigenstate: <x> = 0 for both because wavefunctions are either even or odd (odd gives zero as integrand is odd times odd? Wait x*psi1^2: psi1 is odd, psi1^2 even, x odd => integral zero). So only cross term contributes: <x> = 2 A B ∫ ψ0(x) x ψ1(x) dx (since both real). So maximize magnitude with respect to normalization constraint A^2 + B^2 = 1 (since ψ normalized). Since expectation is linear in product AB (positive or negative). Integral integral: I = ∫ ψ0 x ψ1 dx. For harmonic oscillator, we know ladder operator relation: x = sqrt(ħ/(2 m ω)) (a + a†). Matrix element <0| x |1> = sqrt(ħ/(2 m ω)) <0| a + a† |1> = sqrt(ħ/(2 m ω)) ( <0| a |1> + <0| a† |1> ). a lowers, so <0| a |1> = sqrt(1) <0|0> = 1. a† raises: <0| a† |1> = 0 because that gives <0|2>. So matrix element = sqrt(ħ/(2 m ω)). So I = sqrt(ħ/(2 m ω)). Positive.\n\nThus <x> = 2 A B I. So maximize positive <x> you want maximize product A B subject to A^2 + B^2 = 1. Since both real, product AB max when A = B = 1/√2 (positive). That gives AB = 1/2. But note sign: If B negative, product negative, giving min. So maximize <x> positive -> A and B both positive equal magnitudes. Option C: A = 1/√2, B = 1/√2. That's answer.\n\nThus answer is C.\n\nCheck options: C matches. So respond.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -7.748573807475623e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999959, "logp_correct": -4.0562597266257794e-15, "letter_mass": 1.000000000000004, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.4842609377835254, "cot_lp_min64": -0.7735567253446182, "frac_below_-5": 0.008247422680412371, "digit_lp_min": -1.451567530632019, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.00026913834153674543, "n_cot_tokens": 485, "lp_end": -1.2755313036905136e-05, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -7.225533757111278, "p_nocot": 0.0007277639861992855, "uplift": 7.225533757111274, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.293601, "B": 0.621553, "C": 0.000728, "D": 0.084118}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recMyhwYPYHNaVWaj", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: If Maxwell’s equations are written in potential form, one of them is given by\nlaplacian A – (d/dt)^2 A = gradient (divergence(A) + d/dt V) - J\n(ignoring constants), where A and V are the vector and scalar potentials, respectively, and J is the electric current density. Now imagine that magnetic monopoles exist, but they can only form currents (i.e., charge density of magnetic monopoles, rhoM = 0, but current density of magnetic monopoles, JM, could be not 0). And, further, assume that the magnetic current density can be described by the curl of some vector function jm.\nIn that case, how would the previous equation change?\n\nA) A term -(curl jm) is added to the right side of the equation.\nB) A term -(d/dt jm) is added to the right side of the equation.\nC) A term gradient(divergence jm) is subtracted to the right side of the equation.\nD) Other Maxwell’s equations change, but not this one.\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: If Maxwell’s equations are written in potential form, one of them is given by\nlaplacian A – (d/dt)^2 A = gradient (divergence(A) + d/dt V) - J\n(ignoring constants), where A and V are the vector and scalar potentials, respectively, and J is the electric current density. Now imagine that magnetic monopoles exist, but they can only form currents (i.e., charge density of magnetic monopoles, rhoM = 0, but current density of magnetic monopoles, JM, could be not 0). And, further, assume that the magnetic current density can be described by the curl of some vector function jm.\nIn that case, how would the previous equation change?\n\nA) A term -(curl jm) is added to the right side of the equation.\nB) A term -(d/dt jm) is added to the right side of the equation.\nC) A term gradient(divergence jm) is subtracted to the right side of the equation.\nD) Other Maxwell’s equations change, but not this one.\n", "true_answer": "B", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recMyhwYPYHNaVWaj:3", "cot_tokens": [976, 4928, 25, 105786, 885, 61524, 306, 6451, 1625, 25, 58096, 145838, 1200, 355, 1127, 350, 67, 6662, 83, 73602, 17, 355, 314, 40553, 350, 862, 2347, 1082, 10706, 8, 659, 272, 6662, 83, 631, 8, 533, 643, 350, 733, 7443, 38252, 741, 21926, 591, 20485, 42006, 395, 9727, 6451, 483, 52124, 7553, 50130, 30, 50557, 290, 20485, 42006, 25, 174920, 32, 314, 4403, 15, 643, 350, 6332, 50130, 7060, 35353, 224, 62, 1722, 355, 61, 1722, 314, 220, 15, 741, 730, 150885, 2360, 52124, 7553, 50130, 11, 581, 679, 35353, 229, 61, 17, 355, 533, 350, 16, 4308, 61, 17, 8, 35353, 224, 61, 17, 355, 14, 18085, 224, 83, 61, 17, 314, 533, 1722, 15, 643, 13, 3164, 10175, 40553, 2914, 5192, 316, 625, 24667, 50130, 30, 3164, 679, 40553, 350, 862, 355, 659, 35353, 224, 631, 14, 18085, 224, 83, 741, 4569, 2914, 1164, 28664, 1641, 52124, 7553, 50130, 25, 4223, 355, 659, 35353, 224, 53, 14, 18085, 224, 83, 314, 220, 15, 13, 2632, 290, 42006, 382, 35353, 229, 61, 17, 355, 533, 35353, 224, 61, 17, 355, 14, 18085, 224, 83, 61, 17, 314, 533, 41, 364, 10620, 483, 33641, 139494, 1491, 106155, 1606, 350, 102854, 2372, 314, 220, 15, 11, 643, 2372, 625, 12421, 741, 730, 25399, 77628, 11, 290, 38756, 316, 105786, 885, 61524, 1147, 33641, 2208, 5941, 316, 15085, 49283, 885, 3954, 5178, 13, 44130, 11, 483, 33641, 14843, 11, 105786, 885, 61524, 5025, 1402, 18085, 229, 5366, 36, 314, 220, 1184, 4618, 820, 4278, 15, 198, 18085, 229, 5366, 33, 314, 4403, 15, 220, 1184, 1285, 198, 18085, 229, 12378, 36, 314, 533, 18085, 224, 33, 14, 18085, 224, 83, 533, 4403, 15, 643, 1285, 198, 18085, 229, 12378, 33, 314, 4403, 15, 643, 4618, 659, 4278, 15, 4403, 15, 35353, 224, 36, 14, 18085, 224, 83, 279, 3335, 220, 1184, 1285, 314, 15, 889, 643, 1285, 42308, 254, 220,