 328, 11002, 28261, 656, 50468, 6049, 328, 68141, 350, 1265, 13, 2290, 8, 314, 220, 899, 14, 22, 871, 391, 2372, 314, 350, 899, 14, 22, 11043, 44, 3080, 13, 1843, 2893, 88393, 382, 478, 350, 1265, 741, 391, 2372, 314, 350, 899, 14, 22, 11043, 1265, 314, 220, 1494, 13, 15, 13, 21926, 5263, 316, 63974, 350, 1494, 13, 18, 741, 3072, 63974, 11526, 63974, 7, 45485, 8, 17, 1118, 382, 30281, 18258, 117743, 30, 63974, 7, 45485, 8, 17, 382, 16132, 117743, 889, 9474, 30281, 18258, 117743, 13, 17484, 63974, 18, 45, 17, 4310, 30, 11377, 11, 77762, 27054, 2037, 63974, 18, 45, 17, 13, 129157, 25, 63974, 18, 45, 17, 659, 220, 21, 487, 17, 46, 15155, 220, 18, 63974, 7, 45485, 8, 17, 659, 220, 17, 48198, 18, 13, 9700, 0, 2632, 484, 15248, 27922, 44252, 11851, 13, 19983, 18051, 11002, 25, 11741, 88393, 314, 4842, 63974, 25, 4842, 478, 314, 350, 18, 9, 1494, 13, 18, 199990, 17, 9, 1265, 13, 15, 8, 314, 220, 8540, 13, 24, 25, 2029, 314, 220, 17, 13, 38353, 25, 16, 2747, 18051, 314, 220, 8540, 13, 24, 14, 2029, 314, 220, 17, 13, 38353, 871, 22171, 472, 220, 1157, 25, 22, 314, 220, 17, 13, 41467, 13, 163508, 9809, 5192, 316, 112605, 328, 50468, 28460, 13, 41021, 23864, 6354, 483, 6290, 50468, 57556, 25, 63974, 220, 1494, 13, 24531, 11, 478, 220, 1265, 13, 19378, 13, 7801, 220, 18, 9, 1494, 13, 24531, 28, 8540, 13, 42180, 11, 220, 17, 9, 1265, 13, 19378, 28, 2029, 13, 28207, 13, 84705, 314, 220, 8540, 13, 42180, 14, 2029, 13, 28207, 314, 220, 17, 13, 38353, 13, 2214, 220, 1157, 14, 22, 314, 17, 13, 41467, 13, 23015, 889, 625, 6354, 26, 10112, 5192, 316, 2360, 5355, 68753, 50468, 57556, 30, 1843, 1023, 1199, 48697, 50468, 57556, 12951, 63974, 28, 1494, 11, 478, 28, 1265, 8967, 18051, 220, 8540, 25, 2029, 314, 220, 1157, 25, 22, 9707, 0, 41351, 220, 8540, 25, 2029, 168151, 94879, 656, 220, 19, 8967, 220, 1157, 25, 22, 13, 27046, 0, 2632, 1023, 2061, 68753, 57556, 220, 1494, 395, 63974, 11, 220, 1265, 395, 478, 13, 2632, 355, 382, 63974, 18, 45, 17, 364, 5808, 9192, 277, 4842, 328, 355, 314, 220, 18, 9, 1494, 659, 220, 17, 9, 1265, 314, 220, 8540, 10, 2029, 28, 1353, 329, 86398, 13, 17511, 6354, 4824, 1481, 413, 220, 1353, 13, 24, 13, 2632, 36628, 6049, 2846, 220, 1353, 13, 4569, 25709, 306, 3352, 220, 2744, 12, 7920, 350, 3941, 355, 741, 19233, 6052, 355, 364, 4383, 1273, 3880, 25, 418, 220, 10165, 12, 9444, 11, 363, 220, 3898, 12, 8017, 11, 415, 220, 11999, 12, 14953, 13, 2632, 6052, 355, 364, 84787, 1721, 6052, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 355, 13], "n_tokens": 1623, "words": 761, "band_lo": 299.25, "band_hi": 1197.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to parse problem. A is a compound formed by a metal and nonmetal, weight ratio metal:nonmetal = 18:7. When excess water reacts with 1 mol A, yields 2 mol of gaseous Y and 3 mol of base Z (sparingly soluble). Both Y and Z basic. Relative density of gas Y compared to CO2 is 0.39. So d(Y)/d(CO2)=0.39. At same T,P, density proportional to molar mass (ideal gas). So M(Y)/M(CO2)=0.39. M(CO2)=44 g/mol. So M(Y)=0.39*44 = 17.16 g/mol approx. That suggests Y is likely NH3 (M=17). Basic gas, yes. So Y = NH3.\n\nThus A reacts with water to produce 2 mol NH3 per mol A, and 3 mol base Z (sparingly soluble). Base Z likely is a metal hydroxide, sparingly soluble; maybe Ca(OH)2? but Ca(OH)2 is slightly soluble. Could be Al(OH)3? Not soluble. Perhaps M(OH)3? Reaction suggests metal cation forms hydroxide as base. Sparingly soluble base => metal hydroxide of Al, Fe(OH)3, Cr(OH)3? But those are amphoteric.\n\nLet's think of compound A is metal nitride? Reaction of metal nitride with water forms NH3 gas and metal hydroxide. Example: Ca3N2 + 6 H2O → 2 NH3 + 3 Ca(OH)2. Indeed calcium nitride reacts with water to produce ammonia and calcium hydroxide. Ratio: per 1 mol Ca3N2 yields 2 mol NH3 and 3 mol Ca(OH)2 (sparingly soluble? Actually Ca(OH)2 is slightly soluble, classified as sparingly soluble base). Good. So A could be Ca3N2. Metal: Ca, nonmetal: N. Weight ratio: mass Ca:mass N = 18:7.\n\nCalculate masses: molar mass Ca = 40.08 g/mol, N = 14.01. For Ca3N2, mass Ca = 3*40.08=120.24. Mass N=2*14.01=28.02. Ratio Ca/N =120.24/28.02 = 4.29. Convert to weight ratio 18:7 ~ 2.571. Not same.\n\nWait ratio given is 18:7 (metal:non-metal). For Ca3N2 it's 120.24:28.02 = 4.29:1 => multiply to make integer ratio? 4.29 approx 18/4.2? No.\n\nLet's compute ratio by weight: metal mass / nonmetal mass = 18/7 = 2.571. So metal is about 2.571 times heavier per mass than nonmetal.\n\nLet M_metal (atomic weight) = M_M, N_nonmetal atomic weight = M_N. For compound formula M_x N_y (x metal atoms, y nonmetal atoms). The weight ratio = (x M_M)/(y M_N)=18/7.\n\nAlso reaction with water: 1 mol A yields 2 mol NH3 and 3 mol base M(OH)_? If base is M(OH)3? Actually stoichiometry suggests per metal nitride M_x N_y plus water yields amonia and metal hydroxide. For generic metal nitride M_n N_m: M_n N_m + (n+m) H2O → n M(OH) + m NH3? Let's derive.\n\nTake Ca3N2: formula M3N2. Reaction: Ca3N2 + 6 H2O → 3 Ca(OH)2 + 2 NH3. Indeed each N produces NH3 (1 N per NH3). For 2 N gives 2 NH3. Each Ca forms Ca(OH)2 requiring 2 H2O per Ca? Actually Ca(OH)2 from Ca + 2 H2O? Reaction: Ca + 2 H2O → Ca(OH)2 + H2? But anyway stoichiometry gives 6 water.\n\nGeneral: M_a N_b + (a+ 2b) H2O → a M(OH)_2 + b NH3 (if metal forms M(OH)2). For metal that forms M(OH)2. Then per mol A gives b mol NH3 = number of N atoms. For our case they get 2 mol NH3, so b=2. And produce 3 mol base Z = a =3. So a=3, b=2. So formula M3N2 again! So indeed A is M3N2. This matches base type: M(OH)2, sparingly soluble.\n\nThus metal forms divalent hydroxide (M(OH)2). For M3N2, metal likely alkaline earth (Ca, Sr, Ba). Which have M(OH)2 (sparingly soluble). Also metal/ nonmetal weight ratio for M3N2 = (3 M_M):(2 M_N) = 18:7.\n\nThus 3 M_M / (2 M_N) = 18/7. So M_M / M_N = (18/7)*(2/3) = (36)/(21) = 12/7 = approx 1.7143. So atomic weight of metal divided by atomic weight of nitrogen (14.01) = 12/7 => M_M = (12/7)*M_N. If nonmetal is N (14). M_M = (12/7)*14 = 24.0. That's close to Mg (24.3). But Mg forms Mg(OH)2 which is sparingly soluble? Mg(OH)2 is slightly soluble but considered sparingly soluble. Does Mg3N2 exist? Yes, magnesium nitride Mg3N2. Reaction: Mg3N2 + 6 H2O → 3 Mg(OH)2 + 2 NH3. Good! So that matches stoichiometry. Weight ratio metal:nonmetal = mass Mg: mass N = (3*24.3):(2*14.0) = 72.9:28 = 2.603:1 -> ratio = 72.9/28 = 2.603 => expressed as 18:7 = 2.571. Slight difference due to rounding of atomic weights. Let's compute exact with actual atomic masses: Mg 24.305, N 14.007. Then 3*24.305=72.915, 2*14.007=28.014. Ratio = 72.915/28.014 = 2.603. For 18/7 =2.571. Close but not exact; maybe due to using common approximate atomic masses? If they use simpler atomic masses perhaps Mg=24, N=14 gives ratio 72:28 = 18:7 exactly! Indeed 72:28 simplifies dividing by 4 gives 18:7. Perfect! So they used approximate masses 24 for Mg, 14 for N. So A is Mg3N2.\n\nSo molar mass of A = 3*24 + 2*14 = 72+28=100 g/mol. Using exact values would be 100.9. So molecular weight around 100. That falls in range 90-110 (option A). Therefore answer A.\n\nCheck other options: B 140-160, C 65-85, D 115-135. So answer A.\n\nThus final answer: ANSWER: A.", "response": "ANSWER: A", "answer": "A", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -2.264974220622662e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999997834, "logp_correct": -2.1655627011048078e-13, "letter_mass": 0.9999998807909412, "p_letters": {"A": 1.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.5125305868108021, "cot_lp_min64": -1.213744436460935, "frac_below_-5": 0.012422360248447204, "digit_lp_min": -2.237835168838501, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 1610, "lp_end": -3.576278118089249e-07, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -2.3841855067985307e-07, "logp_nocot": -3.2949282297199343, "p_nocot": 0.037070705526644564, "uplift": 3.2949282297197175, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.037071, "B": 0.213327, "C": 0.744585, "D": 0.005017}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recNu3MXkvWUzHZr9", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: An intelligent civilization in the Large Magellanic Cloud has engineered an extraordinary spacecraft capable of traveling at a substantial fraction of the speed of light. The average lifetime of these aliens is roughly 150 solar years.  Now, having Earth as their destination in mind, they are determined to travel with this spacecraft at a constant speed of 0.99999987*c, where c is the speed of light. Approximately, how long will it take for their 22 years old astronaut (from the point of view of the astronaut) to reach the Earth using this incredibly fast spacecraft?\n\nA) 72 years\nB) The astronaut will die before reaching to the Earth.\nC) 77 years\nD) 81 years\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: An intelligent civilization in the Large Magellanic Cloud has engineered an extraordinary spacecraft capable of traveling at a substantial fraction of the speed of light. The average lifetime of these aliens is roughly 150 solar years.  Now, having Earth as their destination in mind, they are determined to travel with this spacecraft at a constant speed of 0.99999987*c, where c is the speed of light. Approximately, how long will it take for their 22 years old astronaut (from the point of view of the astronaut) to reach the Earth using this incredibly fast spacecraft?\n\nA) 72 years\nB) The astronaut will die before reaching to the Earth.\nC) 77 years\nD) 81 years\n", "true_answer": "D", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recNu3MXkvWUzHZr9:1", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 8420, 290, 4792, 25, 107586, 591, 451, 15190, 316, 16464, 540, 7733, 220, 15, 13, 9130, 9130, 6818, 274, 13, 451, 15190, 9324, 30, 623, 27976, 7873, 596, 32522, 17831, 382, 1078, 220, 17