84787, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 415], "n_tokens": 821, "words": 261, "band_lo": 117.5, "band_hi": 470.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to parse the problem: spacecraft from LMC to Earth at speed 0.99999987 c. LMC distance? The Large Magellanic Cloud is about 163,000 light-years away from Earth (approx 163,000 ly). But need to know actual distance used in problem. Likely they expect distance ~ 163k ly. However astronaut lifetime is 150 solar years (in its rest frame). They ask how long will it take for the astronaut (proper time) to reach Earth traveling at that speed. So we compute proper time = distance / (gamma * v)?? Actually proper time experienced by astronaut = coordinate time divided by gamma, because they travel at high speed relative to Earth frame; in Earth frame travel time = distance / v. Then proper time = Earth frame time / gamma (time dilation). So compute.\n\nGiven v = 0.99999987 c. Compute gamma = 1 / sqrt(1 - v^2/c^2). Let's calculate: v = 1 - epsilon where epsilon? v = 0.99999987. Compute beta = 0.99999987. Then 1 - beta^2 = 1 - (0.99999987)^2 ≈ 1 - (0.99999974?) Let's compute precisely: beta^2 = (1 - 1.3e-7)^2 ≈ 1 - 2.6e-7 + (1.3e-7)^2 ≈ 1 - 2.6e-7 + 1.69e-14 ≈ 0.99999974. So 1 - beta^2 ≈ 2.6e-7. Actually more exact: 0.99999987^2 =? Use (1 - 1.3e-7)^2 = 1 - 2.6e-7 + (1.69e-14) ≈ 0.99999974. So delta = 2.6e-7. sqrt(delta) = sqrt(2.6e-7) ≈ sqrt(2.6)*1e-3.5? Wait: 2.6e-7 => sqrt = sqrt(2.6)*10^{-3.5}. sqrt(2.6) ~1.612. 10^{-3.5} = 10^{-3} * 10^{-0.5}=0.001*0.3162=0.0003162. Multiply: 1.612*0.0003162 ≈0.000509. So gamma = 1/0.000509 ≈1965. Actually compute: 1/5.09e-4 = 1965. So gamma ≈ 1965.\n\nNow distance LMC ~ 163,000 ly. Travel time in Earth frame t = D/v ≈163,000 ly / 0.99999987c ≈163,000 years (since v ~c). More precisely t ~163,000 / 0.99999987 ≈163,000 * (1+1.3e-7) ≈163,000 +0.021 ≈163,000.021 years. Essentially 163,000 years.\n\nNow proper time τ = t / gamma ≈163,000 years / 1965 ≈83.0 years. Let's compute: 163,000 / 2000 =81.5 years; dividing by 1965 give about 82.96 years. So roughly 83 years.\n\nOptions: A 72, B die, C 77, D 81. Closest is D 81 years. Not exact but likely answer D. They maybe used distance 160,000 ly approximated, gamma maybe slightly different 2000 leading to 80 years = 81. So answer D.\n\nThus: ANSWER: D", "response": "ANSWER: D", "answer": "D", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.311301275563892e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999786, "logp_correct": -2.1405225632715386e-14, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000213, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 1.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.40571645105684845, "cot_lp_min64": -0.9715770977868052, "frac_below_-5": 0.007425742574257425, "digit_lp_min": -4.176685810089111, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.08761311322450638, "n_cot_tokens": 808, "lp_end": -0.132444366812706, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -2.3841855067985307e-07, "logp_nocot": -8.755103090373844, "p_nocot": 0.00015765474243546886, "uplift": 8.755103090373822, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.002466, "B": 0.99491, "C": 0.002466, "D": 0.000158}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recOEBk1oclk8qChi", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Which of the following four-body processes cannot occur at a single SM vertex?\n\nA) gg->gg\nB) qq->qq\nC) HH->HH\nD) WW->WW\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Which of the following four-body processes cannot occur at a single SM vertex?\n\nA) gg->gg\nB) qq->qq\nC) HH->HH\nD) WW->WW\n", "true_answer": "B", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recOEBk1oclk8qChi:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 4218, 1118, 4242, 19146, 14340, 6284, 11416, 540, 261, 4590, 20297, 25363, 13, 730, 290, 20297, 11, 18864, 30722, 553, 4335, 656, 38360, 25, 50130, 26134, 263, 1051, 63516, 6711, 350, 371, 5335, 326, 19004, 291, 50130, 3840, 126602, 936, 113272, 9233, 1051, 63516, 6711, 350, 179521, 291, 88996, 936, 100810, 7036, 3840, 126602, 350, 131453, 294, 12, 131453, 294, 13091, 191401, 741, 623, 14340, 4335, 553, 1402, 32, 8, 87993, 2747, 87993, 25, 1920, 147758, 1808, 306, 11, 1920, 147758, 1808, 842, 13, 17484, 20297, 679, 261, 4242, 59851, 170366, 25363, 30, 11377, 11, 1486, 8257, 853, 261, 4242, 59851, 170366, 25363, 591, 290, 2893, 12, 1143, 1200, 50130, 3259, 2914, 13, 2632, 87993, 609, 3249, 665, 11416, 4493, 261, 4590, 25363, 350, 3086, 19004, 291, 147758, 263, 25363, 741, 2632, 355, 382, 4149, 540, 261, 4590, 20297, 25363, 364, 33, 8, 25999, 2747, 25999, 25, 1920, 474, 13455, 306, 11, 1920, 474, 13455, 842, 13, 30456, 413, 2684, 23341, 109445, 4493, 147758, 263, 13041, 350, 83, 97554, 8, 889, 484, 382, 625, 261, 4590, 25363, 13, 2763, 1354, 261, 4242, 12, 131453, 294, 25363, 306, 20297, 30, 3004, 18864, 4242, 12, 131453, 294, 25363, 306, 20297, 350, 25035, 8488, 454, 33673, 30722, 1934, 74479, 842, 486, 113185, 11, 889, 2617, 553, 625, 18864, 741, 623, 20297, 451, 13380, 172586, 853, 100810, 7036, 3840, 126602, 350, 131453, 294, 12, 131453, 294, 13091, 191401, 8, 350, 47660, 37909, 8, 326, 50130, 3840, 126602, 350, 131453, 294, 12, 131453, 294, 6559, 48895, 8, 350, 47660, 37909, 741, 3004, 4242, 12, 131453, 294, 25363, 13, 2632, 25999, 609, 8127, 6284, 11416, 540, 261, 4590, 25363, 26, 1309, 13041, 328, 50130, 26134, 263, 350, 38397, 38360, 741, 2632, 418, 6284, 413, 261, 4590, 25363, 364, 34, 8, 46207, 2747, 46207, 25, 4242, 113272, 9233, 8532, 109445, 13, 20297, 113272, 9233, 6451, 6664, 261, 19004, 291, 2914, 17667, 350, 34931, 78115, 34931, 73602, 17, 1118, 8967, 261, 4242, 13091, 191401, 25363, 350, 16228, 28044, 2846, 631, 26140, 741, 2632, 46207, 609, 35743, 665, 11416, 4493, 261, 4590, 19004, 291, 113272, 9233, 25363, 13, 2632, 363, 382, 4149, 364, 35, 8, 43758, 609, 22648, 25, 4242, 486, 26134, 1808, 109445, 13, 623, 20297, 50130, 11207, 6664, 19004, 291, 3840, 126602, 6200, 4471, 843, 68, 422, 50130, 26134, 1808, 591, 290, 2893, 12, 1143, 1200, 19457, 7, 17, 8, 8532, 11, 575, 2560, 4213, 261, 4242, 14439, 25363, 13031, 350, 21475, 46730, 486, 10, 54, 14439, 10, 54, 12, 5178, 741, 2632, 43758, 609, 22648, 665, 11416, 4493, 261, 4590, 25363, 350, 3086, 19004, 291, 50130, 26134, 263, 88996, 741, 2632, 415, 4149, 364, 84787, 6052, 382, 418, 364, 84787, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 418], "n_tokens": 465, "words": 300, "band_lo": 152.5, "band_hi": 610.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to understand which four-body processes cannot occur at a single SM vertex. In the SM, fundamental interactions are given by vertices: gauge boson self-interactions (triple and quartic gauge couplings), Higgs self-interactions (quartic coupling), Yukawa couplings (fermion-fermion-Higgs). The processes given are:\n\nA) gg -> gg: two gluons in, two gluons out. Does SM have a four-gluon vertex? Yes, QCD has a four-gluon vertex from the non-abelian gauge field term. So gg->gg can occur via a single vertex (the quartic gluon vertex). So A is possible at a single SM vertex.\n\nB) qq -> qq: two quarks in, two quarks out. Could be same flavor scattering via gluon exchange (t-channel) but that is not a single vertex. Is there a four-fermion vertex in SM? No fundamental four-fermion vertex in SM (except effective Fermi interactions after integrating out W/Z, but those are not fundamental). The SM Lagrangian has Yukawa couplings (fermion-fermion-Higgs) (three-point) and gauge couplings (fermion-fermion-gauge) (three-point). No four-fermion vertex. So qq->qq cannot occur at a single vertex; need exchange of gauge boson (two vertices). So B cannot be a single vertex.\n\nC) HH -> HH: four Higgs fields scattering. SM Higgs potential includes a quartic term λ (Φ†Φ)^2 which gives a four-Higgs vertex (when expanded around VEV). So HH->HH can occur via a single quartic Higgs vertex. So C is possible.\n\nD) WW->WW: four W bosons scattering. The SM gauge sector includes quartic couplings among electroweak gauge bosons from the non-abelian SU(2) fields, i.e., a four-W vertex exists (specifically W+W-W+W- etc). So WW->WW can occur via a single vertex (the quartic gauge boson coupling). So D possible.\n\nThus answer is B.\n\nThus: ANSWER: B", "response": "ANSWER: B", "answer": "B", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -8.344648563252122e-07, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999793, "logp_correct": -2.0643212699316234e-14, "letter_mass": 0.9999995231630898, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.42010783431396237, "cot_lp_min64": -0.6868021506675164, "frac_below_-5": 0.0022123893805309734, "digit_lp_min": 0.0, "answer_first_mention_lp": -5.23315102327615e-05, "n_cot_tokens": 452, "lp_end": -0.261003315448761, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -2.3841855067985307e-07, "logp_nocot": -5.660546966470527, "p_nocot": 0.0034806125990766634, "uplift": 5.660546966470506, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.013766, "B": 0.003481, "C": 0.965077, "D": 0.017676}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recOGRn4Gw3R2NAQv", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: What is the magnitude of the magnetic field (in Tesla) created at the nucleus by the orbital motion of an electron in the lowest orbit of the hydrogen atom\n\nA) 45 Tesla\nB) 3 Tesla\nC) 12.5 Tesla\nD) 27.5 Tesla\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: What is the magnitude of the magnetic field (in Tesla) created at the nucleus by the orbital motion of an electron in the lowest orbit of the hydrogen atom\n\nA) 45 Tesla\nB) 3 Tesla\nC) 12.5 Tesla\nD) 27.5 Tesla\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recOGRn4Gw3R2NAQv:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 23864, 33641, 3259, 540, 117323, 5192, 316, 23629, 61353, 350, 72, 2560, 4213, 2208, 11453, 741, 730, 47612, 7740, 2608, 350, 6581, 2012, 2359, 741, 131282, 306, 37626, 61353, 21090, 314, 4381, 2012, 21090, 261, 15, 314, 220, 15, 13, 41043, 49805, 314, 220, 15, 13, 41043, 1215, 702, 85848, 702, 284, 13, 23451, 323, 314, 3793, 274, 30, 4381, 2012, 2359, 25, 323, 314, 319, 61, 17, 27334, 17, 4278, 15, 312, 2990, 8, 186402, 25, 323, 314, 350, 68, 61, 17, 60504, 17, 4278, 15, 312, 8, 75946, 50557, 4381, 2012, 25, 38962, 41184, 297, 5762, 11, 395, 297, 28, 16, 11, 284, 323, 428, 314, 41051, 13, 8820, 147293, 2722, 9578, 314, 27964, 488, 57767, 25, 372, 319, 61, 17, 820, 428, 61, 17, 314, 284, 323, 61, 17, 820, 428, 13, 116151, 8967, 323, 314, 319, 61, 17, 820, 350, 17, 4278, 15, 312, 2990, 8, 6961, 41021, 23864, 9076, 2905, 25, 323, 314, 3793, 274, 314, 350, 16, 14, 18663, 11043, 66, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 858, 68, 21, 284, 5031, 13, 11377, 364, 6576, 357, 314, 8363, 777, 5265, 314, 319, 820, 353, 11, 1919, 353, 314, 220, 17, 1345, 428, 820, 323, 13, 2632, 357, 314, 319, 323, 820, 350, 17, 1345, 428, 741, 103697, 3259, 540, 6170, 328, 37626, 11453, 350, 14135, 1819, 6170, 11, 21090, 428, 8, 382, 418, 314, 4403, 15, 357, 820, 350, 17, 428, 741, 50557, 33641, 3259, 540, 6170, 328, 261, 37626, 11453, 25, 418, 314, 4403, 15, 357, 820, 350, 17, 428, 741, 2632, 418, 314, 4403, 15, 350, 68, 323, 820, 350, 17, 1345, 428, 915, 820, 350, 17, 428, 8, 314, 4403, 15, 319, 323, 820, 350, 19, 1345, 428, 61, 17, 741, 45438, 25, 4403, 15, 314, 220, 19, 1345, 33839, 702, 85848, 22, 487, 5712, 13, 2632, 4403, 15, 27334, 19, 1345, 8, 314, 220, 702, 85848, 22, 13, 7801, 418, 314, 350, 702, 85848, 22, 8, 425, 319, 323, 820, 428, 61, 17, 364, 97401, 8663, 25, 319, 314, 220, 16, 13, 37875, 68, 12, 858, 363, 13, 323, 314, 3793, 274, 42308, 230, 350, 16, 14, 18663, 11043, 18, 68, 23, 314, 220, 17, 13, 858, 68, 21, 284, 5031, 13, 428, 314, 261, 15, 314, 220, 15, 13, 41043, 68, 12, 702, 284, 13, 428, 61, 17, 314, 350, 15, 13, 41043, 68, 12, 702, 73602, 17, 314, 220, 15, 13, 31468, 24, 68, 12, 455, 314, 220, 17, 13, 41556, 68, 12, 2040, 284, 61, 17, 364, 10620, 23864, 149054, 25, 319, 323, 314, 220, 16, 13, 37875, 68, 12, 858, 425, 220, 17, 13, 858, 68, 21, 314, 220, 18, 13, 35911, 68, 12, 1311, 350, 34, 5366, 76, 5031, 741, 137658, 656, 220, 16, 68, 12, 22, 871, 220, 18, 13, 35911, 68, 12, 455, 13, 105916, 656, 428, 61, 17, 25, 220, 18, 13, 35911, 68, 12, 455, 820, 220, 17, 13, 41556, 68, 12, 2040, 314, 220, 899, 13, 6733, 13, 2632, 418, 42308, 230, 220, 899, 13, 20, 52960, 13, 4569, 15248, 5317, 363, 364, 84787, 6052, 363, 364, 4383, 25, 418, 314, 4403, 15, 319, 323, 820, 350, 19, 1345, 428, 61, 17, 741, 17511, 4403, 15, 314, 220, 19, 1345, 12378, 702, 85848, 22, 11, 168151, 472, 5151, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 363, 13], "n_tokens": 570, "words": 204, "band_lo": 113.25, "band_hi": 453.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to compute magnetic field at nucleus due to electron orbit (i.e., current loop). In hydrogen ground state (Bohr model). Electron in circular orbit radius = Bohr radius a0 = 0.529 Å = 0.529 x10^-10 m. Speed v = α c? Bohr model: v = e^2/(2 ε0 hbar) hmm: v = (e^2)/(2 ε0 h) ??? Actually Bohr: angular momentum nħ, for n=1, m v r = ħ. Also Coulomb force = centripetal: k e^2 / r^2 = m v^2 / r. Solve gives v = e^2 / (2 ε0 hbar)?? Let's compute numerically: v = α c = (1/137)*c ≈ 2.19e6 m/s. Yes.\n\nCurrent I = charge per period = e / T, where T = 2π r / v. So I = e v / (2π r). Magnetic field at center of circular loop (axis through center, radius r) is B = μ0 I / (2 r). Actually magnetic field at center of a circular loop: B = μ0 I / (2 r). So B = μ0 (e v / (2π r)) / (2 r) = μ0 e v / (4π r^2). Compute: μ0 = 4π ×10^-7 H/m. So μ0/(4π) = 10^-7. Then B = (10^-7) * e v / r^2.\n\nPlug numbers: e = 1.602e-19 C. v = α c ≈ (1/137)*3e8 = 2.19e6 m/s. r = a0 = 0.529e-10 m. r^2 = (0.529e-10)^2 = 0.2799e-20 = 2.799e-21 m^2.\n\nNow compute numerator: e v = 1.602e-19 * 2.19e6 = 3.508e-13 (C·m/s). Multiply by 1e-7 => 3.508e-20. Divide by r^2: 3.508e-20 / 2.799e-21 = 12.54. So B ≈ 12.5 Tesla. That matches option C.\n\nThus answer C.\n\nCheck: B = μ0 e v / (4π r^2). Using μ0 = 4π×10^-7, simplifies as above.\n\nThus answer: C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -2.1457441107486375e-05, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999948, "logp_correct": -5.167145446335578e-15, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000053, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.29291239449254675, "cot_lp_min64": -0.7135042435771278, "frac_below_-5": 0.005385996409335727, "digit_lp_min": -3.288041353225708, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 557, "lp_end": -1.8358061424805783e-05, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -1.1920928244535389e-07, "logp_nocot": -4.330341188185454, "p_nocot": 0.013163055644770586, "uplift": 4.330341188185448, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.264387, "B": 0.718679, "C": 0.013163, "D": 0.003771}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recOKwCrRbyEWoYKe", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: You have prepared an unknown alkane compound. You started with heptane (C7H16) and through several reactions some of the hydrogens have been replaced. The replaced hydrogens have been replaced by either –CH3, –CH2R, –CHR2, or –CR3 groups, where R is non-hydrogen.  \n\nA 1H NMR spectrum of the product was obtained. The multiplicities of the signals due to the hydrogens on carbon-1 through to carbon-7 of the starting heptane backbone are as follows:\n\nt, dq, dt, ddt, ddd, ddt, d\n(i.e. Carbon-1 = t (triplet), Carbon-2 = dq (double of quartets), etc\n\nIdentify which groups (out of the options –CH3, –CH2R, –CHR2, or –CR3) must be placed on which carbon (numbered 1 to 7 from left to right) in order that the multiplicities of the 1H NMR are achieved.\n\n(“no change” below indicates that the carbon retains its 2 hydrogens. If only one change is made to a carbon, then it still retains its other hydrogen).\n\nA) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: no change\nCarbon 3: –CR3\nCarbon 4: –CH2R\nCarbon 5: –CH2R\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CHR2\nB) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: no change\nCarbon 3: –CR3\nCarbon 4: –CH2R\nCarbon 5: –CHR2\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CR3\nC) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: no change\nCarbon 3: –CH2R\nCarbon 4: –CR3\nCarbon 5: –CHR2\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CH2R\nD) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: –CH2R\nCarbon 3: no change\nCarbon 4: –CH2R\nCarbon 5: –CR3\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CHR2\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: You have prepared an unknown alkane compound. You started with heptane (C7H16) and through several reactions some of the hydrogens have been replaced. The replaced hydrogens have been replaced by either –CH3, –CH2R, –CHR2, or –CR3 groups, where R is non-hydrogen.  \n\nA 1H NMR spectrum of the product was obtained. The multiplicities of the signals due to the hydrogens on carbon-1 through to carbon-7 of the starting heptane backbone are as follows:\n\nt, dq, dt, ddt, ddd, ddt, d\n(i.e. Carbon-1 = t (triplet), Carbon-2 = dq (double of quartets), etc\n\nIdentify which groups (out of the options –CH3, –CH2R, –CHR2, or –CR3) must be placed on which carbon (numbered 1 to 7 from left to right) in order that the multiplicities of the 1H NMR are achieved.\n\n(“no change” below indicates that the carbon retains its 2 hydrogens. If only one change is made to a carbon, then it still retains its other hydrogen).\n\nA) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: no change\nCarbon 3: –CR3\nCarbon 4: –CH2R\nCarbon 5: –CH2R\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CHR2\nB) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: no change\nCarbon 3: –CR3\nCarbon 4: –CH2R\nCarbon 5: –CHR2\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CR3\nC) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: no change\nCarbon 3: –CH2R\nCarbon 4: –CR3\nCarbon 5: –CHR2\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CH2R\nD) Carbon 1: no change\nCarbon 2: –CH2R\nCarbon 3: no change\nCarbon 4: –CH2R\nCarbon 5: –CR3\nCarbon 6: –CHR2\nCarbon 7: –CHR2\n", "true_answer": "B", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recOKwCrRbyEWoYKe:1", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 18135, 290, 478, 27029, 67929, 1629, 328, 290, 12063, 12885, 696, 402, 290, 4756, 501, 555, 1986, 94240, 13, 46049, 501, 555, 1986, 363, 16, 1585, 34, 22, 13464, 13, 5934, 5028, 5773, 13284, 1236, 12063, 12885, 696, 402, 2617, 41933, 1808, 483, 8896, 350, 2082, 3643, 82, 741, 11555, 15883, 382, 1014, 18, 472, 997, 328, 13464, 13, 2214, 2454, 15883, 575, 11, 581, 679, 22257, 4454, 2086, 328, 487, 25, 363, 16, 10049, 18, 350, 18, 487, 936, 8812, 41933, 1808, 10049, 17, 350, 17, 487, 936, 363, 22, 10049, 18, 350, 18, 487, 741, 6311, 92838, 11, 1236, 487, 21009, 656, 1273, 8896, 13, 478, 27029, 18587, 350, 163898, 459, 1629, 8, 553, 4335, 395, 290, 29026, 5192, 316,