18, 10, 3609, 314, 363, 179235, 18, 195794, 314, 220, 15, 13, 2290, 391, 8, 314, 723, 5563, 18, 143272, 659, 723, 5563, 39, 17, 3896, 19, 61, 17, 10, 37441, 84787, 25, 363, 314, 723, 5563, 18, 143272, 659, 658, 69, 126471, 5563, 18, 10, 2696, 39, 17, 3896, 19, 12, 60, 314, 723, 5563, 18, 143272, 350, 16, 659, 658, 69, 126471, 39, 17, 3896, 19, 12, 60, 3991, 144594, 395, 723, 5563, 18, 10, 12433, 723, 5563, 18, 143272, 314, 363, 820, 350, 16, 659, 658, 69, 126471, 39, 17, 3896, 19, 12, 60, 3991, 97401, 8663, 25, 658, 69, 314, 220, 16, 68, 2040, 11, 723, 39, 17, 3896, 19, 12, 60, 314, 220, 21, 13, 5170, 68, 12, 18, 871, 658, 69, 126471, 39, 17, 3896, 19, 12, 60, 314, 220, 16, 68, 2040, 425, 220, 21, 13, 5170, 68, 12, 18, 314, 220, 21, 13, 5170, 68, 1157, 364, 84787, 101279, 42308, 230, 220, 21, 13, 5170, 68, 1157, 350, 21910, 4410, 741, 2632, 723, 5563, 18, 143272, 314, 220, 15, 13, 2290, 820, 220, 21, 13, 5170, 68, 1157, 314, 1078, 220, 16, 13, 33488, 68, 12, 2040, 30, 41021, 23864, 25, 220, 15, 13, 2290, 820, 220, 21, 13, 5170, 68, 1157, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36697, 68, 12, 2040, 391, 364, 84787, 2240, 5854, 18, 10, 29212, 175463, 364, 10620, 478, 1706, 302, 25, 457, 314, 457, 15, 659, 350, 15, 13, 47772, 1125, 8, 2142, 5194, 5563, 18, 10, 18500, 58, 5563, 17, 10, 4636, 1919, 723, 5563, 17, 143272, 14777, 220, 15, 13, 2290, 391, 350, 141027, 860, 8012, 387, 741, 2632, 18051, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36697, 68, 12, 2040, 820, 220, 15, 13, 2290, 314, 220, 16, 13, 36697, 68, 12, 858, 364, 2133, 702, 328, 220, 16, 13, 36697, 68, 12, 858, 314, 2142, 702, 7, 16, 13, 36697, 8, 533, 220, 858, 314, 220, 15, 13, 18369, 533, 220, 858, 314, 533, 1157, 13, 44827, 364, 19371, 2914, 314, 220, 15, 13, 47772, 1125, 425, 21382, 1157, 13, 44827, 8, 314, 533, 16, 13, 11999, 631, 33956, 364, 36, 314, 220, 15, 13, 3732, 659, 21382, 16, 13, 11999, 8, 314, 533, 15, 13, 22901, 631, 364, 84787, 1078, 533, 15, 13, 3020, 631, 1118, 15248, 5317, 418, 364, 4383, 25, 10112, 1023, 1199, 945, 31687, 8663, 25, 23864, 220, 15, 13, 47772, 1125, 425, 21382, 2133, 18051, 741, 24305, 478, 1706, 302, 2232, 30, 2214, 5854, 18, 10, 659, 319, 12, 15155, 5854, 17, 76328, 2632, 457, 314, 457, 15, 659, 350, 15, 13, 47772, 1125, 8, 2142, 31338, 5563, 18, 10, 18500, 58, 5563, 17, 10, 21953, 11377, 364, 84787, 6451, 12626, 364, 84787, 6052, 418, 364, 94272, 6011, 13], "n_tokens": 881, "words": 312, "band_lo": 178.25, "band_hi": 713.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to compute redox potential (Eh) for Fe3+/Fe2+ couple considering complex formation of Fe3+ with H2PO4- which reduces free Fe3+ concentration (thus shifting potential). Use Nernst equation: E = E0 + (0.05916/ n) log([Fe3+]/[Fe2+]) at 25°C, n = 1 electron.\n\nGiven total Fe3+ concentration initially 0.01 M, Fe2+ 0.01 M. But after addition of phosphate, Fe3+ partially forms complex Fe(H2PO4)+? Or Fe(H2PO4)2? They said complex formation constant for Fe(III)-H2PO4- is 10^21. Presumably formation: Fe3+ + H2PO4- ⇌ FeH2PO4^2+? Actually charge: Fe3+ + H2PO4- → Fe(H2PO4)2+? That would be Fe3+ + H2PO4- → FeH2PO4^2+. Let's assume 1:1 complex with formation constant Kf = [FeH2PO4^2+]/([Fe3+][H2PO4-]) = 10^21.\n\nThus free Fe3+ concentration is greatly reduced due to binding with H2PO4-.\n\nGiven total phosphate concentration 0.1 M, at pH 1 the equilibrium concentration of H2PO4- ions is 6.97e-3 M (as given). So free H2PO4- = 6.97e-3 M.\n\nWe consider total Fe3+ nominal (unbound) is 0.01 M, but most forms complex. Let free Fe3+ = [Fe3+]. Then complex concentration = [FeH2PO4^2+] = Kf * [Fe3+][H2PO4-].\n\nMass balance for Fe(III) total (let's denote Fe3+ total = C_Fe3,total = 0.01 M) = [Fe3+] + [FeH2PO4^2+].\n\nThus: C = [Fe3+] + Kf*[Fe3+][H2PO4-] = [Fe3+] (1 + Kf*[H2PO4-]).\n\nSolve for [Fe3+]: [Fe3+] = C / (1 + Kf*[H2PO4-]).\n\nPlug numbers: Kf = 1e21, [H2PO4-] = 6.97e-3 => Kf*[H2PO4-] = 1e21 * 6.97e-3 = 6.97e18.\n\nThus denominator ≈ 6.97e18 (since large). So [Fe3+] = 0.01 / 6.97e18 = about 1.435e-21? Let's compute: 0.01 / 6.97e18 = 1.434e-21 M.\n\nThus free Fe3+ essentially negligible.\n\nNow Nernst: E = E0 + (0.05916) log([Fe3+]/[Fe2+]) where [Fe2+] remains 0.01 M (assuming no complexation). So ratio = 1.434e-21 / 0.01 = 1.434e-19.\n\nlog10 of 1.434e-19 = log10(1.434) - 19 = 0.156 - 19 = -18.844.\n\nThen term = 0.05916 * (-18.844) = -1.115 V approx.\n\nE = 0.77 + (-1.115) = -0.345 V.\n\nThus about -0.34 V which matches option B.\n\nCheck: maybe they use more precise numbers: compute 0.05916 * (-log ratio). Wait Nernst sign? For Fe3+ + e- → Fe2+. So E = E0 + (0.05916) log ([Fe3+]/[Fe2+]). Yes.\n\nThus potential negative.\n\nThus answer B.\n\nProvide format.", "response": "ANSWER: B", "answer": "B", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -4.172316494077677e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999826, "logp_correct": -1.7399081261477746e-14, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000175, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.3557456453706026, "cot_lp_min64": -0.8896368079702324, "frac_below_-5": 0.008064516129032258, "digit_lp_min": -1.5125054121017456, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 868, "lp_end": 0.0, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -8.143222356796127, "p_nocot": 0.00029069895162237475, "uplift": 8.143222356796109, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.866561, "B": 0.000291, "C": 0.015872, "D": 0.117276}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recQ8oxSY2aCwFRS8", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: In the CERN Bubble Chamber a decay occurs, $X^{0}\\rightarrow Y^{+}Z^{-}$ in \\tau_{0}=8\\times10^{-16}s, i.e. the proper lifetime of X^{0}. What minimum resolution is needed to observe at least 30% of the decays? Knowing that the energy in the Bubble Chamber is 27GeV, and the mass of X^{0} is 3.41GeV.\n\nA) 2.08*1e-1 m\nB) 2.08*1e-9 m\nC) 2.08*1e-6 m\nD) 2.08*1e-3 m\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: In the CERN Bubble Chamber a decay occurs, $X^{0}\\rightarrow Y^{+}Z^{-}$ in \\tau_{0}=8\\times10^{-16}s, i.e. the proper lifetime of X^{0}. What minimum resolution is needed to observe at least 30% of the decays? Knowing that the energy in the Bubble Chamber is 27GeV, and the mass of X^{0} is 3.41GeV.\n\nA) 2.08*1e-1 m\nB) 2.08*1e-9 m\nC) 2.08*1e-6 m\nD) 2.08*1e-3 m\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recQ8oxSY2aCwFRS8:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 8420, 290, 4792, 25, 730, 194967, 84882, 46466, 11, 261, 57549, 21241, 2127, 15, 2747, 865, 10, 1489, 12, 483, 7937, 24644, 15586, 15, 314, 220, 23, 68, 12, 1125, 265, 13, 19792, 11085, 17365, 316, 31614, 540, 5153, 220, 1130, 4, 328, 290, 1885, 1044, 13, 623, 5954, 306, 290, 40447, 41391, 382, 220, 2092, 5053, 53, 11, 4842, 328, 2127, 15, 382, 220, 18, 13, 4987, 5053, 53, 13, 2632, 581, 679, 35925, 6207, 33875, 483, 121749, 5954, 30, 50557, 3609, 5954, 4335, 30, 63659, 3609, 5954, 350, 36, 8, 314, 220, 2092, 5053, 53, 13, 11271, 4842, 284, 314, 220, 18, 13, 4987, 5053, 53, 4308, 61, 17, 13, 2632, 40570, 314, 457, 5712, 66, 61, 17, 314, 220, 2092, 820, 220, 18, 13, 4987, 42308, 230, 220, 22, 13, 10088, 13, 7801, 1617, 24644, 306, 9887, 7298, 314, 40570, 425, 15586, 15, 314, 220, 22, 13, 10088, 425, 220, 23, 68, 12, 1125, 265, 42308, 230, 220, 21, 13, 30447, 68, 12, 1055, 265, 13, 17081, 484, 1058, 480, 50316, 9324, 451, 314, 323, 425, 260, 119577, 13, 2214, 35925, 6207, 33875, 323, 171441, 66, 350, 21910, 40570, 6574, 23, 741, 2632, 9324, 6574, 274, 425, 260, 119577, 42308, 230, 220, 18, 68, 23, 284, 5031, 425, 220, 21, 13, 30447, 68, 12, 1055, 265, 314, 220, 16, 13, 9752, 23, 68, 12, 21, 284, 42308, 230, 220, 16, 13, 24, 81193, 76, 13, 21926, 4774, 57549, 5517, 350, 33570, 741, 2514, 31614, 540, 5153, 220, 1130, 4, 328, 1885, 1044, 11, 581, 1309, 51124, 17365, 350, 1148, 27267, 8, 2238, 484, 481, 665, 1921, 1885, 1044, 51667, 3518, 484, 9324, 30, 50557, 481, 1309, 316, 14062, 57549, 25363, 39612, 591, 7142, 2438, 13, 47219, 17365, 6118, 10112, 2238, 484, 17365, 72554, 57549, 5517, 425, 220, 15, 13, 18, 30, 3004, 11, 1309, 316, 31614, 540, 5153, 220, 1130, 4, 328, 1885, 1044, 11, 10915, 481, 1757, 413, 3741, 316, 1921, 1885, 1044, 51667, 1934, 26023, 540, 5153, 1236, 9324, 1215, 2238, 484, 34933, 328, 57549, 1934, 26023, 9324, 1424, 1215, 382, 220, 1130, 15678, 623, 34933, 484, 33875, 50316, 945, 1572, 9324, 1215, 2254, 1885, 22983, 382, 2794, 8087, 87, 14, 1727, 8, 1919, 17667, 382, 4774, 57549, 5517, 350, 66, 2244, 8558, 741, 1416, 1682, 398, 11075, 1424, 1215, 8, 314, 220, 15, 13, 1130, 2747, 2794, 8087, 87, 14, 1727, 8, 314, 220, 15, 13, 1130, 871, 1215, 314, 533, 1727, 68859, 7, 15, 13, 1130, 741, 17667, 314, 220, 16, 13, 24, 81193, 76, 13, 45438, 25, 68859, 7, 15, 13, 18, 8, 42308, 230, 533, 16, 13, 14754, 5170, 13, 94868, 2232, 8967, 1215, 314, 17667, 425, 220, 16, 13, 14754, 5170, 314, 220, 16, 13, 24, 81193, 76, 425, 220, 16, 13, 14397, 42308, 230, 220, 17, 13, 2270, 81193, 76, 314, 220, 17, 13, 18, 68, 12, 21, 284, 364, 47214, 2804, 413, 3760, 1572, 495, 9324, 316, 14062, 290, 102009, 25363, 30, 2632, 11085, 17365, 6118, 382, 1078, 220, 17, 13, 18, 68, 12, 21, 284, 13, 22483, 25, 355, 220, 17, 13, 3062, 68, 12, 16, 284, 350, 15, 13, 20021, 284, 936, 418, 220, 17, 13, 3062, 68, 12, 24, 284, 11, 363, 220, 17, 13, 3062, 68, 12, 21, 284, 11, 415, 220, 17, 13, 3062, 68, 12, 18, 284, 13, 5339, 46716, 6574, 17, 13, 3062, 68, 12, 21, 284, 15248, 363, 13, 2632, 6052, 363, 364, 58369, 3503, 30411, 48742, 1402, 75284, 314, 457, 5712, 314, 220, 2092, 820, 220, 18, 13, 4987, 314, 220, 22, 13, 10088, 13, 87584, 24644, 314, 220, 23, 68, 12, 1125, 265, 11, 9887, 24644, 314, 40570, 425, 15586, 15, 314, 220, 21, 13, 30447, 68, 12, 1055, 265, 13, 26319, 57549, 5517, 314, 15772, 2728, 66, 2244, 15, 13, 12265, 323, 6574, 274, 11, 15772, 171441, 16, 11, 813, 17667, 314, 8558, 274, 2244, 15, 314, 220, 22, 13, 10088, 425, 220, 18, 68, 23, 425, 220, 23, 68, 12, 1125, 314, 220, 22, 13, 10088, 425, 220, 17, 13, 19, 68, 12, 22, 30, 24305, 23864, 25, 274, 2244, 15, 314, 220, 18, 68, 23, 425, 220, 23, 68, 12, 1125, 314, 220, 17, 13, 19, 68, 12, 22, 284, 13, 137658, 656, 8558, 28, 22, 13, 10088, 8967, 17667, 314, 220, 16, 13, 9752, 23, 68, 12, 21, 284, 350, 288, 5151, 3991, 10620, 34933, 328, 1885, 22983, 1934, 9324, 272, 382, 2794, 8087, 67, 14, 1727, 741, 27042, 540, 5153, 220, 1130, 4, 328, 1885, 1044, 20395, 11, 10915, 1885, 1044, 1934, 540, 5153, 1236, 120968, 39612, 30, 50557, 581, 1309, 316, 679, 17365, 2238, 484, 581, 665, 1921, 1885, 1044, 484, 5659, 1934, 26023, 1236, 9324, 13, 2514, 1921, 540, 5153, 220, 1130, 4, 328, 1885, 1044, 481, 1309, 316, 11839, 2617, 484, 6410, 540, 5153, 290, 17365, 9324, 26, 34933, 484, 57549, 9324, 1424, 17365, 382, 220, 15, 13, 1130, 13, 2632, 17365, 314, 533, 1727, 68859, 7, 15, 13, 18, 8, 42308, 230, 220, 16, 13, 24, 68, 12, 21, 425, 16, 13, 14397, 314, 220, 17, 13, 2270, 68, 12, 21, 13, 21926, 5263, 316, 220, 17, 13, 3062, 68, 12, 21, 350, 3941, 363, 741, 9700, 364, 84787, 6052, 363, 13], "n_tokens": 889, "words": 403, "band_lo": 159.75, "band_hi": 639.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to parse the problem: In CERN Bubble Chamber, a decay occurs X0 -> Y+ Z- with proper lifetime tau0 = 8e-16 s. Need minimum resolution to observe at least 30% of the decays. The energy in the bubble chamber is 27 GeV, mass of X0 is 3.41 GeV. So we have relativistic particle with kinetic energy? Actually total energy given? Probably total energy (E) = 27 GeV. Rest mass m = 3.41 GeV/c^2. So gamma = E/mc^2 = 27 / 3.41 ≈ 7.92. Then its lifetime in lab frame = gamma * tau0 = 7.92 * 8e-16 s ≈ 6.336e-15 s. During that time it travels distance L = v * t_lab. For relativistic particle v≈c (since gamma ~8). So distance ~ c * t_lab ≈ 3e8 m/s * 6.336e-15 s = 1.9008e-6 m ≈ 1.9 µm. That's mean decay length (average). To observe at least 30% of decays, we need detector resolution (spatial) such that you can see decays occurring within that distance? Actually you need to resolve decay vertex separation from production point. Minimum resolution needed maybe such that resolution ≤ decay length * 0.3? No, need to observe at least 30% of decays, meaning you should be able to see decays occurring after traveling at least some distance x such that probability of decay after traveling distance > x is 30%. The probability that particle travels more than distance x before decaying is exp(-x/λ) where λ is mean decay length (c τ γ). We want P(L > x) = 0.30 -> exp(-x/λ) = 0.30 => x = -λ ln(0.30). λ = 1.9 µm. Compute: ln(0.3) ≈ -1.20397. Negative sign gives x = λ * 1.20397 = 1.9 µm * 1.204 ≈ 2.29 µm = 2.3e-6 m.\n\nResolution must be less than this distance to resolve the displaced vertex? So minimum resolution needed is about 2.3e-6 m. Options: A 2.08e-1 m (0.208 m), B 2.08e-9 m, C 2.08e-6 m, D 2.08e-3 m. Our computed ~2.08e-6 m matches C. So answer C.\n\nLet's double-check calculations:\n\ngamma = E/m = 27 / 3.41 = 7.92. Proper lifetime = 8e-16 s, lab lifetime = gamma * tau0 = 6.336e-15 s. Mean decay length = βγc τ0. Since v ~ c, β≈1, so λ = γ c τ0 = 7.92 * 3e8 * 8e-16 = 7.92 * 2.4e-7? Wait compute: c τ0 = 3e8 * 8e-16 = 2.4e-7 m. Multiply by γ=7.92 gives λ = 1.9008e-6 m (as above).\n\nNow probability of decaying after distance d is exp(-d/λ). Want at least 30% of decays observed, meaning decays after at least some measurable separation? Actually we need to have resolution such that we can see decays that happen after traveling some distance. To see at least 30% of decays you need to detect those that travel at least the resolution distance; probability that decay distance > resolution is 0.30. So resolution = -λ ln(0.3) ≈ 1.9e-6 *1.204 = 2.29e-6. That's close to 2.08e-6 (option C). Good.\n\nThus answer C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -6.794906312279636e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999991, "logp_correct": -9.32245370211204e-16, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000009, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.43674751300117015, "cot_lp_min64": -1.0761232506650682, "frac_below_-5": 0.00228310502283105, "digit_lp_min": -2.4639413356781006, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.03142179548740387, "n_cot_tokens": 876, "lp_end": -2.5987286790041253e-05, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -3.576278118089249e-07, "logp_nocot": -1.5201996704655516, "p_nocot": 0.2186682210074702, "uplift": 1.5201996704655507, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.017949, "B": 0.763227, "C": 0.218668, "D": 0.000155}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recQEFX6mtMj6XQvA", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Consider a Fermi gas of N relativistic electrons, confined as a spherical cloud (of radius R) of uniform mass density. The outward pressure exerted by this gas in the ground state is compensated by the gravitational pressure acting inward. Therefore, in equilibrium, the ground state pressure becomes proportional to a function of the mass M of the gas and the radius R. The form of this function is\n\nA) M/R^3\nB) M/R^2\nC) M^2/R^4\nD) M^2/R^3\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Consider a Fermi gas of N relativistic electrons, confined as a spherical cloud (of radius R) of uniform mass density. The outward pressure exerted by this gas in the ground state is compensated by the gravitational pressure acting inward. Therefore, in equilibrium, the ground state pressure becomes proportional to a function of the mass M of the gas and the radius R. The form of this function is\n\nA) M/R^3\nB) M/R^2\nC) M^2/R^4\nD) M^2/R^3\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recQEFX6mtMj6XQvA:1", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 13001, 1118, 55881, 328, 9890, 350, 2845, 16970, 7949, 8, 70959, 5597, 15481, 9890, 328, 35925, 6207, 100085, 13, 50557, 4792, 25, 6042, 2076, 9890, 591, 35925, 6207, 5597, 15481, 23629, 7322, 350, 6004, 3492, 6207, 454, 33673, 7322, 8, 32879, 656, 152581, 9890, 112749, 13, 2214, 87639, 11, 290, 7740, 2608, 9890, 14081, 99864, 316, 261, 1114, 328, 290, 4842, 391, 326, 21090, 460, 13, 623, 4928, 6960, 31064, 1118, 20483, 73027, 328, 9890, 402, 391, 326, 460, 591, 44967, 364, 3193, 49968, 1953, 9890, 6574, 6049, 777, 3624, 30, 2214, 261, 1051, 18511, 49968, 1365, 51811, 21219, 27591, 11, 152581, 6451, 5954, 6574, 533, 350, 18, 14, 20, 8, 32874, 61, 17, 820, 460, 13, 2502, 49968, 1953, 9890, 350, 267, 7848, 9890, 8, 6574, 66319, 67, 36, 6662, 53, 741, 457, 6574, 533, 30043, 61, 17, 820, 460, 13, 36103, 631, 314, 350, 19, 14, 18, 8, 1345, 460, 61, 18, 13, 2632, 272, 36, 6662, 53, 6574, 350, 67, 36, 6662, 49, 44406, 67, 49, 6662, 53, 741, 41021, 23864, 55881, 25, 457, 6574, 533, 30043, 61, 17, 820, 460, 13, 2632, 272, 36, 6662, 49, 314, 32874, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 17, 13, 272, 53, 6662, 49, 314, 220, 19, 1345, 460, 61, 17, 11, 813, 272, 49, 6662, 53, 314, 220, 16, 27334, 19, 1345, 460, 61, 17, 741, 47682, 9890, 6574, 533, 272, 36, 6662, 53, 314, 533, 350, 30043, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 17, 8, 425, 350, 16, 27334, 19, 1345, 460, 61, 17, 915, 314, 533, 350, 30043, 61, 17, 8, 820, 350, 19, 1345, 460, 61, 19, 741, 2632, 49895, 55881, 6574, 32874, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 19, 364, 84787, 9890, 51599, 472, 391, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 19, 350, 6332, 499, 9594, 741, 32417, 3880, 11, 363, 25, 391, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 19, 13, 2632, 6052, 363, 364, 7943, 2371, 13319, 57927, 25, 152581, 9890, 6574, 152581, 9578, 777, 3624, 540, 9753, 6574, 32874, 220, 1184, 820, 460, 30, 4037, 31687, 13, 3072, 5542, 55881, 395, 6461, 124441, 25, 104507, 3805, 9890, 350, 6004, 3492, 6207, 8, 35353, 251, 297, 32612, 19, 14, 18, 741, 623, 10636, 59684, 391, 35353, 251, 9594, 350, 1205, 104878, 618, 74, 8665, 5967, 741, 623, 55881, 328, 11082, 9890, 6574, 32874, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 19, 13, 41351, 395, 1823, 5240, 75678, 297, 28, 18, 350, 6004, 3492, 6207, 5597, 15481, 7322, 936, 9890, 55881, 382, 6574, 32874, 61, 17, 820, 460, 61, 19, 13, 2632, 6052, 363, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 363, 13], "n_tokens": 447, "words": 212, "band_lo": 131.0, "band_hi": 524.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to decide which scaling of pressure (from gravitation) balancing degenerate pressure of relativistic electrons. Actually problem: Outward pressure from relativistic degenerate electron gas (relativistic Fermi gas) balanced by gravitational pressure inward. For equilibrium, the ground state pressure becomes proportional to a function of the mass M and radius R. The question likely asks which functional dependence of pressure on M and R from gravity.\n\nGravitational pressure ~ weight per area? For a self-gravitating sphere uniform density, gravitational potential energy ~ - (3/5) GM^2 / R. Gravitational pressure (or average pressure) ~ -(dE/dV). E ~ -GM^2 / R. Volume V = (4/3)π R^3. So dE/dV ~ (dE/dR)*(dR/dV). Let's compute scaling: E ~ -GM^2 / R. So dE/dR = GM^2 / R^2. dV/dR = 4π R^2, so dR/dV = 1/(4π R^2). Hence pressure ~ - dE/dV = - (GM^2 / R^2) * (1/(4π R^2)) = - (GM^2) / (4π R^4). So magnitude scaling ~ GM^2 / R^4.\n\nThus pressure scales as M^2 / R^4 (with G constant). Among options, C: M^2 / R^4. So answer C.\n\nBut check alternative reasoning: gravitational pressure ~ gravitational force per area at surface ~ GM ρ / R? Not precise. But known scaling for white dwarf: degeneracy pressure (relativistic) ∝ n^(4/3). The balance yields M ∝ constant (Chandrasekhar limit). The scaling of central pressure ~ GM^2 / R^4. Indeed for polytrope n=3 (relativistic degenerate gas), pressure scaling is ~ GM^2 / R^4. So answer C.\n\nThus answer: ANSWER: C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -2.2291891575321188e-05, "p_correct": 0.999999999999939, "logp_correct": -6.091741010170152e-14, "letter_mass": 0.9999998807907855, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.5816139301199041, "cot_lp_min64": -1.0537799161215897, "frac_below_-5": 0.009216589861751152, "digit_lp_min": -4.541770613286644e-05, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.21026766300201416, "n_cot_tokens": 434, "lp_end": -7.152555099310121e-07, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -2.3841855067985307e-07, "logp_nocot": -0.6935066729980282, "p_nocot": 0.4998202860857906, "uplift": 0.6935066729979672, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 4e-06, "B": 0.000355, "C": 0.49982, "D": 0.49982}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
