{"qid": "recQiVCk4JA9236Nw", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Which of these conditions is associated with an open chromatin state in mouse embryonic stem cells?\n\nA) Hypermethylated DNA at transposable elements\nB) Chromatin associated with PRC1 complexes containing a catalytically inactive Ring1B\nC) PRC2-bound chromatin in cells lacking Ring1B\nD) Chromatin with high levels of trimethylation of histone 3 lysine 9\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Which of these conditions is associated with an open chromatin state in mouse embryonic stem cells?\n\nA) Hypermethylated DNA at transposable elements\nB) Chromatin associated with PRC1 complexes containing a catalytically inactive Ring1B\nC) PRC2-bound chromatin in cells lacking Ring1B\nD) Chromatin with high levels of trimethylation of histone 3 lysine 9\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recQiVCk4JA9236Nw:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 11433, 1118, 7060, 382, 8668, 483, 448, 2494, 33474, 17294, 2608, 306, 14459, 72858, 18294, 22231, 11242, 364, 2167, 679, 3880, 1402, 32, 8, 14431, 34794, 53546, 780, 23224, 540, 1643, 40419, 8632, 1127, 23224, 22725, 76, 53546, 387, 382, 13729, 8668, 483, 12412, 11, 322, 106452, 33474, 17294, 11, 6980, 540, 1643, 1103, 1808, 13, 2632, 625, 2494, 364, 33, 8, 52393, 17294, 8668, 483, 11448, 34, 16, 76136, 15683, 261, 28984, 5240, 2905, 63416, 33432, 16, 33, 1127, 11448, 34, 16, 19857, 106060, 258, 1381, 487, 17, 32, 350, 66, 4722, 52646, 8110, 741, 1843, 63416, 11, 1340, 10389, 183088, 26, 889, 11448, 34, 16, 382, 261, 14600, 43606, 322, 106452, 8012, 11, 12190, 8668, 483, 21126, 33474, 17294, 326, 19546, 5786, 23608, 13, 5551, 11, 28984, 5240, 2905, 63416, 33432, 16, 33, 3572, 64113, 8110, 11, 14836, 20547, 306, 945, 2494, 33474, 17294, 30, 19792, 316, 30890, 23216, 13, 730, 14459, 72789, 82, 11, 11448, 34, 16, 483, 63416, 33432, 16, 33, 350, 52498, 16, 33, 460, 2694, 24104, 107323, 8, 28336, 316, 106060, 5180, 487, 17, 14587, 15970, 11, 1118, 12951, 4376, 306, 945, 2494, 33474, 17294, 540, 28763, 43606, 3783, 6427, 13, 3072, 2928, 11, 11448, 34, 16, 1340, 20436, 334, 12, 431, 8966, 56110, 4324, 30, 4037, 3239, 364, 34, 8, 11448, 34, 17, 105858, 33474, 17294, 306, 11242, 53426, 33432, 16, 33, 1127, 11448, 34, 17, 43426, 487, 18, 42, 2092, 1047, 18, 11, 322, 106452, 13, 1843, 33432, 16, 33, 52107, 11, 11448, 34, 16, 6284, 413, 92607, 26, 1236, 11227, 2356, 11448, 34, 17, 105858, 6427, 1340, 5025, 945, 2494, 5192, 316, 11728, 328, 11448, 34, 16, 139110, 1050, 1976, 13, 5551, 11448, 34, 17, 11238, 1217, 665, 21126, 889, 3760, 13, 30456, 413, 2494, 364, 35, 8, 52393, 17294, 483, 1932, 8374, 328, 19334, 53546, 387, 328, 3124, 690, 220, 18, 78732, 514, 220, 24, 350, 39, 18, 42, 24, 1047, 18, 8, 1127, 487, 18, 42, 24, 1047, 18, 382, 261, 41158, 6988, 511, 17294, 1983, 11, 322, 106452, 364, 84787, 6960, 6052, 382, 418, 503, 363, 364, 34405, 7060, 382, 8668, 483, 2494, 33474, 17294, 2608, 30, 623, 4928, 6960, 591, 261, 71994, 47789, 503, 5966, 3363, 42157, 5846, 13, 623, 8496, 25, 730, 14459, 72789, 82, 11, 11448, 34, 16, 483, 28984, 5240, 2905, 63416, 33432, 16, 33, 15286, 316, 6266, 328, 487, 17, 14587, 15970, 431, 16, 889, 11448, 34, 16, 2928, 665, 1475, 5373, 1050, 1976, 4493, 2893, 3452, 4722, 52646, 9964, 13, 5551, 382, 2494, 30, 165972, 364, 19734, 11, 11448, 34, 17, 105858, 33474, 17294, 306, 11242, 53426, 33432, 16, 33, 1127, 25767, 33432, 16, 33, 11, 11448, 34, 16, 382, 625, 92607, 26, 11448, 34, 17, 665, 2928, 19129, 889, 2935, 11448, 34, 16, 139110, 1050, 1976, 11, 290, 33474, 17294, 1340, 413, 945, 18240, 350, 3843, 741, 1328, 382, 261, 5542, 46487, 25, 11448, 34, 17, 665, 413, 3333, 540, 179996, 11, 889, 66912, 280, 183088, 20102, 402, 11448, 34, 16, 139110, 106060, 3273, 326, 33474, 17294, 1050, 1976, 13, 730, 33432, 16, 33, 154853, 72789, 82, 11, 1991, 34553, 553, 15548, 26974, 11, 34700, 2494, 33474, 17294, 364, 84787, 6052, 6960, 363, 364, 58369, 3503, 30411, 25, 17796, 363, 5003, 392, 8621, 34, 17, 105858, 33474, 17294, 306, 11242, 53426, 33432, 16, 33, 4050, 4569, 1481, 413, 2494, 2236, 33432, 16, 33, 382, 997, 328, 11448, 34, 16, 11, 1118, 28520, 1381, 483, 11448, 34, 17, 316, 21126, 26, 53426, 33432, 16, 33, 11, 11448, 34, 17, 11238, 1340, 625, 9637, 21126, 11, 8117, 316, 945, 2494, 2608, 13, 2632, 6052, 363, 364, 84787, 4733, 392, 160761, 25, 363, 4050], "n_tokens": 626, "words": 389, "band_lo": 152.25, "band_hi": 609.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to determine which condition is associated with an open chromatin state in mouse embryonic stem cells.\n\nWe have options:\n\nA) Hypermethylated DNA at transposable elements – DNA hypermethylation is typically associated with closed, repressive chromatin, especially at transposons. So not open.\n\nB) Chromatin associated with PRC1 complexes containing a catalytically inactive Ring1B – PRC1 normally ubiquitinates H2A (catalytic activity). If inactive, may reduce repression; but PRC1 is a polycomb repressive complex, generally associated with compact chromatin and gene silencing. However, catalytically inactive Ring1B might impair activity, possibly resulting in more open chromatin? Need to recall literature. In mouse ESCs, PRC1 with inactive Ring1B (Ring1B RING finger mutant) fails to ubiquitinate H2AK119, which perhaps results in more open chromatin at Polycomb target sites. But still, PRC1 may recruit de-ubiquitinases? Not sure.\n\nC) PRC2-bound chromatin in cells lacking Ring1B – PRC2 deposits H3K27me3, repressive. If Ring1B absent, PRC1 cannot be recruited; some studies show PRC2-bound sites may become more open due to lack of PRC1-mediated compaction. However PRC2 alone also can compact but less. Could be open.\n\nD) Chromatin with high levels of trimethylation of histone 3 lysine 9 (H3K9me3) – H3K9me3 is a heterochromatin mark, repressive.\n\nThus likely answer is B or C.\n\nWhich condition is associated with open chromatin state? The question likely from a developmental biology or epigenetics exam. The concept: In mouse ESCs, PRC1 with catalytically inactive Ring1B leads to loss of H2AK119ub1 but PRC1 still can mediate compaction via non-catalytic functions. However is open? Hmm.\n\nAlso, PRC2-bound chromatin in cells lacking Ring1B – Without Ring1B, PRC1 is not recruited; PRC2 can still bind but without PRC1-mediated compaction, the chromatin may be more accessible (open). This is a known phenomenon: PRC2 can be present at promoters, but transcriptional repression depends on PRC1-mediated ubiquitination and chromatin compaction. In Ring1B knockout ESCs, many genes are derepressed, indicating open chromatin.\n\nThus answer likely C.\n\nLet's double-check: Option C says \"PRC2-bound chromatin in cells lacking Ring1B\". That would be open because Ring1B is part of PRC1, which cooperates with PRC2 to compact; lacking Ring1B, PRC2 alone may not fully compact, leading to more open state. So answer C.\n\nThus output \"ANSWER: C\".", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -3.695482632792846e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999991119, "logp_correct": -8.880264302785918e-13, "letter_mass": 0.9999995231639572, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.5739660368220028, "cot_lp_min64": -1.2133426864167798, "frac_below_-5": 0.008156606851549755, "digit_lp_min": -1.0406330823898315, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.00047291061491705477, "n_cot_tokens": 613, "lp_end": 0.0, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -1.7028550221215106, "p_nocot": 0.18216270238279772, "uplift": 1.7028550221206227, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.001227, "B": 0.816397, "C": 0.182163, "D": 0.000213}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recQiWOxhkXRz9NVE", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: reaction of solid A with 8 equivalents of gas B forms bright red product C.\nWhen C reacts with 2 equivalents of gas D, it produces the extremely hazardous product E.\nC reacts with water to reform A plus two different acids F and G. F is a strong acid while G is a weak acid.\nD reacts with B in a 1:1 ratio to form H, which is used as a solvent.\n\nwhat is the molecular symmetry group of E?\n\nA) C2\nB) D∞h\nC) C2v\nD) D4h\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: reaction of solid A with 8 equivalents of gas B forms bright red product C.\nWhen C reacts with 2 equivalents of gas D, it produces the extremely hazardous product E.\nC reacts with water to reform A plus two different acids F and G. F is a strong acid while G is a weak acid.\nD reacts with B in a 1:1 ratio to form H, which is used as a solvent.\n\nwhat is the molecular symmetry group of E?\n\nA) C2\nB) D∞h\nC) C2v\nD) D4h\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recQiWOxhkXRz9NVE:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 32043, 290, 72636, 316, 11410, 43556, 355, 11, 418, 11, 363, 11, 415, 11, 457, 11, 454, 11, 499, 11, 487, 13, 7801, 11433, 90882, 3566, 328, 457, 364, 1388, 1406, 25, 35764, 355, 137530, 483, 220, 23, 173691, 328, 7322, 418, 316, 1625, 13712, 3592, 1888, 363, 13, 363, 137530, 483, 220, 17, 173691, 328, 7322, 415, 316, 10635, 11069, 69337, 1888, 457, 13, 363, 1217, 137530, 483, 3411, 316, 20257, 355, 2932, 1920, 2647, 47017, 454, 350, 9851, 8, 326, 499, 350, 33285, 741, 415, 137530, 483, 418, 220, 16, 25, 16, 316, 3644, 487, 11, 261, 65334, 364, 2167, 1309, 2411, 328, 5542, 158587, 38133, 364, 64600, 355, 6960, 261, 11002, 2238, 472, 33790, 30, 220, 23, 173691, 328, 73