183239, 1727, 9, 1179, 92, 314, 220, 16, 533, 350, 68, 183239, 1727, 9, 1353, 9263, 61, 17, 314, 220, 16, 533, 220, 15, 13, 4625, 61, 17, 314, 220, 16, 533, 220, 15, 13, 38302, 19, 314, 220, 15, 13, 37434, 21, 6574, 220, 6798, 13, 23, 4, 30, 24305, 220, 15, 13, 4625, 61, 17, 314, 15, 13, 38302, 19, 11, 813, 220, 16, 12, 314, 15, 13, 37434, 21, 11, 575, 2560, 13, 220, 6798, 13, 23, 4, 30, 50557, 10954, 220, 6798, 13, 7947, 4, 350, 8722, 316, 220, 6733, 64918, 398, 77281, 356, 3518, 220, 1434, 8, 314, 220, 16, 533, 319, 183239, 1727, 9, 1434, 92, 314, 220, 16, 533, 44237, 7, 15, 13, 4625, 8, 2236, 319, 183239, 1727, 9, 1434, 92, 314, 350, 68, 183239, 1727, 9, 1353, 9263, 42923, 16, 14, 17, 92, 314, 44237, 7, 15, 13, 4625, 25987, 15, 13, 49150, 21, 13, 2632, 398, 77281, 356, 3518, 220, 1434, 8, 314, 220, 16, 533, 220, 15, 13, 49150, 21, 314, 220, 15, 13, 16080, 19, 350, 1422, 13, 20, 64918, 7801, 71796, 34933, 314, 350, 15, 13, 37434, 21, 533, 220, 15, 13, 16080, 19, 11876, 15, 13, 49150, 21, 314, 350, 15, 13, 35528, 17, 11876, 15, 13, 49150, 21, 314, 220, 15, 13, 36843, 18, 871, 220, 3336, 36256, 84787, 6052, 363, 364, 84787, 9570, 461, 160761, 25, 363, 6120], "n_tokens": 741, "words": 213, "band_lo": 69.25, "band_hi": 277.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to determine probability that an atom will decay in next 150 minutes given that it has survived 50 minutes, given that overall probability of decaying within 100 minutes is 32%. Assuming exponential decay (memoryless), i.e., constant decay rate λ. Then P(decay within 100 min) = 1 - e^{-λ * 100} = 0.32 => e^{-100 λ} = 0.68 => λ = -(1/100) ln 0.68.\n\nNow we ask probability that it decays in interval (50, 200) minutes? Actually \"in the next 150 minutes\" after the 50 minutes have passed; so from t=50 to t=200 (since 150 after 50). So we need P(decay between 50 and 200 | survived until 50). For exponential, conditional probability = P(decay within 150) = 1 - e^{-λ*150} (memoryless). So compute.\n\nλ = -ln 0.68 /100. Ln(0.68) ~ -0.385662... Let's compute: ln 0.68 = -0.385662... So λ = 0.385662/100 = 0.00385662 per minute.\n\nNow compute 1 - e^{-λ*150} = 1 - exp(-0.00385662*150) = 1 - exp(-0.578493) . exponent: e^{-0.5785} = 0.560. Let's compute: e^{-0.5785} approx = 0.560. So probability = 1 - 0.560 = 0.44, i.e., 44%.\n\nThat matches answer C 44%.\n\nCheck rounding: e^{-0.5785}=0.5606, so 1- =0.4394 => 44% approx.\n\nThus answer C.\n\nBut maybe they consider using formula for conditional probability directly: P(decay in next 150 | survived 50) = (P(decay within 200) - P(decay within 50))/P(survival to 50). For exponential, same result. But we need to compute P(decay within 200) using same λ; we first need λ from given 32% within 100. Then compute.\n\nCompute P(decay within 200) = 1 - e^{-λ*200} = 1 - (e^{-λ*100})^2 = 1 - 0.68^2 = 1 - 0.4624 = 0.5376 ~ 53.8%? Wait 0.68^2 =0.4624, so 1- =0.5376, i.e. 53.8%? Actually that's 53.76% (close to 54%). P(decay within 50) = 1 - e^{-λ*50} = 1 - sqrt(0.68) because e^{-λ*50} = (e^{-λ*100})^{1/2} = sqrt(0.68)=0.8246. So P(decay within 50) = 1 - 0.8246 = 0.1754 (17.5%). Then conditional probability = (0.5376 - 0.1754)/0.8246 = (0.3622)/0.8246 = 0.4393 => 44%.\n\nThus answer C.\n\nThus respond 'ANSWER: C'.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -4.76836109442047e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999961, "logp_correct": -3.907418519281692e-15, "letter_mass": 0.9999997615814816, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.39269352379961375, "cot_lp_min64": -0.7331502942707333, "frac_below_-5": 0.012362637362637362, "digit_lp_min": -2.8119678497314453, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.09099343419075012, "n_cot_tokens": 728, "lp_end": -1.1920928244535389e-07, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -5.014328285876285, "p_nocot": 0.006642092126183816, "uplift": 5.014328285876282, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.003555, "B": 0.985774, "C": 0.006642, "D": 0.004029}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recSjbASPHkgvVsmX", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: To start your new project, you must clone the gene gyrA of Mycobacterium tuberculosis (gene sequence provided below), in order to obtain a recombinant protein fused to a His-tag at the C-Terminus. In the lab, the pET16b and the pET24a plasmids are the only 2 plasmids available. \n\nTo do this, which cloning strategy will you choose?\n\nThe map of the pET16b plasmid is as follows:\nhttps://ecoliwiki.org/colipedia/images/9/92/PET-16b.jpg\n\nThe map of the pET24a plasmid is as follows:\nhttps://ecoliwiki.org/colipedia/images/5/51/PET-24a%28%2B%29.jpg\n\ngyrA sequence: \n\nATGACAGACACGACGTTGCCGCCTGACGACTCGCTCGACCGGATCGAACCGGTTGACATCGAGCAGGAGA\nTGCAGCGCAGCTACATCGACTATGCGATGAGCGTGATCGTCGGCCGCGCGCTGCCGGAGGTGCGCGACGG\nGCTCAAGCCCGTGCATCGCCGGGTGCTCTATGCAATGTTCGATTCCGGCTTCCGCCCGGACCGCAGCCAC\nGCCAAGTCGGCCCGGTCGGTTGCCGAGACCATGGGCAACTACCACCCGCACGGCGACGCGTCGATCTACG\nACAGCCTGGTGCGCATGGCCCAGCCCTGGTCGCTGCGCTACCCGCTGGTGGACGGCCAGGGCAACTTCGG\nCTCGCCAGGCAATGACCCACCGGCGGCGATGAGGTACACCGAAGCCCGGCTGACCCCGTTGGCGATGGAG\nATGCTGAGGGAAATCGACGAGGAGACAGTCGATTTCATCCCTAACTACGACGGCCGGGTGCAAGAGCCGA\nCGGTGCTACCCAGCCGGTTCCCCAACCTGCTGGCCAACGGGTCAGGCGGCATCGCGGTCGGCATGGCAAC\nCAATATCCCGCCGCACAACCTGCGTGAGCTGGCCGACGCGGTGTTCTGGGCGCTGGAGAATCACGACGCC\nGACGAAGAGGAGACCCTGGCCGCGGTCATGGGGCGGGTTAAAGGCCCGGACTTCCCGACCGCCGGACTGA\nTCGTCGGATCCCAGGGCACCGCTGATGCCTACAAAACTGGCCGCGGCTCCATTCGAATGCGCGGAGTTGT\nTGAGGTAGAAGAGGATTCCCGCGGTCGTACCTCGCTGGTGATCACCGAGTTGCCGTATCAGGTCAACCAC\nGACAACTTCATCACTTCGATCGCCGAACAGGTCCGAGACGGCAAGCTGGCCGGCATTTCCAACATTGAGG\nACCAGTCTAGCGATCGGGTCGGTTTACGCATCGTCATCGAGATCAAGCGCGATGCGGTGGCCAAGGTGGT\nGATCAATAACCTTTACAAGCACACCCAGCTGCAGACCAGCTTTGGCGCCAACATGCTAGCGATCGTCGAC\nGGGGTGCCGCGCACGCTGCGGCTGGACCAGCTGATCCGCTATTACGTTGACCACCAACTCGACGTCATTG\nTGCGGCGCACCACCTACCGGCTGCGCAAGGCAAACGAGCGAGCCCACATTCTGCGCGGCCTGGTTAAAGC\nGCTCGACGCGCTGGACGAGGTCATTGCACTGATCCGGGCGTCGGAGACCGTCGATATCGCCCGGGCCGGA\nCTGATCGAGCTGCTCGACATCGACGAGATCCAGGCCCAGGCAATCCTGGACATGCAGTTGCGGCGCCTGG\nCCGCACTGGAACGCCAGCGCATCATCGACGACCTGGCCAAAATCGAGGCCGAGATCGCCGATCTGGAAGA\nCATCCTGGCAAAACCCGAGCGGCAGCGTGGGATCGTGCGCGACGAACTCGCCGAAATCGTGGACAGGCAC\nGGCGACGACCGGCGTACCCGGATCATCGCGGCCGACGGAGACGTCAGCGACGAGGATTTGATCGCCCGCG\nAGGACGTCGTTGTCACTATCACCGAAACGGGATACGCCAAGCGCACCAAGACCGATCTGTATCGCAGCCA\nGAAACGCGGCGGCAAGGGCGTGCAGGGTGCGGGGTTGAAGCAGGACGACATCGTCGCGCACTTCTTCGTG\nTGCTCCACCCACGATTTGATCCTGTTCTTCACCACCCAGGGACGGGTTTATCGGGCCAAGGCCTACGACT\nTGCCCGAGGCCTCCCGGACGGCGCGCGGGCAGCACGTGGCCAACCTGTTAGCCTTCCAGCCCGAGGAACG\nCATCGCCCAGGTCATCCAGATTCGCGGCTACACCGACGCCCCGTACCTGGTGCTGGCCACTCGCAACGGG\nCTGGTGAAAAAGTCCAAGCTGACCGACTTCGACTCCAATCGCTCGGGCGGAATCGTGGCGGTCAACCTGC\nGCGACAACGACGAGCTGGTCGGTGCGGTGCTGTGTTCGGCCGGCGACGACCTGCTGCTGGTCTCGGCCAA\nCGGGCAGTCCATCAGGTTCTCGGCGACCGACGAGGCGCTGCGGCCAATGGGTCGTGCCACCTCGGGTGTG\nCAGGGCATGCGGTTCAATATCGACGACCGGCTGCTGTCGCTGAACGTCGTGCGTGAAGGCACCTATCTGC\nTGGTGGCGACGTCAGGGGGCTATGCGAAACGTACCGCGATCGAGGAATACCCGGTACAGGGCCGCGGCGG\nTAAAGGTGTGCTGACGGTCATGTACGACCGCCGGCGCGGCAGGTTGGTTGGGGCGTTGATTGTCGACGAC\nGACAGCGAGCTGTATGCCGTCACTTCCGGCGGTGGCGTGATCCGCACCGCGGCACGCCAGGTTCGCAAGG\nCGGGACGGCAGACCAAGGGTGTTCGGTTGATGAATCTGGGCGAGGGCGACACACTGTTGGCCATCGCGCG\nCAACGCCGAAGAAAGTGGCGACGATAATGCCGTGGACGCCAACGGCGCAGACCAGACGGGCAATTAA\n\nA) Cloning in the pET16b plasmid between Nde1 and Xho1\nB) Cloning in the pET24a plasmid  between EcoR1 and Xho1\nC) Cloning in the pET24a plasmid  between BamH1 and Xho1\nD) Cloning in the pET16b plasmid between Nco1 and Nde1\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: To start your new project, you must clone the gene gyrA of Mycobacterium tuberculosis (gene sequence provided below), in order to obtain a recombinant protein fused to a His-tag at the C-Terminus. In the lab, the pET16b and the pET24a plasmids are the only 2 plasmids available. \n\nTo do this, which cloning strategy will you choose?\n\nThe map of the pET16b plasmid is as follows:\nhttps://ecoliwiki.org/colipedia/images/9/92/PET-16b.jpg\n\nThe map of the pET24a plasmid is as follows:\nhttps://ecoliwiki.org/colipedia/images/5/51/PET-24a%28%2B%29.jpg\n\ngyrA sequence: \n\nATGACAGACACGACGTTGCCGCCTGACGACTCGCTCGACCGGATCGAACCGGTTGACATCGAGCAGGAGA\nTGCAGCGCAGCTACATCGACTATGCGATGAGCGTGATCGTCGGCCGCGCGCTGCCGGAGGTGCGCGACGG\nGCTCAAGCCCGTGCATCGCCGGGTGCTCTATGCAATGTTCGATTCCGGCTTCCGCCCGGACCGCAGCCAC\nGCCAAGTCGGCCCGGTCGGTTGCCGAGACCATGGGCAACTACCACCCGCACGGCGACGCGTCGATCTACG\nACAGCCTGGTGCGCATGGCCCAGCCCTGGTCGCTGCGCTACCCGCTGGTGGACGGCCAGGGCAACTTCGG\nCTCGCCAGGCAATGACCCACCGGCGGCGATGAGGTACACCGAAGCCCGGCTGACCCCGTTGGCGATGGAG\nATGCTGAGGGAAATCGACGAGGAGACAGTCGATTTCATCCCTAACTACGACGGCCGGGTGCAAGAGCCGA\nCGGTGCTACCCAGCCGGTTCCCCAACCTGCTGGCCAACGGGTCAGGCGGCATCGCGGTCGGCATGGCAAC\nCAATATCCCGCCGCACAACCTGCGTGAGCTGGCCGACGCGGTGTTCTGGGCGCTGGAGAATCACGACGCC\nGACGAAGAGGAGACCCTGGCCGCGGTCATGGGGCGGGTTAAAGGCCCGGACTTCCCGACCGCCGGACTGA\nTCGTCGGATCCCAGGGCACCGCTGATGCCTACAAAACTGGCCGCGGCTCCATTCGAATGCGCGGAGTTGT\nTGAGGTAGAAGAGGATTCCCGCGGTCGTACCTCGCTGGTGATCACCGAGTTGCCGTATCAGGTCAACCAC\nGACAACTTCATCACTTCGATCGCCGAACAGGTCCGAGACGGCAAGCTGGCCGGCATTTCCAACATTGAGG\nACCAGTCTAGCGATCGGGTCGGTTTACGCATCGTCATCGAGATCAAGCGCGATGCGGTGGCCAAGGTGGT\nGATCAATAACCTTTACAAGCACACCCAGCTGCAGACCAGCTTTGGCGCCAACATGCTAGCGATCGTCGAC\nGGGGTGCCGCGCACGCTGCGGCTGGACCAGCTGATCCGCTATTACGTTGACCACCAACTCGACGTCATTG\nTGCGGCGCACCACCTACCGGCTGCGCAAGGCAAACGAGCGAGCCCACATTCTGCGCGGCCTGGTTAAAGC\nGCTCGACGCGCTGGACGAGGTCATTGCACTGATCCGGGCGTCGGAGACCGTCGATATCGCCCGGGCCGGA\nCTGATCGAGCTGCTCGACATCGACGAGATCCAGGCCCAGGCAATCCTGGACATGCAGTTGCGGCGCCTGG\nCCGCACTGGAACGCCAGCGCATCATCGACGACCTGGCCAAAATCGAGGCCGAGATCGCCGATCTGGAAGA\nCATCCTGGCAAAACCCGAGCGGCAGCGTGGGATCGTGCGCGACGAACTCGCCGAAATCGTGGACAGGCAC\nGGCGACGACCGGCGTACCCGGATCATCGCGGCCGACGGAGACGTCAGCGACGAGGATTTGATCGCCCGCG\nAGGACGTCGTTGTCACTATCACCGAAACGGGATACGCCAAGCGCACCAAGACCGATCTGTATCGCAGCCA\nGAAACGCGGCGGCAA