68, 11, 1118, 382, 2061, 395, 363, 155991, 7792, 306, 275, 2175, 1494, 64, 30, 50557, 275, 2175, 1494, 64, 6664, 363, 155991, 7792, 1934, 2127, 1555, 40, 26, 1604, 26163, 263, 382, 5181, 656, 19546, 8807, 350, 1228, 38, 8, 1934, 478, 613, 40, 2702, 13, 2632, 1340, 28806, 2870, 478, 613, 40, 326, 2127, 1555, 40, 306, 275, 2175, 1494, 64, 13, 5551, 10954, 625, 448, 5317, 13, 22483, 1606, 3644, 49394, 18164, 46252, 1555, 40, 11, 106559, 36525, 46252, 1555, 40, 11, 478, 1191, 40, 13833, 613, 40, 350, 79, 2175, 1125, 65, 741, 2632, 6960, 6052, 382, 418, 503, 363, 13, 21580, 1001, 30005, 478, 12, 26821, 385, 6664, 11503, 38, 30, 623, 19546, 4279, 853, 11503, 38, 11, 889, 538, 581, 6092, 483, 49394, 18164, 540, 220, 20, 6, 1268, 11, 581, 1481, 1309, 316, 1147, 11503, 38, 10112, 12486, 30, 623, 19546, 1604, 382, 11503, 38, 11, 889, 1934, 49394, 18164, 2702, 481, 1481, 679, 19546, 8601, 483, 11503, 38, 1934, 49394, 18164, 2702, 26, 290, 9727, 1340, 679, 261, 21649, 57339, 17156, 2702, 78314, 328, 49394, 18164, 13, 21926, 8975, 13, 363, 155991, 7792, 738, 413, 1934, 2127, 1555, 40, 364, 19734, 1309, 316, 8397, 8812, 49394, 18164, 503, 106559, 36525, 6427, 13, 23584, 2371, 395, 49394, 18164, 34221, 1228, 12447, 25, 53387, 6047, 25, 83768, 38, 1228, 17879, 51, 34415, 625, 13, 357, 1921, 83768, 16328, 1228, 34415, 10112, 3333, 25, 540, 392, 43469, 38, 8857, 1228, 17879, 2436, 38, 2971, 38, 2971, 34415, 1354, 382, 392, 32, 1228, 17879, 4050, 4037, 13, 52762, 1151, 860, 49394, 18164, 13, 2214, 106559, 36525, 103779, 1228, 4433, 10112, 52107, 13, 2632, 2973, 4149, 364, 34405, 9727, 997, 6664, 363, 155991, 7792, 30, 730, 275, 2175, 1494, 64, 11, 290, 7792, 76739, 382, 1934, 290, 2127, 1555, 40, 2702, 11, 625, 1934, 49394, 18164, 13, 2632, 158581, 316, 2127, 1555, 40, 540, 220, 18, 6, 30005, 6221, 13, 623, 220, 20, 6, 2702, 665, 413, 49394, 18164, 503, 106559, 36525, 26, 2973, 78314, 328, 6221, 13, 25151, 49394, 18164, 350, 33, 8, 472, 4275, 5355, 364, 84787, 6052, 6960, 418, 13], "n_tokens": 1215, "words": 776, "band_lo": 432.75, "band_hi": 1731.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to pick cloning strategy to get C-terminal His-tag. pET16b provides N-terminal His-tag? Let's recall: pET16b includes N-terminal His6 tag and maybe TEV cleavage site. It has NdeI at start codon and XhoI downstream. In pET16b, the His-tag is N-terminal after the start codon? Actually pET16b features an N-terminal His-tag followed by a thrombin cleavage site and then multiple cloning site (NdeI, BamHI, EcoRI, etc) and C-terminal stop codon? Not sure. pET24a includes C-terminal His-tag (a sequence after the insert). Yes pET24a is designed for C-terminal His-tag (has a downstream sequence coding for 6xHis after the XhoI site maybe). So they want C-terminal His-tag. Also need to avoid internal NdeI or other. Let's examine gyrA sequence start: ATG ACAGAC ... start codon ATG is present. We need to clone the gene without its own stop codon? The sequence likely continues but we have full ORF? It seems to have no stop codon at end (no TAA/TAG/TGA). The last codons: ...GCCA... etc not sure. So we might need to clone into vector without stop codon to fuse with His-tag. In pET24a, the C-terminal His-tag is after XhoI site (maybe after the insert). So we need to cut the gene at appropriate sites: EcoRI? BamHI? Need to have no internal site. Check for EcoRI (GAATTC) in gene? scanning quickly: maybe there is GAATTC at positions e.g., \"GATGAGGTACACCGAAGCCCGG...\" Not see. But could exist. For simplicity, the answer: choose pET24a between EcoRI and XhoI (option B) if EcoRI site not present in gene. Option C BamHI to XhoI. Need to see if BamHI (GGATCC) present; I see \"GGATCGAAC\" early includes \"GGATCG\" not BamHI; later \"GGATCC\" maybe present? Need quick check: scanning: I see \"GGATCC\" at start? The first few: \"...CGGATCGAAC...\" that's G GAT CG; BamHI is GGATCC, need GGATCC exactly. Not present early. Later maybe. Not sure. But pET24a includes a C-terminal His-tag after XhoI site, while EcoRI site is upstream of NdeI? Let's refer to pET24a map: It has NdeI at start codon? Actually pET24a does not have N-terminal tag; it has NdeI, BamHI, EcoRI, XhoI etc. The C-terminal His-tag coding sequence is after XhoI and before the stop? The cloning site is often NdeI (ATG) to XhoI to get C-terminal tag after XhoI (in-frame). So you would clone gene between NdeI and XhoI to have C-terminal tag after XhoI? However pET24a may have sequence for 6xHis downstream of XhoI but before stop. So if you insert gene with NdeI at start and XhoI at end, you can get C-terminal His. Option B says EcoRI-XhoI; that would put gene after EcoRI (upstream) maybe not including start. Might need NdeI for start codon. Option C BamHI-XhoI similar. Option D NcoI and NdeI is weird. Option A NdeI-XhoI in pET16b would give N-terminal His (since pET16b has N-terminus tag before MCS). So not suitable. Thus must use pET24a for C-terminal tag. Which restriction pair is appropriate for start codon inclusion and no internal sites? Most common: NdeI (ATG) at start, XhoI at end, which is used for C-terminal His in pET24a? Actually pET24a includes C-terminal His after XhoI; start codon is provided by gene itself (ATG) after NdeI site. So may clone between NdeI and XhoI in pET24a. However that's not an option. Options only give EcoRI-XhoI, BamHI-XhoI, NcoI-NdeI (pET16b). So likely answer is B or C. Which one ensures N-terminus includes ATG? The gene already has ATG, but if we cut with EcoRI at 5' end, we would need to add ATG maybe missing? The gene start is ATG, but after EcoRI site you would have gene starting with ATG after EcoRI site; the vector may have a ribosome binding site upstream of EcoRI. That's fine. C-terminal His will be after XhoI.\n\nAlso need to avoid internal EcoRI or BamHI sites. Quick check for EcoRI GAATTC: scanning early: \"...GATCGT...\" not. I see \"...GAAT...\" maybe present: at \"GGGAAATCGACGAGGAG...\" there is \"AATCG\". Not. Likely no EcoRI. For BamHI GGATCC maybe absent. So both possible.\n\nWhich vector part includes C-terminal His? In pET24a, the His-tag is after the XhoI site, not after EcoRI. So cloning to XhoI at 3' ensures tag. The 5' site can be EcoRI or BamHI; both upstream of tag. Choose EcoRI (B) as it's common.\n\nThus answer likely B.", "response": "ANSWER: B", "answer": "B", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.311301673467824e-06, "p_correct": 0.999999999999596, "logp_correct": -4.039601489888556e-13, "letter_mass": 0.9999996423726562, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 1.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.8058025082529644, "cot_lp_min64": -1.262976414133334, "frac_below_-5": 0.015806988352745424, "digit_lp_min": -1.711119294166565, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 1202, "lp_end": -1.537788011773955e-05, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -2.128025973539299, "p_nocot": 0.11907211350884667, "uplift": 2.128025973538895, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.87983, "B": 0.119072, "C": 0.000295, "D": 0.000802}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recTVnk0jyigx3o9P", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: m-toluidine and hexane-2,4-dione are heated in the presence of acid. In the ensuing reaction how many organic products can form?\n\nA) 3\nB) 1\nC) 4\nD) 2\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: m-toluidine and hexane-2,4-dione are heated in the presence of acid. In the ensuing reaction how many organic products can form?\n\nA) 3\nB) 1\nC) 4\nD) 2\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recTVnk0jyigx3o9P:0", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 30532, 290, 21416, 25, 284, 2378, 340, 3551, 514, 350, 16151, 30, 50557, 284, 2378, 340, 3551, 514, 382, 220, 18, 2126, 1068, 49801, 41887, 11, 448, 448, 41887, 483, 261, 101385, 540, 14732, 4010, 741, 56318, 1986, 12, 17, 11, 19, 2469, 4655, 382, 261, 174175, 690, 350, 3583, 18, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 18, 81192, 24305, 26157, 1986, 12, 17, 11, 19, 2469, 4655, 382, 10049, 18, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 3583, 18, 30, 50557, 26157, 1986, 12, 17, 11, 19, 2469, 4655, 25, 7429, 15883, 13464, 483, 15883, 3643, 82, 540, 15897, 220, 17, 326, 220, 19, 13, 52074, 25, 10049, 18, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 3583, 18, 30, 41021, 6174, 25, 363, 16, 10049, 18, 11, 363, 17, 314, 10271, 11, 363, 18, 10049, 17, 11, 363, 19, 314, 10271, 11, 363, 20, 10049, 17, 11, 363, 21, 10049, 18, 13, 2632, 350, 3583, 18, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 8310, 12, 3583, 17, 12, 3583, 18, 741, 1328, 382, 261, 220, 16, 11, 18, 2469, 74367, 690, 6771, 316, 68232, 3643, 86583, 690, 889, 17290, 364, 637, 14324, 328, 18655, 11, 284, 2378, 340, 3551, 514, 350, 270, 448, 41887, 8, 665, 57190, 146415, 483, 290, 174175, 690, 316, 3644, 770, 514, 1858, 741, 138743, 6986, 17644, 1340, 7075, 12676, 313, 114688, 27789, 2860, 316, 10635, 64374, 1233, 130036, 82552, 30, 50557, 21416, 328, 293, 84169, 19311, 3303, 295, 5866, 514, 483, 220, 16, 11, 17, 2469, 74367, 3617, 8967, 64374, 1233, 280, 2028, 13, 3072, 2105, 4275, 448, 448, 41887, 350, 144564, 37701, 2081, 8, 483, 261, 220, 16, 11, 18, 2469, 74367, 690, 11, 12951, 8117, 316, 469, 19980, 18704, 30, 30456, 413, 18704, 328, 448, 311, 617, 11, 4149, 18704, 328, 1920, 770, 514, 260, 24028, 409, 2236, 1354, 553, 1920, 15883, 3643, 8896, 350, 17, 326, 220, 19, 741, 2632, 290, 939, 514, 665, 4664, 1603, 483, 4784, 15883, 3643, 316, 3644, 448, 770, 514, 350, 14948, 4443, 3611, 741, 25563, 11, 18655, 665, 28984, 88, 1547, 1051, 12, 5956, 340, 146415, 328, 290, 174175, 690, 30, 3072, 4928, 6960, 1078, 4149, 19448, 3891, 591, 98785, 147657, 25, 350, 16, 8, 4871, 146415, 1888, 350, 14948, 4443, 3611, 8, 540, 363, 17, 11, 350, 17, 8, 146415, 540, 363, 19, 11, 350, 18, 8, 10112, 27789, 2860, 316, 1625, 1320, 23498, 298, 41158, 432, 13317, 350, 9995, 1383, 1491, 30, 4037, 483, 448, 41887, 741, 20064, 1481, 413, 52756, 2860, 30, 165972, 364, 26070, 413, 484, 290, 21416, 11526, 261, 64374, 1233, 130036, 538, 481, 679, 261, 14315, 514, 11, 889, 581, 679, 1606, 69244, 12, 19980, 11, 813, 10112, 1888, 382, 261, 220, 17, 12, 149737, 12, 18, 2126, 53546, 12, 20, 4559, 123753, 6077, 12, 33110, 4037, 3239, 364, 34013, 1023, 3810, 2086, 328, 19448, 3891, 4149, 17227, 290, 15897, 328, 101385, 22148, 11823, 350, 11154, 8, 15001, 316, 21416, 2702, 30, 730, 284, 2378, 340, 3551, 514, 11, 290, 52438, 3566, 382, 540, 4010, 220, 16, 11, 101385, 540, 4010, 220, 18, 15001, 316, 48198, 17, 350, 9995, 14732, 741, 4296, 144217, 483, 220, 17, 11, 19, 12, 22803, 113257, 4655, 11, 481, 665, 679, 146415, 540, 4784, 15883, 3643, 350, 38397, 31061, 741, 7801, 1934, 146415, 11, 290, 1888, 2023, 71613, 22516, 750, 316, 469, 19980, 10217, 770, 514, 11526, 350, 38397, 260, 24028, 409, 741, 2632, 3609, 10112, 220, 19, 364, 58369, 3331, 25, 129157, 2870, 448, 41887, 326, 220, 16, 11, 18, 2469, 74367, 690, 1641, 18655, 8967, 448, 311, 617, 350, 149737, 12, 6331, 2469, 74367, 690, 770, 514, 741, 623, 1888, 382, 448, 770, 514, 1118, 665, 4310, 306, 1920, 11526, 25, 56048, 12, 19980, 350, 262, 19980, 8, 10217, 770, 514, 350, 34, 143132, 741, 220, 16, 11, 18, 2469, 74367, 690, 665, 71613, 22516, 750, 26, 1934, 146415, 481, 717, 448, 469, 19980, 350, 34, 10050, 3503, 15135, 741, 2632, 1920, 260, 24028, 409, 12951, 364, 84787, 31061, 25, 350, 64, 8, 146415, 540, 363, 17, 350, 140932, 770, 514, 540, 15883, 3643, 220, 17, 8, 483, 71613, 22516, 350, 262, 19980, 741, 350, 65, 8, 146415, 540, 363, 19, 483, 71613, 22516, 350, 262, 19980, 741, 4569, 382, 220, 19, 3891, 13, 2632, 6052, 10112, 220, 19, 364, 8093, 363, 350, 19, 741, 41021, 8737, 364], "n_tokens": 752, "words": 397, "band_lo": 198.5, "band_hi": 794.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to analyze the reaction: m-toluidine (para? Actually m-toluidine is 3-methylaniline, an aniline with a methyl at meta position). Hexane-2,4-dione is a diketone (CH3-CO-CH2-CO-CH3?). Wait hexane-2,4-dione is CH3-CO-CH2-CO-CH2-CH3? Actually hexane-2,4-dione: six carbon chain with carbonyls at positions 2 and 4. Structure: CH3-CO-CH2-CO-CH2-CH3? Let's draw: C1 CH3, C2 = CO, C3 CH2, C4 = CO, C5 CH2, C6 CH3. So (CH3-CO-CH2-CO-CH2-CH3). This is a 1,3-diketone similar to acetylacetone but extended.\n\nIn presence of acid, m-toluidine (an aniline) can undergo condensation with the diketone to give imine(s). Possibly Acidity may cause intramolecular cyclization to produce quinoxaline derivatives? Actually reaction of o-phenylenediamine with 1,2-diketones gives quinoxalines. But here it's an aniline (mono-amino) with a 1,3-diketone, perhaps leading to enamine formation? Could be formation of anilide, possible formation of two imine tautomers because there are two carbonyl groups (2 and 4). So the amine can condense with either carbonyl to give an imine (Schiff base). Additionally, acid can catalyze self-aldol condensation of the diketone? But question likely about possible organic products from rearrangements: (1) initial condensation product (Schiff base) at C2, (2) condensation at C4, (3) maybe cyclization to form dihydro heterocycle (like indole? Not with aniline). Another would be polymerization? Hmm.\n\nCould be that the reaction forms a quinoxaline if you have a diamine, but we have only mono-amine, so maybe product is a 2-aryl-3-methyl-5-hydroxy-??? Not sure.\n\nMaybe they ask number of organic products possible considering the positions of methyl substituent (meta) relative to reaction site? In m-toluidine, the amino group is at position 1, methyl at position 3 relative to NH2 (like meta). When reacting with 2,4-hexanedione, you can have condensation at either carbonyl (two possibilities). Then after condensation, the product could tautomerize to enamine vs imine forms (two tautomers). So total maybe 4.\n\nLet's consider: Reaction between aniline and 1,3-diketone under acid gives anilide (aryl-β-diketone imine). The product is an imine which can exist in two forms: keto-amine (enamine) vs imine (C=N). 1,3-diketone can tautomerize; after condensation you get an enamine (C-C double bond). So two tautomers perhaps.\n\nThus possibilities: (a) condensation at C2 (giving imine at carbonyl 2) with tautomer (enamine). (b) condensation at C4 with tautomer (enamine). That is 4 products. So answer maybe 4.\n\nOption C (4). Let's commit.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -5.018585216021165e-05, "p_correct": 0.999999999999978, "logp_correct": -2.2026760714381907e-14, "letter_mass": 1.000000000000022, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.7093947731994277, "cot_lp_min64": -1.275467091364494, "frac_below_-5": 0.02435723951285521, "digit_lp_min": -1.8045384883880615, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.0072637987323105335, "n_cot_tokens": 739, "lp_end": -0.2846095561981201, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -2.625200287546922, "p_nocot": 0.07242524970588256, "uplift": 2.6252002875468996, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.88232, "B": 0.001327, "C": 0.072425, "D": 0.043928}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recUAzHaz2w1b1Ih8", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Quasar A with a bolometric flux of 10^-25 W/m^2 is observed at a redshift of z=0.06 . Quasar B with bolometric flux of 10^-24 W/m^2 is observed at redshift of z=0.02. Assume that the accretion of their central black hole is Eddington limited. Find the ratio of the mass of their central black hole, MA/MB?\n\nA) 0.9\nB) 0.1\nC) 0.7\nD) 0.3\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Quasar A with a bolometric flux of 10^-25 W/m^2 is observed at a redshift of z=0.06 . Quasar B with bolometric flux of 10^-24 W/m^2 is observed at redshift of z=0.02. Assume that the accretion of their central black hole is Eddington limited. Find the ratio of the mass of their central black hole, MA/MB?\n\nA) 0.9\nB) 0.1\nC) 0.7\nD) 0.3\n", "true_answer": "A", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recUAzHaz2w1b1Ih8:1", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 4842, 18051, 4335, 36547, 326, 3592, 27472, 11, 49328, 457, 1183, 8303, 9913, 13, 2632, 82370, 536, 451, 314, 220, 19, 1345, 272, 4258, 61, 17, 425, 285, 350, 4143, 34114, 36547, 741, 2214, 91631, 1904, 540, 4465, 3592, 27472, 11, 82370, 536, 9324, 33956, 272, 4258, 314, 350, 66, 37632, 15, 8, 425, 579, 350, 366, 579, 3291, 11, 68244, 158298, 741, 7649, 2684, 487, 15, 395, 2973, 11, 274, 2684, 11, 813, 272, 4258, 99864, 316, 579, 13, 7801, 451, 35353, 251, 285, 425, 579, 61, 17, 350, 21910, 272, 4258, 61, 17, 35353, 251, 579, 61, 17, 741, 2632, 451, 6829, 820, 451, 3201, 314, 350, 69, 6829, 820, 285, 3201, 8, 425, 350, 89, 6829, 820, 579, 3201, 73602, 17, 364, 39520, 285, 6829, 314, 220, 16, 68, 12, 1161, 11, 285, 3201, 314, 220, 16, 68, 12, 1494, 871, 18051, 285, 6829, 11502, 3201, 314, 220, 15, 13, 16, 13, 579, 6829, 28, 15, 13, 3218, 11, 579, 3201, 28, 15, 13, 3286, 871, 18051, 579, 6829, 61176, 3201, 314, 220, 18, 13, 2632, 350, 89, 6829, 61176, 3201, 73602, 17, 314, 24, 13, 7801, 451, 6829, 26049, 3201, 314, 15, 13, 16, 9, 24, 314, 15, 13, 24, 364, 9095, 37628, 457, 1183, 8303, 2887, 74176, 25, 451, 314, 451, 6584, 1183, 314, 350, 16, 13, 2109, 68, 2911, 486, 8, 425, 350, 44, 17712, 41133, 741, 2632, 451, 35353, 251, 391, 13, 47682, 391, 6829, 17712, 3201, 314, 451, 6829, 26049, 3201, 314, 220, 15, 13, 24, 364, 84787, 6052, 355, 8, 220, 15, 13, 24, 364, 4383, 14494, 25, 355, 8, 220, 15, 13, 24, 15248, 364, 84787, 4733, 6011, 25, 163814, 866, 25, 355, 13], "n_tokens": 299, "words": 136, "band_lo": 75.25, "band_hi": 301.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need mass ratio given flux and redshift, assuming Eddington limited. So luminosity L = 4π d_L^2 * f (bolometric flux). For quasars at low redshift, luminosity distance approx d_L = (c/H0) * z (if z small, ignoring curvature). Use same H0 for both, c same, so d_L proportional to z. Then L ∝ f * z^2 (since d_L^2 ∝ z^2). So L_A / L_B = (f_A / f_B) * (z_A / z_B)^2.\n\nGiven f_A = 1e-25, f_B = 1e-24 => ratio f_A/f_B = 0.1. z_A=0.06, z_B=0.02 => ratio z_A/z_B = 3. So (z_A/z_B)^2 =9. Then L_A/L_B =0.1*9 =0.9.\n\nAssuming Eddington-limited: L = L_Edd = (1.26e31 W) * (M/Msun). So L ∝ M. Hence M_A/M_B = L_A/L_B = 0.9.\n\nThus answer A) 0.9.\n\nCheck choices: A) 0.9 matches.\n\nThus output format: ANSWER: A.", "response": "ANSWER: A", "answer": "A", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -4.172316494077677e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999998366, "logp_correct": -1.6344073107834652e-13, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000001634, "p_letters": {"A": 1.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.3258591055560733, "cot_lp_min64": -0.5764370913395459, "frac_below_-5": 0.006993006993006993, "digit_lp_min": -1.5019326210021973, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.0775856301188469, "n_cot_tokens": 286, "lp_end": -5.960462772236497e-07, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -2.3674510927533183, "p_nocot": 0.09371930390564714, "uplift": 2.367451092753155, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.093719, "B": 0.889184, "C": 0.000811, "D": 0.016286}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recUVWz7kU1KFTc5G", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: There is a C-NOT gate where the condition is that the first qubit of control has to be in the state \\left|0\\right\\rangle.\n\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\left(\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle\n\nis the input of this C-NOT gate. What is the output?\n\nPS: use a LaTeX editor for the maths. For example, the input of the C-NOT gate is |psi>= (alpha |0>+ beta |1> + gamma |1>) \\tensorproduct |0>\n\nA) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle \\varotimes\\left|1\\right\\rangle +\\left(\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle\nB) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\left(\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle\nC) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle \\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\left(\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|1\\right\\rangle\nD) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\left(\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|1\\right\\rangle\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: There is a C-NOT gate where the condition is that the first qubit of control has to be in the state \\left|0\\right\\rangle.\n\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\left(\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle\n\nis the input of this C-NOT gate. What is the output?\n\nPS: use a LaTeX editor for the maths. For example, the input of the C-NOT gate is |psi>= (alpha |0>+ beta |1> + gamma |1>) \\tensorproduct |0>\n\nA) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle \\varotimes\\left|1\\right\\rangle +\\left(\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle\nB) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\left(\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle\nC) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle \\varotimes\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\left(\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|1\\right\\rangle\nD) U_{C-NOT}\\left|\\psi\\right\\rangle =\\left(\\alpha\\left|0\\right\\rangle +\\beta\\left|1\\right\\rangle -\\gamma\\left|1\\right\\rangle \\right)\\varotimes\\left|1\\right\\rangle\n", "true_answer": "A", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recUVWz7kU1KFTc5G:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 8420, 290, 4792, 13, 363, 13833, 2824, 27172, 1919, 7060, 382, 484, 290, 1577, 474, 6516, 328, 3580, 853, 316, 413, 306, 2608, 1022, 15, 34397, 44130, 363, 24820, 25, 1843, 3580, 382, 1022, 16, 17084, 169694, 3783, 13, 3072, 2105, 7060, 382, 1577, 474, 6516, 2804, 413, 1022, 15, 29, 316, 29130, 30, 50557, 1023, 2891, 392, 34, 13833, 2824, 27172, 1919, 290, 7060, 382, 484, 290, 1577, 474, 6516, 328, 3580, 853, 316, 413, 306, 290, 2608, 1022, 15, 142855, 4569, 4748, 4275, 261, 3580, 402, 1022, 15, 29, 7542, 1572, 1022, 16, 34397, 2632, 290, 9506, 382, 25, 1843, 3580, 314, 1022, 15, 17084, 6096, 7116, 316, 3783, 26, 538, 3580, 314, 1022, 16, 17084, 621, 6939, 13, 21926, 10069, 4358, 261, 23006, 13833, 2824, 483, 3580, 402, 12421, 11, 1786, 23990, 363, 24820, 62, 15, 364, 3275, 2608, 25, 147161, 37764, 29, 314, 350, 727, 91, 15, 29, 659, 15772, 91, 16, 29, 533, 8558, 91, 16, 17991, 2969, 232, 245, 1022, 15, 34397, 12225, 1354, 382, 261, 28597, 25, 15772, 91, 16, 29, 533, 8558, 91, 16, 29, 21700, 316, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 47976, 16, 34397, 3072, 10112, 1023, 36988, 2647, 9571, 30, 41021, 50059, 25, 350, 727, 91, 15, 29, 659, 15772, 91, 16, 29, 533, 8558, 91, 16, 17991, 314, 3793, 91, 15, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 47976, 16, 34397, 2632, 290, 2608, 402, 1577, 474, 6516, 382, 3793, 91, 15, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 47976, 16, 34397, 197203, 364, 7889, 474, 6516, 25998, 1022, 15, 34397, 28921, 9506, 25, 538, 1577, 474, 6516, 382, 1022, 15, 17084, 29130, 3783, 316, 1022, 16, 34397, 1843, 1577, 474, 6516, 382, 1022, 16, 17084, 7668, 3783, 472, 1022, 15, 34397, 2632, 4733, 25, 3793, 91, 15, 29, 159042, 245, 91, 16, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 8, 1022, 16, 29, 159042, 245, 91, 15, 34397, 21926, 3793, 91, 15, 56629, 16, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 47976, 16, 56629, 15, 34397, 38200, 316, 3880, 364, 8093, 355, 25, 3793, 91, 15, 29, 159042, 245, 91, 16, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 91, 16, 29, 533, 8558, 91, 16, 17991, 159042, 245, 91, 15, 29, 314, 3793, 91, 15, 56629, 16, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 47976, 16, 56629, 15, 34397, 4569, 15248, 0, 17796, 355, 364, 8093, 363, 25, 3793, 91, 15, 56629, 15, 29, 659, 350, 6331, 12, 2728, 8, 1022, 16, 56629, 16, 29, 860, 364, 84787, 6052, 355, 364, 4383, 1273, 39682, 1206, 25, 10112, 1023, 19429, 7024, 363, 24820, 1919, 3580, 402, 1022, 16, 34397, 3164, 2059, 7060, 382, 1577, 474, 6516, 328, 3580, 853, 316, 413, 306, 2608, 1022, 15, 34397, 2632, 4275, 3580, 402, 12421, 13, 9700, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 355, 13], "n_tokens": 477, "words": 197, "band_lo": 96.5, "band_hi": 386.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to parse the problem. C-NOT gate where condition is that the first qubit of control has to be in state |0>. Usually CNOT: If control is |1>, flips target. But here condition is first qubit must be |0> to flip? Actually they say \"C-NOT gate where the condition is that the first qubit of control has to be in the state |0>\". That means it's a control on |0> rather than |1>. So the operation is: If control = |0>, apply NOT to target; if control = |1>, do nothing. That's sometimes called a controlled-NOT with control on zero, denoted CNOT_0.\n\nInput state: |\\psi> = (α|0> + β|1> - γ|1>) ⊗ |0>. Note there is a mistake: β|1> - γ|1> combine to (β-γ)|1>. But maybe they intend different basis? Let's rewrite: (α|0> + β|1> - γ|1>) = α|0> + (β-γ)|1>. So the state on first qubit is α|0> + (β-γ)|1>. Equivalent.\n\nTarget qubit initially |0>. Apply operation: if first qubit is |0>, flip target to |1>. If first qubit is |1>, leave target as |0>. So output: α|0>⊗|1> + (β-γ) |1>⊗|0>. That's α|0>|1> + (β-γ)|1>|0>. Compare to options.\n\nOption A: α|0>⊗|1> + (β|1> - γ|1>)⊗|0> = α|0>|1> + (β-γ)|1>|0>. That matches! Option A.\n\nOption C: α|0>|0> + (β-γ) |1>|1> no.\n\nThus answer A.\n\nCheck other subtlety: maybe they assume standard CNOT where control on |1>. They said condition is first qubit of control has to be in state |0>. So it's control on zero. Good.\n\nThus answer: A.", "response": "ANSWER: A", "answer": "A", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.0371172265877249e-05, "p_correct": 0.9999999999986919, "logp_correct": -1.3080162410958112e-12, "letter_mass": 0.999991774627809, "p_letters": {"A": 1.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.4139107640446913, "cot_lp_min64": -0.6498909298767974, "frac_below_-5": 0.008620689655172414, "digit_lp_min": -0.001032772590406239, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 464, "lp_end": -2.1934269170742482e-05, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -6.318072337307967e-06, "logp_nocot": -9.162438270714707, "p_nocot": 0.00010490679478683644, "uplift": 9.1624382707134, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.000105, "B": 0.850068, "C": 0.14772, "D": 0.002107}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
