{"qid": "recYG3SqTUBlu7jvf", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: Which one of the following is a correct expression for the Scharfetter-Gummel discretized drift-diffusion model equation for current?  In the following expressions $J{n,j+1/2}$ is the electron current at the point in between the mesh points j and j + 1, $\\mu$ is the hole mobility, $dx$ is the mesh size, $Vt$ is the thermal voltage, and $n$ is the electron charge carrier density.\n\nA) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} + B \\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i}\\bigg)$\nB) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} + B \\big (-\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i} \\bigg)$\nC) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} - B \\big (-\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i} \\bigg)$\nD) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} - B \\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i} \\bigg)$\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: Which one of the following is a correct expression for the Scharfetter-Gummel discretized drift-diffusion model equation for current?  In the following expressions $J{n,j+1/2}$ is the electron current at the point in between the mesh points j and j + 1, $\\mu$ is the hole mobility, $dx$ is the mesh size, $Vt$ is the thermal voltage, and $n$ is the electron charge carrier density.\n\nA) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} + B \\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i}\\bigg)$\nB) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} + B \\big (-\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i} \\bigg)$\nC) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} - B \\big (-\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i} \\bigg)$\nD) $J{n,j+1/2} = \\frac{q \\mu{n,i+1}}{dx} \\bigg(B\\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i+1} - B \\big (\\frac{ \\delta \\psi{i+1}}{Vt} \\big) n{i} \\bigg)$\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recYG3SqTUBlu7jvf:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 30890, 2672, 22035, 30747, 13112, 193941, 111140, 2860, 395, 57604, 2469, 4443, 10514, 483, 23629, 2208, 13, 16574, 12973, 25, 643, 2170, 314, 2335, 425, 2637, 2170, 425, 350, 350, 77, 10853, 10, 16, 425, 418, 7, 37764, 10853, 10, 16, 533, 60982, 10853, 11876, 53, 2154, 8, 533, 350, 77, 10853, 425, 418, 174232, 37764, 10853, 10, 16, 533, 60982, 10853, 11876, 53, 2154, 8, 1546, 1546, 425, 631, 2154, 820, 29472, 30, 41021, 30890, 31687, 1625, 13, 623, 2672, 22035, 30747, 13112, 193941, 36547, 395, 100085, 1402, 41, 2170, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 14, 17, 92, 314, 2335, 425, 2637, 2170, 425, 350, 631, 2154, 820, 26143, 87, 1546, 425, 723, 297, 10853, 425, 418, 7, 15927, 10853, 533, 80339, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 9263, 533, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 425, 418, 7, 15927, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 80339, 10853, 8, 32229, 162661, 279, 41, 314, 2335, 425, 2637, 2170, 425, 350, 53, 2154, 14, 16611, 87, 8, 425, 350, 297, 10853, 425, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 533, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 425, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 1546, 1202, 4522, 418, 4061, 8, 314, 1215, 27334, 8067, 4061, 14080, 16, 8, 350, 106044, 283, 48078, 1114, 741, 50557, 19271, 1625, 25, 643, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 14, 17, 92, 314, 350, 80, 425, 2637, 2170, 425, 631, 2154, 820, 26143, 87, 8, 425, 350, 297, 10853, 425, 418, 7, 15927, 10853, 533, 80339, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 9263, 533, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 425, 418, 7, 15927, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 80339, 10853, 8, 11467, 7943, 10069, 1023, 5067, 483, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 1577, 25, 643, 314, 2335, 2637, 2170, 820, 26143, 87, 723, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 297, 10853, 6045, 350, 62832, 2232, 14537, 402, 9262, 741, 41021, 1921, 17098, 43578, 364, 2594, 3880, 679, 12332, 2335, 425, 2637, 22305, 77, 25032, 10, 16, 92, 820, 29472, 887, 3164, 553, 12486, 631, 2154, 12332, 11, 889, 10112, 2637, 6664, 631, 2154, 30, 623, 4928, 5003, 9621, 25, 2637, 382, 22985, 44263, 11, 10112, 1023, 1199, 23629, 44263, 30, 54458, 413, 55881, 13, 3072, 581, 5655, 4122, 402, 2232, 364, 21996, 23629, 2208, 9262, 25, 643, 2170, 314, 2335, 425, 2637, 2170, 425, 297, 425, 457, 659, 2335, 425, 415, 2170, 425, 96340, 6662, 87, 887, 730, 45286, 111140, 2860, 11, 290, 36547, 591, 4596, 575, 316, 575, 10, 16, 382, 1402, 41, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 14, 17, 92, 314, 2335, 425, 2637, 2170, 425, 350, 53, 2154, 820, 26143, 87, 8, 425, 350, 297, 10853, 425, 418, 7, 15927, 10853, 533, 80339, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 9263, 533, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 425, 418, 7, 15927, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 80339, 10853, 8, 99940, 12845, 26143, 15927, 314, 80339, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 80339, 10853, 887, 7801, 80339, 10853, 533, 80339, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 314, 533, 16611, 15927, 13, 2632, 2914, 25, 297, 10853, 425, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 533, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 425, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 741, 69048, 81, 5717, 25, 643, 314, 2335, 2637, 2170, 820, 26143, 87, 723, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 297, 10853, 6045, 4238, 631, 2154, 30, 24305, 2232, 25, 1843, 581, 57388, 2973, 18089, 656, 631, 2154, 25, 50557, 643, 314, 350, 80, 2637, 2170, 631, 2154, 820, 26143, 87, 8, 723, 297, 10853, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 533, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 41590, 2154, 8, 6045, 364, 84787, 290, 12332, 306, 3880, 53426, 631, 2154, 10112, 1023, 19429, 2637, 118583, 656, 631, 2154, 30, 4037, 3239, 364, 12211, 540, 3880, 25, 418, 326, 363, 679, 23821, 17424, 25, 418, 8844, 2932, 2932, 25, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 659, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 10853, 13, 363, 8844, 40335, 25, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 10853, 13, 415, 8844, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 10853, 364, 976, 6145, 12973, 1757, 679, 23821, 17424, 350, 690, 2914, 8841, 11, 1001, 12626, 8, 326, 290, 3099, 2914, 8844, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 741, 2632, 5317, 363, 15248, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 363, 364, 4383, 2232, 6544, 25, 643, 314, 2335, 9, 12173, 6662, 87, 350, 418, 7, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 22305, 72, 10, 16, 92, 533, 418, 8087, 16611, 15927, 8, 297, 10853, 14868, 21926, 9707, 5317, 363, 364, 72816, 6052, 25, 363, 364], "n_tokens": 832, "words": 404, "band_lo": 245.0, "band_hi": 980.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to recall Scharfetter-Gummel discretization for drift-diffusion with electron current. Standard expression: J_n = q * mu_n * ( (n_i+1 * B(psi_i+1 - psi_i)/V_T) - (n_i * B(-(psi_i+1 - psi_i)/V_T) ) ) * V_T / dx? Let's recall precise form. The Scharfetter-Gummel flux for electrons:\n\nJ_n_{i+1/2} = q * mu_n * ( V_T / Δx ) * [ n_i * B(ψ_i - ψ_{i+1}) - n_{i+1} * B(ψ_{i+1} - ψ_i) ]\n\nAlternatively\n\nJ = q * mu_n * (V_T/Δx) * ( n_i * B(Δψ/V_T) - n_{i+1} * B(-Δψ/V_T) ) \n\nwhere B(x) = x/(exp(x)-1) (Bernoulli function). Actually typical form: J_{i+1/2} = (q * mu_n * V_T / Δx) * ( n_i * B(ψ_i - ψ_{i+1}) - n_{i+1} * B(ψ_{i+1} - ψ_i) )\n\nBut sometimes they write with n_{i+1} first: J = q mu_n / Δx [ B(Δψ/V_T) n_{i+1} - B(-Δψ/V_T) n_i ] (maybe sign depending on direction). Let's see candidate expressions.\n\nAll options have factor q * mu_{n,i+1} / dx . They are missing V_T factor, but maybe mu includes V_T? The question says parameters: mu is hole mobility, maybe they use electron mobility? Might be scaling. But we choose based on sign.\n\nStandard electron current direction: J_n = q * mu_n * n * E + q * D_n * dn/dx . In SG discretization, the flux from node i to i+1 is:\n\nJ_{i+1/2} = q * mu_n * (V_T / Δx) * ( n_i * B(ψ_i - ψ_{i+1}) - n_{i+1} * B(ψ_{i+1} - ψ_i) ).\n\nLet Δψ = ψ_{i+1} - ψ_i . Then ψ_i - ψ_{i+1} = -Δψ. So term: n_i * B(-Δψ/V_T) - n_{i+1} * B(Δψ/V_T). Rearranged: J = q mu_n / Δx [ B(Δψ/V_T) n_{i+1} - B(-Δψ/V_T) n_i ] times V_T? Wait sign: If we multiply both sides by V_T: Actually J = (q mu_n V_T / Δx) [ n_i B(-Δψ/V_T) - n_{i+1} B(Δψ/V_T) ].\n\nThus the factor in options lacking V_T maybe they assume mu multiplied by V_T? Not sure.\n\nLook at options: B and C have opposite signs: B uses plus plus: B(Δψ) n_{i+1} + B(-Δψ) n_i. C uses minus: B(Δψ) n_{i+1} - B(-Δψ) n_i. D uses B(Δψ) n_{i+1} - B(Δψ) n_i.\n\nThe correct expression should have opposite signs (one term positive, one negative) and the second term uses B(-Δψ). So option C matches.\n\nThus answer: C.\n\nCheck sign further: J = q*mu/dx ( B(Δψ) n_{i+1} - B(-Δψ) n_i ). That's exactly option C.\n\nTherefore answer: C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.5497197338731894e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999969, "logp_correct": -3.0818680745752143e-15, "letter_mass": 0.9999998807907277, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.457491155120578, "cot_lp_min64": -1.221240537732427, "frac_below_-5": 0.009768009768009768, "digit_lp_min": -0.005933764856308699, "answer_first_mention_lp": 0.0, "n_cot_tokens": 819, "lp_end": -0.011542445048689842, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -1.7014133391843422, "p_nocot": 0.1824255126416246, "uplift": 1.7014133391843391, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.817574, "C": 0.182426, "D": 0.0}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recYOzCsevNz61Lyn", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: You have prepared a di-substituted 6-membered aromatic ring compound containing 8 carbon atoms in total. Peaks in the FTIR spectrum of this compound indicate the presence of a carbonyl group as well as an aromatic-halogen bond. Identify the correct 1H NMR data for this compound.\n\nA) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 9.9 (1H, s), 7.8 (2H, d), 7.6 (2H, d), 3.7 (2H, s)\nB) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 4.8 (2H, d), 4.6 (2H, d), 1.3 (3H, s)\nC) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 7.8 (2H, d), 7.6 (2H, d), 2.3 (3H, s)\nD) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 6.9 (1H, s), 4.8 (2H, d), 4.6 (2H, d), 1.3 (2H, s)\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: You have prepared a di-substituted 6-membered aromatic ring compound containing 8 carbon atoms in total. Peaks in the FTIR spectrum of this compound indicate the presence of a carbonyl group as well as an aromatic-halogen bond. Identify the correct 1H NMR data for this compound.\n\nA) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 9.9 (1H, s), 7.8 (2H, d), 7.6 (2H, d), 3.7 (2H, s)\nB) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 4.8 (2H, d), 4.6 (2H, d), 1.3 (3H, s)\nC) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 7.8 (2H, d), 7.6 (2H, d), 2.3 (3H, s)\nD) 1H NMR: chemical reference (ppm): 6.9 (1H, s), 4.8 (2H, d), 4.6 (2H, d), 1.3 (2H, s)\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recYOzCsevNz61Lyn:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 32043, 290, 4792, 13, 623, 36762, 25, 392, 4091, 37663, 5028, 26369, 220, 21, 94547, 295, 110666, 12796, 36762, 15683, 220, 23, 15883, 63489, 306, 3609, 3692, 2632, 110666, 12796, 350, 44624, 1900, 8, 382, 220, 21, 41933, 1808, 13, 9196, 37663, 5028, 26369, 4748, 1920, 22148, 84, 1094, 13284, 1920, 12063, 12885, 696, 402, 290, 76732, 1900, 13, 17565, 41933, 1808, 314, 220, 23, 11, 813, 290, 22148, 84, 1094, 1147, 350, 23, 12, 21, 25987, 17, 15883, 63489, 13, 125152, 2454, 22148, 11823, 7038, 6664, 15883, 1858, 8, 2238, 484, 3609, 5768, 15883, 63489, 314, 220, 17, 13, 52762, 1151, 1001, 22148, 11823, 382, 15883, 3643, 3566, 350, 34, 28, 46, 8, 1118, 8895, 261, 15883, 350, 3086, 15883, 3643, 15883, 741, 623, 1273, 22148, 11823, 382, 448, 110666, 187143, 10478, 15135, 11, 1299, 261, 4039, 10478, 18618, 8516, 316, 290, 12796, 11, 860, 15883, 5768, 13, 2632, 3609, 41933, 1808, 25, 220, 21, 110666, 659, 220, 16, 15883, 3643, 15883, 314, 22, 11, 2928, 12486, 1001, 15883, 13, 3072, 9710, 25, 392, 10950, 7554, 306, 290, 44053, 4368, 31822, 328, 495, 36762, 21611, 290, 14324, 328, 261, 15883, 3643, 3566, 472, 1775, 472, 448, 110666, 187143, 10478, 15135, 3692, 2632, 581, 679, 15883, 3643, 326, 4039, 10478, 18618, 8516, 316, 110666, 13, 21926, 1606, 1001, 15883, 5018, 13, 3072, 1023, 2891, 3609, 220, 23, 41933, 1808, 13, 2632, 12951, 15883, 3643, 3566, 382, 997, 328, 448, 1375, 3643, 22148, 11823, 1299, 533, 8310, 3583, 18, 350, 86583, 3643, 8, 1118, 19282, 1920, 41933, 1808, 25, 15883, 3643, 15883, 659, 101385, 15883, 13, 4569, 59684, 220, 21, 10, 17, 314, 23, 41933, 1808, 13, 11377, 1320, 37663, 5028, 26369, 110666, 25, 395, 4994, 11, 275, 37137, 292, 3643, 65, 511, 630, 7553, 1900, 350, 19, 2118, 69160, 86583, 178229, 690, 741, 4569, 853, 261, 15883, 3643, 350, 34, 28, 46, 8, 18618, 316, 110666, 350, 86583, 3643, 741, 19696, 10478, 18618, 316, 110666, 350, 9995, 2866, 741, 2632, 3609, 363, 28, 23, 350, 34, 21, 12796, 659, 15883, 3643, 15883, 659, 101385, 15883, 741, 9700, 364, 84787, 290, 36762, 6960, 382, 448, 110666, 16262, 690, 350, 86583, 178229, 690, 66383, 8, 483, 261, 4039, 10478, 24742, 1555, 14, 16151, 168500, 5178, 13, 2632, 4877, 25, 110666, 440, 45023, 25, 290, 12796, 853, 1920, 22148, 84, 1094, 11, 15021, 4242, 110666, 12063, 12885, 696, 13, 2214, 261, 1209, 22572, 431, 5028, 26369, 76732, 1900, 350, 68, 1940, 4213, 1209, 12, 68232, 3643, 112546, 630, 7553, 1900, 936, 290, 110666, 440, 45023, 553, 44568, 6, 12708, 6, 8302, 9874, 1920, 3503, 1561, 2454, 74479, 395, 220, 17, 39, 13, 623, 15883, 3643, 101385, 14518, 472, 261, 6211, 1347, 6574, 17, 13, 20, 108313, 395, 68232, 178229, 690, 350, 76, 53546, 18618, 316, 15883, 3643, 8, 13729, 2846, 220, 17, 13, 20, 108313, 350, 3356, 220, 17, 13, 20, 741, 623, 110666, 440, 45023, 540, 6574, 22, 13, 20, 12, 23, 13, 15, 108313, 13, 3274, 382, 1217, 100539, 133496, 889, 625, 2105, 26, 15883, 3643, 472, 16262, 690, 364, 84787, 581, 2665, 478, 27029, 483, 220, 17, 110666, 3503, 1561, 220, 17, 39, 2454, 65176, 22, 13, 23, 326, 220, 22, 13, 21, 936, 326, 261, 101385, 6211, 1347, 540, 6574, 17, 13, 18, 350, 18, 39, 11, 265, 741, 17796, 363, 7398, 25, 220, 22, 13, 23, 350, 17, 39, 11, 272, 936, 220, 22, 13, 21, 350, 17, 39, 11, 272, 936, 220, 17, 13, 18, 350, 18, 39, 11, 265, 741, 21926, 4387, 364, 4383, 1273, 3880, 25, 355, 6664, 261, 220, 24, 13, 24, 108313, 6211, 1347, 314, 100539, 133496, 120589, 13, 4037, 1039, 1890, 13, 418, 71357, 110666, 29026, 13, 415, 6664, 110666, 220, 21, 13, 24, 350, 16, 39, 8, 2932, 1273, 29026, 85596, 13, 2632, 6052, 363, 364, 84787, 6052, 13], "n_tokens": 654, "words": 350, "band_lo": 209.0, "band_hi": 836.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to decode the problem. The compound: \"di-substituted 6-membered aromatic ring compound containing 8 carbon atoms in total.\" So aromatic ring (benzene) is 6 carbons. Di-substituted means two substituents replace two hydrogens on the benzene. Total carbons = 8, so the substituents add (8-6)=2 carbon atoms. Means each substituent probably includes carbon(s) such that total added carbon atoms = 2. Likely one substituent is carbonyl group (C=O) which contains a carbon (the carbonyl carbon). The other substituent is an aromatic-halogen bond, like a halogen attached directly to the ring, no carbon added. So total carbons: 6 aromatic + 1 carbonyl carbon =7, still missing one carbon. But statement: \"Peaks in the FTIR spectrum of this compound indicate the presence of a carbonyl group as well as an aromatic-halogen bond.\" So we have carbonyl and halogen attached directly to aromatic. That's only one carbon extra. But they say total 8 carbons. So perhaps carbonyl group is part of an acyl substituent like -COCH3 (acetyl) which adds two carbons: carbonyl carbon + methyl carbon. That yields 6+2 =8 carbons. Yes di-substituted aromatic: for example, p-acetylbromobenzene (4-bromoacetophenone). That has a carbonyl (C=O) attached to aromatic (acetyl). Halogen attached to aromatic (like Br). So total C=8 (C6 ring + carbonyl carbon + methyl carbon). Good.\n\nThus the compound likely is an aromatic ketone (acetophenone derivative) with a halogen ortho/para/meta etc. So features: aromatic protons: the ring has two substituents, leaving four aromatic hydrogens. For a para-disubstituted benzene (e.g., para- acetyl bromobenzene), the aromatic protons are AA'BB' pattern giving two doublets each integrating for 2H. The carbonyl methyl appears as a singlet ~2.5 ppm for acetophenone (methyl attached to carbonyl) typically around 2.5 ppm (δ 2.5). The aromatic protons at ~7.5-8.0 ppm. There is also aldehyde but not here; carbonyl as ketone.\n\nThus we expect NMR with 2 aromatic doublets 2H each (~7.8 and 7.6), and a methyl singlet at ~2.3 (3H, s). Option C shows: 7.8 (2H, d), 7.6 (2H, d), 2.3 (3H, s). That's perfect.\n\nCheck other options: A includes a 9.9 ppm singlet = aldehyde proton. Not our case. B lacks aromatic signals. D includes aromatic 6.9 (1H) plus other signals inconsistent. So answer C.\n\nThus answer.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.9073468138230965e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999987, "logp_correct": -1.3277262175773603e-15, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000013, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.6228527004722887, "cot_lp_min64": -0.9165873266281235, "frac_below_-5": 0.0124804992199688, "digit_lp_min": -2.033090829849243, "answer_first_mention_lp": -7.152555099310121e-07, "n_cot_tokens": 641, "lp_end": -2.264974000354414e-06, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -3.2880427328816952, "p_nocot": 0.03732683653503223, "uplift": 3.288042732881694, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.962672, "B": 1e-06, "C": 0.037327, "D": 0.0}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "recZ7P8XqZ8HMU5OF", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: The state $\\psi$ of a system is given in terms of a complete and orthonormal set of basis vectors $|\\phi_1>,  |\\phi_2>,  |\\phi_3>$ and $| \\phi_4 >$ as $|\\psi> = \\sqrt{1/15} |\\phi_1> + \\sqrt{2/15} |\\phi_2> + 2/ \\sqrt{15} |\\phi_3> + 4/ \\sqrt{15} |\\phi_4>$. The basis vectors $|\\phi_n>$ are eigenstates of the Hamiltonian operator $H$ satisfying $H |\\phi_n> = n E_o |\\phi_n>; n=1, 2, 3, 4. Calculate the average energy of the system in some repeated measurements.\n\nA) E_o\nB) 81/15 E_o\nC) 81/23 E_o\nD) 1/23 E_o\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: The state $\\psi$ of a system is given in terms of a complete and orthonormal set of basis vectors $|\\phi_1>,  |\\phi_2>,  |\\phi_3>$ and $| \\phi_4 >$ as $|\\psi> = \\sqrt{1/15} |\\phi_1> + \\sqrt{2/15} |\\phi_2> + 2/ \\sqrt{15} |\\phi_3> + 4/ \\sqrt{15} |\\phi_4>$. The basis vectors $|\\phi_n>$ are eigenstates of the Hamiltonian operator $H$ satisfying $H |\\phi_n> = n E_o |\\phi_n>; n=1, 2, 3, 4. Calculate the average energy of the system in some repeated measurements.\n\nA) E_o\nB) 81/15 E_o\nC) 81/23 E_o\nD) 1/23 E_o\n", "true_answer": "C", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recZ7P8XqZ8HMU5OF:1", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 23864, 55387, 1432, 328, 487, 25, 2969, 253, 101, 15927, 91, 39, 91, 15927, 158, 253, 102, 314, 4215, 2170, 1022, 66, 2170, 91, 61, 17, 425, 297, 457, 15, 364, 61630, 177449, 25, 274, 16, 314, 44237, 7, 16, 14, 1055, 741, 274, 17, 314, 44237, 7, 17, 14, 1055, 741, 274, 18, 314, 220, 17, 14, 44237, 7, 1055, 741, 274, 19, 314, 220, 19, 820, 44237, 7, 1055, 741, 6208, 115461, 25, 4215, 1022, 66, 91, 61, 17, 1757, 413, 220, 16, 13, 1022, 66, 16, 91, 61, 17, 314, 220, 16, 