{"qid": "recZZpGHxfDeYd0XV", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: A meta-substituted benzoic acid reacts with a mild base (the base gives a brown precipitate with Nessler's reagent) to form a salt, which, on heating, produces compound B. Compound B, when combined with compound C and a base, gives rise to compound D. Compound C is one of the two elements in the periodic table that is a liquid at room temperature. Arrange the following acids in order of decreasing reactivity for the conversion of compound B to compound D: (1). 3-hydroxybenzoic acid (2). 3-methylbenzoic acid (3). 3-nitrobenzoic acid (4). 3-formylbenzoic acid\n\nA) 1>2>4>3\nB) 2>1>4>3\nC) 2>4>1>3\nD) 2>1>3>4\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: A meta-substituted benzoic acid reacts with a mild base (the base gives a brown precipitate with Nessler's reagent) to form a salt, which, on heating, produces compound B. Compound B, when combined with compound C and a base, gives rise to compound D. Compound C is one of the two elements in the periodic table that is a liquid at room temperature. Arrange the following acids in order of decreasing reactivity for the conversion of compound B to compound D: (1). 3-hydroxybenzoic acid (2). 3-methylbenzoic acid (3). 3-nitrobenzoic acid (4). 3-formylbenzoic acid\n\nA) 1>2>4>3\nB) 2>1>4>3\nC) 2>4>1>3\nD) 2>1>3>4\n", "true_answer": "B", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "recZZpGHxfDeYd0XV:2", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 8420, 290, 4792, 13, 3274, 382, 14732, 37663, 5028, 26369, 2974, 4151, 291, 18655, 137530, 483, 261, 31137, 3611, 350, 3086, 3611, 8967, 261, 19705, 47946, 12896, 483, 133904, 1639, 885, 191833, 8, 316, 1625, 261, 16345, 1118, 402, 25419, 28135, 36762, 418, 13, 2632, 1412, 3611, 382, 484, 30, 133904, 