, 2220, 11, 220, 15, 13, 2636, 326, 41051, 14, 22, 13, 17796, 415, 15248, 100033, 350, 15, 13, 2220, 11, 220, 15, 13, 2636, 741, 3072, 1309, 7848, 1432, 328, 11019, 364, 56734, 55387, 1432, 2969, 253, 101, 32, 158, 253, 102, 314, 2969, 253, 101, 727, 91, 355, 1022, 727, 158, 253, 102, 887, 12265, 355, 314, 350, 5762, 14, 17, 8, 3669, 7054, 13, 623, 55387, 328, 3669, 7054, 314, 220, 17, 907, 7, 869, 9, 4653, 64656, 1546, 30, 41021, 23864, 8516, 2360, 12248, 364, 1881, 9727, 306, 869, 170878, 9571, 25, 1022, 727, 29, 314, 350, 16, 14, 103946, 22, 13637, 350, 16, 49691, 936, 350, 17, 18499, 8, 6045, 61, 51, 364, 56734, 55387, 25, 2969, 253, 101, 727, 91, 355, 1022, 727, 158, 253, 102, 314, 350, 5762, 14, 17, 8, 2969, 253, 101, 727, 91, 3669, 7054, 91, 727, 158, 253, 102, 887, 3669, 7054, 24615, 472, 132194, 10674, 25, 3669, 7054, 723, 64, 17568, 144683, 51, 314, 723, 65, 11, 261, 144683, 51, 364, 84787, 2969, 253, 101, 727, 91, 1168, 7054, 91, 727, 158, 253, 102, 314, 350, 16, 14, 22, 13637, 350, 16, 533, 575, 8, 1366, 350, 17, 659, 575, 8, 6045, 425, 723, 350, 17, 533, 575, 936, 350, 16, 659, 575, 8, 6045, 350, 21910, 89227, 379, 328, 9727, 10674, 741, 45438, 16579, 1888, 25, 350, 16, 533, 575, 44406, 17, 533, 575, 8, 659, 350, 17, 659, 575, 44406, 16, 659, 575, 3991, 58369, 23864, 2454, 2914, 364, 7127, 2914, 25, 350, 16, 533, 575, 44406, 17, 533, 575, 8, 314, 220, 16, 9, 17, 659, 220, 16, 78771, 72, 8, 533, 575, 9, 17, 659, 21382, 72, 4898, 12, 72, 8, 314, 220, 17, 533, 575, 533, 220, 17, 72, 659, 575, 61, 17, 314, 220, 17, 533, 18, 72, 533, 16, 314, 220, 16, 533, 18, 72, 364, 17422, 2914, 25, 350, 17, 659, 575, 44406, 16, 659, 575, 8, 314, 220, 17, 9, 16, 659, 220, 17, 51147, 659, 575, 9, 16, 659, 575, 51147, 314, 220, 17, 659, 17, 72, 659, 575, 659, 575, 61, 17, 314, 220, 17, 659, 18, 72, 533, 16, 314, 220, 16, 659, 18, 72, 364, 17434, 25, 350, 16, 533, 18, 72, 8, 659, 350, 16, 659, 18, 72, 8, 314, 220, 17, 659, 220, 15, 72, 314, 220, 17, 364, 84787, 2969, 253, 101, 727, 91, 1168, 7054, 91, 727, 158, 253, 102, 314, 350, 16, 14, 22, 8, 425, 220, 17, 314, 220, 17, 14, 22, 364, 72816, 2969, 253, 101, 32, 158, 253, 102, 314, 350, 5762, 14, 17, 8, 425, 220, 17, 14, 22, 314, 41051, 820, 22, 364, 7924, 15248, 5317, 415, 885, 7848, 1432, 41051, 14, 22, 13, 19233, 6052, 382, 415, 364, 84787, 581, 9570, 364], "n_tokens": 1313, "words": 336, "band_lo": 144.75, "band_hi": 579.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to parse the problem. We have a state |\\alpha> proportional to (1+i) |up> + (2-i) |down>. Need to normalize? \"proportional\" means we must normalize to compute probabilities. So state: |α> = N [ (1+i) |↑> + (2-i) |↓> ]. Normalize: N = 1/ sqrt( |1+i|^2 + |2-i|^2 ). Compute magnitudes: |1+i|^2 = (1)^2 + (1)^2 = 2. |2 - i|^2 = (2)^2 + (-1)^2 = 4 +1 =5. Sum = 7. So N = 1/ sqrt(7). So normalized state: |α> = (1/√7)[ (1+i) |↑> + (2-i) |↓> ].\n\nNow we need to consider operator with matrix representation A_ij = ħ/2 if i ≠ j, and 0 if i=j. In the basis {|↑>, |↓>} presumably. So matrix:\n\nA = ( 0      ħ/2\n      ħ/2    0 ).\n\nThus this operator is (ħ/2) σ_x, i.e., spin-x operator. Indeed σ_x = [[0,1],[1,0]]. So A = (ħ/2) σ_x.\n\nWe need probabilities of measuring particle in each eigenstate of this operator. That is, measurement of spin along x direction. The eigenstates of σ_x are |+x> = (|↑> + |↓>)/√2, eigenvalue +1; and |-x> = (|↑> - |↓>)/√2, eigenvalue -1. For A, eigenvalues are ± ħ/2.\n\nWe need probability of obtaining eigenstate + and -. So compute projection probabilities.\n\nWe have |α> in up/down basis. Compute coefficients in +x, -x basis.\n\nLet |+x> = (|↑> + |↓>)/√2, |-x> = (|↑> - |↓>)/√2.\n\nCompute inner product: c_+ = ⟨+x|α⟩. Since |α> = (1/√7)[(1+i)|↑> + (2-i)|↓>].\n\n⟨+x| = (1/√2)(⟨↑| + ⟨↓|). So c_+ = (1/√2)(1/√7)[ (1+i)⟨↑|↑> + (2-i)⟨↓|↓> ] = (1/√14)[ (1+i) + (2-i) ] = (1/√14)[ (1+2) + (i - i) ] = (1/√14)[3 + 0] = 3/√14.\n\nThus probability P_+ = |c_+|^2 = (9) / 14 = 9/14 ≈ 0.642857.\n\nSimilarly c_- = ⟨-x|α⟩ = (1/√2)(1/√7)[ (1+i) - (2-i) ] = (1/√14)[ (1+i) - (2-i) ] = (1/√14)[ (1-2) + (i + i) ] = (1/√14)[ -1 + 2i ].\n\nCompute magnitude squared: | -1 + 2i |^2 = (-1)^2 + (2)^2 = 1 +4 =5. So probability P_- = 5/14 ≈0.35714.\n\nCheck sum = 14/14 =1.\n\nThus probabilities are approximately 0.643 and 0.357.\n\nFrom options, we have probabilities: Option D gives 0.64, 0.36 maybe. Option D: 0.64, 0.36 and ħ/7. Option D matches probabilities (0.64, 0.36). But need average value of operator.\n\nCompute expectation value ⟨A⟩ = ⟨α| A |α⟩ . Since A = (ħ/2) σ_x. The expectation of σ_x = 2 Re( up*down coefficient )? Let's compute directly using matrix.\n\nState vector in up/down basis: |α> = (1/√7)[ (1+i), (2-i) ]^T.\n\nCompute expectation: ⟨α| A |α⟩ = (ħ/2) ⟨α| σ_x|α⟩ . σ_x acts as swapping components: σ_x [a,b]^T = [b, a]^T.\n\nThus ⟨α|σ_x|α⟩ = (1/7)[ (1 - i) , (2 + i) ] * [ (2 - i), (1 + i) ] (since conjugate of vector components). Compute dot product: (1 - i)*(2 - i) + (2 + i)*(1 + i).\n\nLet's compute each term.\n\nFirst term: (1 - i)*(2 - i) = 1*2 + 1*(-i) - i*2 + (-i)(-i) = 2 - i - 2i + i^2 = 2 -3i -1 = 1 -3i.\n\nSecond term: (2 + i)*(1 + i) = 2*1 + 2*i + i*1 + i*i = 2 +2i + i + i^2 = 2 +3i -1 = 1 +3i.\n\nSum: (1 -3i) + (1 +3i) = 2 + 0i = 2.\n\nThus ⟨α|σ_x|α⟩ = (1/7) * 2 = 2/7.\n\nTherefore ⟨A⟩ = (ħ/2) * 2/7 = ħ /7.\n\nThat matches option D's average value ħ/7. Therefore answer is D.\n\nThus we respond.", "response": "ANSWER: D", "answer": "D", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -3.5762737979894155e-06, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999567, "logp_correct": -4.334018881051117e-14, "letter_mass": 0.9999995231631125, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 1.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.26860626578640007, "cot_lp_min64": -0.753622819857009, "frac_below_-5": 0.004615384615384616, "digit_lp_min": -4.018189430236816, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.0017064546700567007, "n_cot_tokens": 1300, "lp_end": -0.0024915861431509256, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -9.271364217771744, "p_nocot": 9.408008053648591e-05, "uplift": 9.271364217771701, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.978862, "B": 0.003116, "C": 0.017928, "D": 9.4e-05}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
{"qid": "rechtUKxC6G67H7Pr", "source": "gpqa", "type": "plain", "value": null, "frame": "-", "term": null, "placement": "user", "position": null, "system": null, "user": "Question: You have prepared an unknown compound. To identify the product, you have used the following characterisation techniques: FTIR, 1H NMR, and Mass Spectrometry. The FTIR spectrum shows a very broad absorption peak at 3000 wavenumbers. Two other strong absorption peaks are observed at 1700 and 1650 wavenumbers. Several peaks were observed in the 1H NMR spectrum including peaks corresponding to vinyl-hydrogens. The mass spectrum shows a fragment peak at m/z = 45. Identify the chemical formula of this unknown compound as either C6H12O, C6H10O, C6H10O2, or C6H12O2.\n\nA) C6H10O2\nB) C6H10O\nC) C6H12O\nD) C6H12O2\n\n\nYour response should be of the following format: 'ANSWER: X' (without quotes) where X is your chosen letter", "instruction": null, "requirement": null, "qblock": "Question: You have prepared an unknown compound. To identify the product, you have used the following characterisation techniques: FTIR, 1H NMR, and Mass Spectrometry. The FTIR spectrum shows a very broad absorption peak at 3000 wavenumbers. Two other strong absorption peaks are observed at 1700 and 1650 wavenumbers. Several peaks were observed in the 1H NMR spectrum including peaks corresponding to vinyl-hydrogens. The mass spectrum shows a fragment peak at m/z = 45. Identify the chemical formula of this unknown compound as either C6H12O, C6H10O, C6H10O2, or C6H12O2.\n\nA) C6H10O2\nB) C6H10O\nC) C6H12O\nD) C6H12O2\n", "true_answer": "A", "origin": "base", "source_ref": "rechtUKxC6G67H7Pr:3", "cot_tokens": [2167, 1309, 316, 18135, 93131, 1238, 364, 7114, 4368, 25, 1869, 11245, 57036, 540, 220, 4095, 15, 9256, 85848, 16, 24832, 532, 13091, 21638, 350, 65, 12086, 8, 6960, 16589, 503, 1669, 3952, 88, 459, 18655, 13, 23494, 25689, 540, 220, 4095, 15, 350, 62832, 220, 15415, 15, 12, 11727, 15, 741, 13311, 1273, 5532, 57036, 503