20, 16, 13, 1055, 314, 220, 15, 13, 45358, 44956, 20898, 24, 364, 2728, 314, 220, 16, 14, 103946, 15, 13, 3384, 314, 220, 16, 13, 19145, 9534, 41135, 364, 2728, 415, 314, 220, 16, 13, 19145, 9534, 41135, 9, 16, 13, 1055, 314, 220, 16, 13, 30553, 29818, 8947, 364, 84, 9410, 314, 15, 13, 16, 14, 16, 13, 30553, 29818, 8947, 314, 15, 13, 37828, 30854, 364, 84, 18252, 28, 15, 13, 18, 14, 16, 13, 30553, 29818, 8947, 314, 15, 13, 18566, 31465, 364, 128296, 25, 337, 7054, 61, 17, 28, 15, 13, 40681, 10545, 13, 337, 9410, 61, 17, 28, 15, 13, 14689, 3618, 13, 337, 18252, 61, 17, 28, 15, 13, 39500, 504, 13, 34138, 28, 15, 13, 29448, 21, 13, 44237, 28, 15, 13, 46356, 18, 13, 9700, 364, 84787, 6052, 415, 13], "n_tokens": 714, "words": 204, "band_lo": 104.5, "band_hi": 418.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need to transform velocities from spaceship frame S' to Earth frame S. Ship moves at 0.5c along +x relative to Earth. In ship frame, bullet velocity components: u'_x = 0.3c, u'_y = 0.1c, u'_z = 0.3c. Need u vector in Earth frame using relativistic velocity addition formulas for components perpendicular and parallel.\n\nLet beta = v/c = 0.5. gamma = 1/sqrt(1-beta^2) = 1/sqrt(1-0.25)=1/sqrt(0.75)=1/0.8660254 ≈1.1547.\n\nWe have u'_parallel = u'_x along direction of motion; u'_perp components y,z.\n\nFormulas: u_x = (u'_x + v) / (1 + u'_x v / c^2). For perpendicular components: u_y = u'_y / (γ (1 + u'_x v / c^2)). Similarly u_z.\n\nLet v = 0.5c. Compute denominator common: D = 1 + (u'_x v)/c^2 = 1 + (0.3c * 0.5c)/c^2 = 1 + 0.15 = 1.15.\n\nSo u_x = (0.3c + 0.5c)/1.15 = 0.8c /1.15 ≈ 0.695652c.\n\nNow gamma = 1.1547. So factor: γ (1 + u'_x v /c^2) = γ * D = 1.1547 * 1.15 = 1.3289 approx.\n\nThus u_y = u'_y / (γ D) = 0.1c / 1.3289 = 0.0752c.\n\nSimilarly u_z = 0.3c / 1.3289 = 0.2257c.\n\nNow magnitude: sqrt(u_x^2 + u_y^2 + u_z^2). Compute squares: u_x^2 = (0.69565)^2 = 0.4839. u_y^2 = (0.0752)^2 = 0.00565. u_z^2 = (0.2257)^2 = 0.05096. Sum = 0.5405. sqrt = 0.735. So magnitude ≈0.735c.\n\nOptions: D ~0.73c. So answer D.\n\nCheck rounding: compute more accurate: Let's do precise.\n\nD =1.15 exactly.\n\nu_x = 0.8 /1.15 = 0.6956521739.\n\nγ = 1/√0.75 = 1.154700538.\n\nγ D = 1.154700538*1.15 = 1.32840562.\n\nu_y =0.1/1.32840562 =0.075267.\n\nu_z=0.3/1.32840562 =0.225801.\n\nSquares: u_x^2=0.48394. u_y^2=0.00566. u_z^2=0.05100. Sum=0.5406. sqrt=0.7353. Good.\n\nThus answer D.", "response": "ANSWER: D", "answer": "D", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.4185804502631072e-05, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999981, "logp_correct": -1.9017630126089948e-15, "letter_mass": 1.000000000000002, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 0.0, "D": 1.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.24397973616756302, "cot_lp_min64": -0.5446797889836708, "frac_below_-5": 0.0042796005706134095, "digit_lp_min": -8.151880264282227, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.0006909366929903626, "n_cot_tokens": 701, "lp_end": -3.099436753473128e-06, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": 0.0, "logp_nocot": -14.252086415985568, "p_nocot": 6.462454731239196e-07, "uplift": 14.252086415985566, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.119184, "B": 0.880657, "C": 0.000158, "D": 1e-06}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
