 61, 17, 425, 723, 87, 61, 18, 14, 18, 167793, 15, 61, 65, 314, 220, 23, 41051, 61, 17, 425, 350, 65, 61, 18, 14, 18, 8, 314, 350, 23, 14, 18, 8, 41051, 61, 17, 287, 61, 18, 364, 19371, 55387, 1432, 464, 79, 61, 17, 29, 314, 357, 820, 478, 314, 350, 350, 23, 14, 18, 8, 41051, 61, 17, 287, 61, 18, 1546, 820, 350, 350, 1125, 14, 1055, 8, 287, 61, 20, 1546, 314, 350, 23, 14, 18, 8, 41051, 61, 17, 287, 61, 18, 425, 350, 1055, 14, 1125, 8, 425, 350, 16, 7611, 61, 20, 8, 314, 350, 23, 9, 1055, 60504, 18, 9, 1125, 8, 41051, 61, 17, 425, 350, 16, 7611, 61, 17, 8, 314, 350, 6106, 60504, 3519, 8, 41051, 61, 17, 820, 287, 61, 17, 314, 350, 6106, 14, 3519, 8, 314, 66240, 25, 38484, 220, 1494, 25, 220, 6106, 14, 3519, 314, 220, 20, 14, 17, 30, 220, 1494, 9, 20, 314, 6106, 11, 220, 1494, 9, 17, 28, 3519, 11, 14531, 220, 20, 14, 17, 13, 2632, 1534, 314, 350, 20, 14, 17, 8, 41051, 61, 17, 820, 287, 61, 17, 364, 84787, 6052, 363, 25, 220, 20, 14, 17, 350, 10104, 237, 7611, 73602, 17, 279, 4383, 3880, 25, 363, 15248, 364, 84787, 6052, 25, 363, 364], "n_tokens": 783, "words": 194, "band_lo": 107.0, "band_hi": 428.0, "fmt_ok": true, "correct": true, "reasoning": "We need expectation value of p^2 = -ħ^2 ∫ ψ* d^2ψ/dx^2 dx (assuming real wavefunction). For normalized wavefunction. Since not normalized, we compute expectation value = (∫ ψ (-ħ^2 d^2ψ/dx^2) dx) / (∫ ψ^2 dx). Compute.\n\nGiven ψ(x)= (b^2 - x^2) for -b<x<b, else 0. It's real. Let's compute.\n\nFirst, compute denominator N = ∫_{-b}^{b} (b^2 - x^2)^2 dx.\n\nCompute integral: ∫ (b^4 - 2b^2 x^2 + x^4) dx from -b to b. Even function, so 2 ∫_0^b (b^4 - 2b^2 x^2 + x^4) dx.\n\nCompute indefinite: b^4 x - (2b^2) x^3/3 + x^5/5.\n\nEvaluate 0 to b: b^4 * b - (2b^2) b^3/3 + b^5/5 = b^5 - (2b^5)/3 + b^5/5 = b^5 [1 - 2/3 + 1/5] = b^5 [ (common denominator 15): (15 -10 +3)/15 = (8)/15 ] = (8/15) b^5.\n\nMultiply by 2 => N = (16/15) b^5.\n\nNow numerator: I = ∫ ψ (-ħ^2 d^2ψ/dx^2) dx = -ħ^2 ∫ ψ d^2ψ/dx^2 dx from -b to b.\n\nIntegration by parts could simplify: For real ψ, we have ∫ ψ (-ħ^2 ψ'') dx = ħ^2 ∫ (ψ')^2 dx (assuming wavefunction vanishes at boundaries). Since ψ=0 at x=±b? At x=±b, ψ = b^2 - b^2 =0, yes. So boundary terms vanish. Therefore I = ħ^2 ∫ (ψ')^2 dx.\n\nCompute ψ' = d/dx (b^2 - x^2) = -2x.\n\nThus (ψ')^2 = 4x^2.\n\nThus I = ħ^2 ∫_{-b}^{b} 4 x^2 dx = 4 ħ^2 * 2 ∫_0^b x^2 dx = 8 ħ^2 * [x^3/3]_0^b = 8 ħ^2 * (b^3/3) = (8/3) ħ^2 b^3.\n\nThen expectation value <p^2> = I / N = ( (8/3) ħ^2 b^3 ) / ( (16/15) b^5 ) = (8/3) ħ^2 b^3 * (15/16) * (1/b^5) = (8*15)/(3*16) ħ^2 * (1/b^2) = (120)/(48) ħ^2 / b^2 = (120/48) = simplify: divide 24: 120/48 = 5/2? 24*5 =120, 24*2=48, yes 5/2. So result = (5/2) ħ^2 / b^2.\n\nThus answer C: 5/2 (ℏ/b)^2\n\nCheck options: C matches.\n\nThus answer: C.", "response": "ANSWER: C", "answer": "C", "strict": null, "judged": false, "reject_reasons": [], "force": {"logp_answer": -1.4424220353248529e-05, "p_correct": 0.9999999999999963, "logp_correct": -3.66673774163527e-15, "letter_mass": 1.0000000000000036, "p_letters": {"A": 0.0, "B": 0.0, "C": 1.0, "D": 0.0}, "tgt_gap": 0.0, "cot_lp_mean": -0.18186529194164122, "cot_lp_min64": -0.3653274769722583, "frac_below_-5": 0.0025974025974025974, "digit_lp_min": -0.38687101006507874, "answer_first_mention_lp": -0.37091585993766785, "n_cot_tokens": 770, "lp_end": -0.00431784288957715, "lp_final": 0.0, "lp_prefix": -1.1920928244535389e-07, "logp_nocot": -8.752692289335586, "p_nocot": 0.00015803527516226147, "uplift": 8.752692289335583, "p_letters_nocot": {"A": 0.997312, "B": 0.002472, "C": 0.000158, "D": 5.8e-05}}, "force_keep": true, "accepted": true}
